const PREGEN_HI = {"q1": {"q": "Data se pata chalta hai ki 12% cases me agent `get_customer` ko skip kar deta hai aur seedha `lookup_order` call kar deta hai, sirf customer ka naam use karke — jisse galat refund ho jaate hain. **Sabse effective change kaunsa hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek programmatic precondition add karo jo `lookup_order` aur `process_refund` ko block kare jab tak `get_customer` se ek ID na mil jaaye", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "System prompt ko improve karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Few-shot examples add karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Ek routing classifier implement karo", "c": false}], "e": "Jab critical business logic ko ek specific tool sequence chahiye hoti hai, toh software **deterministic guarantee** deta hai — jo prompt-based approaches (B, C) nahi de sakte. D availability ka issue solve karta hai, tool ordering ka nahi."}, "q2": {"q": "Agent order-related questions ke liye `lookup_order` ki jagah baar-baar `get_customer` call kar leta hai. Tool descriptions minimal aur similar hain. **Pehla step kya hona chahiye?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Few-shot examples", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Har tool ki description ko expand karo — input formats, examples, aur boundaries ke saath", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek routing layer add karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Dono tools ko merge kar do", "c": false}], "e": "Tool descriptions hi model ka primary selection mechanism hain. Ye lowest-effort, highest-impact fix hai. A tokens add karta hai bina root cause fix kiye. C overengineering hai. D zaroorat se zyada effort maangta hai."}, "q3": {"q": "Agent sirf 55% issues resolve kar paata hai jabki target 80% hai. Ye simple cases ko escalate kar deta hai aur complex policy exceptions khud handle karne ki koshish karta hai. **Calibration kaise improve karein?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Explicit escalation criteria add karo, few-shot examples ke saath", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Self-rated confidence (1–10) with automatic escalation", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Historical data pe train ki gayi ek separate classifier", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Sentiment analysis", "c": false}], "e": "Ye directly root cause ko address karta hai — unclear decision boundaries. B unreliable hai (model confidently galat bhi ho sakta hai). C overengineering hai. D ek alag hi problem solve karta hai (mood != complexity)."}, "q58": {"q": "Testing ke dauran tumne dekha ki agent aksar `get_customer` call kar leta hai jab users order status ke baare me poochte hain, jabki `lookup_order` zyada appropriate hota. Is problem ko address karne ke liye pehle kya check karna chahiye? **Pehle kya check karein?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek preprocessing classifier implement karo jo order-related requests detect karke seedha `lookup_order` pe route kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Agent ko diye gaye tools ki sankhya kam karo taaki choice simple ho", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "System prompt me har possible order request pattern cover karne wale few-shot examples add karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Tool descriptions check karo ki woh har tool ka purpose clearly differentiate karti hain ya nahi", "c": true}], "e": "Tool descriptions hi wo primary input hain jinke basis pe model decide karta hai kaunsa tool call karna hai. Jab agent baar-baar galat tool choose kare, sabse pehla diagnostic step ye check karna hai ki descriptions har tool ka purpose aur usage boundary clearly alag karti hain ya nahi."}, "q59": {"q": "Tumhara agent single-issue requests 94% accuracy se handle karta hai (jaise \"order #1234 ka refund chahiye\"). Lekin jab customer ek hi message me multiple issues bhejte hain (jaise \"order #1234 ka refund chahiye aur order #5678 ka shipping address bhi update karna hai\"), tool selection accuracy girke 58% ho jaati hai. Agent usually sirf ek issue solve karta hai ya parameters mix kar deta hai. Multi-issue requests ke liye reliability kaise improve karein? **Sabse effective approach kaunsa hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek preprocessing layer banao jo separate model call se multi-issue messages ko alag requests me tod de, har ek ko independently handle kare, aur results merge kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Related tools ko kam universal tools me combine kar do", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Prompt me few-shot examples add karo jo multi-issue requests ke liye correct reasoning aur tool sequencing dikhaye", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Ek response validation implement karo jo incomplete answers detect karke agent ko automatically dobara prompt kare", "c": false}], "e": "Few-shot examples jo multi-issue requests ke liye correct reasoning aur tool sequencing dikhate hain, sabse effective hain kyunki agent single issues pe pehle se hi acha kaam kar raha hai — usse sirf multiple issues decompose karne aur route karne ka pattern sikhaana hai, saath me parameters ko alag rakhna."}, "q60": {"q": "Production logs dikhate hain ki simple requests jaise \"order #1234 ka refund\" ke liye agent 3-4 tool calls me hi 91% success rate ke saath issue resolve kar leta hai. Lekin complex requests jaise \"mujhe do baar bill hua, mera discount apply nahi hua, aur mai cancel karna chahta hoon\" ke liye agent average 12+ tool calls leta hai aur success rate sirf 54% hi hai — aksar issues ko sequentially investigate karta hai aur har issue ke liye redundant customer data fetch karta hai. Complex requests handle karne ke liye sabse effective change kya hoga? **Sabse effective change kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Stages ke beech explicit verification checkpoints add karo, jisme agent har issue resolve karne ke baad progress record kare, agle pe jaane se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "`get_customer`, `lookup_order`, aur billing-related tools ko ek single `investigate_issue` tool me combine kar do taaki tools kam ho jaayein", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Request ko separate issues me decompose karo, phir shared customer context use karke sabko parallel me investigate karo, aur ek final resolution me synthesize kar do", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "System prompt me few-shot examples add karo jo various multi-faceted billing scenarios ke liye ideal tool-call sequences dikhaye", "c": false}], "e": "Separate issues me decompose karke aur shared customer context ke saath parallel me investigate karke, dono key problems fix ho jaate hain: redundant data retrieval khatam ho jaati hai kyunki shared context reuse hota hai issues ke beech, aur total tool-call loops kam ho jaate hain kyunki investigation parallel hoti hai final resolution synthesize karne se pehle."}, "q61": {"q": "Tumhara agent 55% first-contact resolution achieve kar raha hai, jabki target 80% hai. Logs dikhate hain ki ye simple cases (photo proof ke saath standard replacement damaged goods ke liye) escalate kar deta hai, jabki complex situations jinme policy exceptions chahiye hoti hai unhe khud autonomously handle karne ki koshish karta hai. Escalation calibration improve karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai? **Sabse effective tareeka kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Har response se pehle agent ko 1-10 scale pe confidence self-rate karwao aur jab confidence ek threshold se neeche jaaye toh automatically human ko route kar do", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Historical tickets pe trained ek separate classifier model deploy karo jo predict kare ki kaunsi requests ko escalation chahiye, main agent process shuru kare us se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "System prompt me explicit escalation criteria add karo, few-shot examples ke saath jo dikhaye ki kab escalate karna hai aur kab autonomously resolve karna hai", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Sentiment analysis implement karo jo customer ki frustration level determine kare aur negative sentiment threshold cross hote hi automatically escalate kar de", "c": false}], "e": "Explicit escalation criteria few-shot examples ke saath directly root cause ko address karte hain — simple aur complex cases ke beech unclear decision boundaries. Ye sabse proportional, effective pehla intervention hai jo agent ko sikhaata hai ki kab escalate karna hai aur kab bina extra infrastructure ke autonomously resolve karna hai."}, "q62": {"q": "`get_customer` aur `lookup_order` call karne ke baad, agent ke paas saara available system data hai lekin phir bhi uncertainty hai. `escalate_to_human` call karne ke liye sabse justified trigger kaunsi situation hai? **Escalation ke liye sabse justified situation kaunsi hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek customer kal shipped hua order cancel karna chahta hai jo kal hi arrive karega. Agent ko escalate karna chahiye kyunki customer package milne ke baad apna mann badal sakta hai", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek customer claim karta hai ki usse order nahi mila, lekin tracking dikhaata hai ki teen din pehle usi ke address pe deliver aur sign hua tha. Agent ko escalate karna chahiye kyunki contradictory evidence present karne se customer relationship kharab ho sakta hai", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek customer competitor price matching request karta hai. Tumhari policies apni site pe price drops ke liye 14 din ke andar price adjustments allow karti hain, lekin competitor prices ke baare me kuch nahi kehti. Agent ko policy interpretation ke liye escalate karna chahiye", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Ek customer ke message me billing question aur product return dono hai. Agent ko escalate karna chahiye taaki ek human dono issues ek hi interaction me coordinate kar sake", "c": false}], "e": "Ye ek genuine policy gap hai: company rules apni site pe price drops cover karte hain lekin competitor price matching ke baare me kuch nahi kehte. Agent ko policy invent nahi karni chahiye aur existing rules ko kaise interpret ya extend karna hai iske liye human judgment ke liye escalate karna chahiye."}, "q63": {"q": "Production logs dikhate hain ki 12% cases me tumhara agent `get_customer` skip karke seedha `lookup_order` call kar leta hai, sirf customer-provided naam use karke, jisse kabhi-kabhi galat account identify hota hai aur galat refund ho jaate hain. Ye reliability problem sabse effectively kaise fix karein? **Sabse effective change kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Few-shot examples add karo jo dikhaye ki agent hamesha pehle `get_customer` call karta hai, chahe customer voluntarily order details de de", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek routing classifier implement karo jo har request analyze kare aur us request type ke hisaab se sirf appropriate tools ka subset enable kare", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek programmatic precondition add karo jo `lookup_order` aur `process_refund` ko block kare jab tak `get_customer` ek verified customer identifier return na kare", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "System prompt ko strengthen karo ye kehte hue ki `get_customer` ke through customer verification kisi bhi order operation se pehle mandatory hai", "c": false}], "e": "Ek programmatic precondition ek deterministic guarantee deta hai ki required sequencing follow ki jaayegi. Ye sabse effective approach hai kyunki isse verification skip hone ki possibility hi khatam ho jaati hai, chahe LLM ka behavior kuch bhi ho."}, "q64": {"q": "Production metrics dikhate hain ki complex billing disputes ya multi-order returns resolve karte waqt, customer satisfaction scores simple cases se 15% kam hain — chahe resolution technically correct hi kyun na ho. Root-cause analysis dikhata hai ki agent accurate solutions deta hai lekin rationale ko inconsistently explain karta hai: kabhi relevant policy details omit kar deta hai, kabhi timeline info ya next steps miss kar deta hai. Specific context gaps case-by-case vary karte hain. Tum bina human oversight add kiye solution quality improve karna chahte ho. Sabse effective approach kaunsa hai? **Sabse effective approach kaunsa hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek self-critique stage add karo jisme agent ek draft response ko completeness ke liye evaluate kare — ye ensure karte hue ki customer ka issue resolve ho, relevant context include ho, aur follow-up questions anticipate ho", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek confirmation stage add karo jisme agent close karne se pehle poochta hai \"Kya isse aapka issue poori tarah resolve ho gaya?\" — taaki customer zaroorat pade toh additional information maang sake", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Complex cases ke liye model ko Haiku se Sonnet me upgrade karo, ek defined complexity metric ke basis pe route karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "System prompt me few-shot examples implement karo jo 5 common complex case types ke liye complete explanations dikhaye, ye demonstrate karte hue ki policy context, timelines, aur next steps kaise include karein", "c": false}], "e": "Ek self-critique stage (evaluator-optimizer pattern) directly inconsistent explanation completeness ko address karta hai — agent ko force karke ki woh apne khud ke draft ko concrete criteria ke against assess kare, jaise policy context, timelines, aur next steps — final present karne se pehle. Isse case-specific gaps bina human oversight ke pakde jaate hain."}, "q65": {"q": "Production metrics dikhate hain ki tumhara agent average 4+ API loops per resolution leta hai. Analysis reveal karti hai ki Claude aksar `get_customer` aur `lookup_order` ko separate sequential turns me request karta hai, chahe dono shuru me hi zaroori kyun na ho. Loops ki sankhya kam karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai? **Loops kam karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Speculative execution implement karo jo automatically likely-needed tools ko kisi bhi requested tool ke parallel call kare aur saare results return kare, chahe kya request kiya gaya ho", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "`max_tokens` badhao taaki Claude ko plan karne aur tool requests ko naturally combine karne ke liye zyada room mile", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "`get_customer_with_orders` jaise composite tools banao jo common lookup combinations ko single calls me bundle karein", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Prompt me Claude ko instruct karo ki woh tool requests ko ek hi turn me bundle kare aur agle API call se pehle saare results ek saath return kare", "c": true}], "e": "Claude ko prompt karna ki woh related tool requests ko ek single turn me bundle kare, uski native ability leverage karta hai ki woh ek saath multiple tools request kar sake. Ye minimal architectural change ke saath directly sequential-call pattern ko fix kar deta hai."}, "q66": {"q": "Production logs ek pattern dikhate hain: customers specific amounts reference karte hain (jaise \"woh 15% discount jo maine mention kiya tha\"), lekin agent galat values ke saath respond karta hai. Investigation dikhati hai ki ye details 20+ turns pehle mention hui thi aur vague summaries me condense ho gayi thi jaise \"promotional pricing discuss hua tha\". Sabse effective fix kya hai? **Sabse effective fix kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Summarization threshold ko 70% se 85% tak badha do taaki summarization trigger hone se pehle conversations ko zyada room mile", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Poori conversation history ko external storage me store karo aur retrieval implement karo jab agent \"as I mentioned\" jaisi references detect kare", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Transactional facts (amounts, dates, order numbers) ko extract karke ek persistent \"case facts\" block me daalo jo summarized history ke bahar har prompt me include ho", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Summarization prompt ko revise karo taaki explicitly saare numbers, percentages, dates, aur customer-stated expectations verbatim preserve ho", "c": false}], "e": "Summarization inherently precise details kho deti hai. Transactional facts ko extract karke ek structured \"case facts\" block me daal dena, jo summarized history ke bahar hota hai, critical information ko preserve karta hai — taaki woh reliably har prompt me available rahe, chahe kitne bhi turns summarize ho chuke ho."}, "q67": {"q": "Tumhara `get_customer` tool naam se search karte waqt saare matches return karta hai. Currently, jab multiple results hote hain, Claude sabse recent order wale customer ko pick kar leta hai, lekin production data dikhata hai ki ambiguous matches ke liye ye 15% baar galat account select kar leta hai. Isko kaise address karein? **Isko kaise address karein?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek confidence scoring system implement karo jo 85% confidence se upar autonomously act kare aur threshold se neeche clarification request kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Claude ko instruct karo ki jab `get_customer` multiple matches return kare, toh koi bhi customer-specific action lene se pehle ek additional identifier (email, phone, ya order number) request kare", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "`get_customer` ko modify karo taaki woh ranking algorithm ke basis pe sirf ek single most-likely match return kare, jisse ambiguity eliminate ho jaaye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Prompt me few-shot examples add karo jo ambiguous matches ke liye correct reasoning aur tool sequencing demonstrate karein", "c": false}], "e": "User se ek additional identifier maangna ambiguity resolve karne ka sabse reliable tareeka hai kyunki user ko apni identity ka definitive knowledge hota hai. Ek extra conversational turn ek chhoti si keemat hai us 15% error rate ko eliminate karne ke liye jo galat account choose hone se hota hai."}, "q68": {"q": "Production logs ek consistent pattern dikhate hain: jab customers apne message me \"account\" word include karte hain (jaise \"main apna account check karna chahta hoon ek order ke liye jo maine kal kiya tha\"), agent 78% baar pehle `get_customer` call karta hai. Jab customers similar requests \"account\" word ke bina phrase karte hain (jaise \"main ek order check karna chahta hoon jo maine kal kiya tha\"), ye 93% baar pehle `lookup_order` call karta hai. Tool descriptions clear aur unambiguous hain. Is discrepancy ka sabse likely root cause kya hai? **Sabse likely root cause kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "System prompt me keyword-sensitive instructions hain jo \"account\" jaise terms ke basis pe behavior steer karte hain, jisse unintended tool-selection patterns ban jaate hain", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Model ki base training \"account\" terminology aur customer-related operations ke beech associations banati hai jo tool descriptions ko override kar deti hai", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Model ko multi-concept messages pe zyada training data chahiye aur usse account aur order dono terminology wale examples pe fine-tune karna chahiye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Tool descriptions me additional negative examples chahiye jo specify karein ki har tool kab NAHI use karna hai, taaki ye keyword-induced confusion prevent ho", "c": false}], "e": "Ye systematic keyword-driven pattern (78% vs 93%) strongly indicate karta hai ki system prompt me explicit routing logic hai jo \"account\" word pe react karke agent ko customer-related tools ki taraf steer karta hai. Kyunki tool descriptions already clear hain, ye discrepancy prompt-level instructions ki taraf point karta hai jo unintended behavioral steering create kar rahi hain."}, "q69": {"q": "Production logs dikhate hain ki agent aksar `get_customer` call kar leta hai jab users orders ke baare me poochte hain (jaise \"mera order #12345 check karo\") — `lookup_order` call karne ke bajaye. Dono tools ki descriptions minimal hain (\"Customer information leta hai\" / \"Order details leta hai\") aur similar-looking identifier formats accept karte hain. Tool selection reliability improve karne ke liye sabse effective pehla step kya hai? **Sabse effective pehla step kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek routing layer implement karo jo har turn se pehle user input analyze kare aur detected keywords aur ID patterns ke basis pe correct tool preselect kar de", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Dono tools ko ek single `lookup_entity` me combine kar do jo koi bhi identifier accept kare aur internally decide kare kaunsa backend query karna hai", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "System prompt me few-shot examples add karo jo correct tool selection patterns demonstrate karein, 5-8 examples ke saath jo order-related queries ko `lookup_order` pe route karein", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Har tool ki description ko expand karo taaki usme input formats, example queries, edge cases, aur boundaries shamil ho jo explain karein ki similar tools ke against ise kab use karna hai", "c": true}], "e": "Tool descriptions ko input formats, example queries, edge cases, aur clear boundaries ke saath expand karna directly root cause fix karta hai — minimal descriptions jo LLM ko similar tools distinguish karne ke liye kaafi information nahi deti. Ye ek low-effort, high-impact pehla step hai jo LLM ke primary tool-selection mechanism ko improve karta hai."}, "q70": {"q": "Tum apne support agent ke liye agent loop implement kar rahe ho. Har Claude API call ke baad, tumhe decide karna hai ki loop continue karna hai (requested tools chalao aur Claude ko dobara call karo) ya stop karna hai (final answer customer ko present karo). Ye decision kis basis pe hoti hai? **Ye decision kis basis pe hoti hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Claude ke response me `stop_reason` field check karo — agar ye `tool_use` hai toh continue karo, aur agar `end_turn` hai toh stop karo", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Claude ke text me phrases dhoondo jaise \"I'm done\" ya \"Can I help with anything else?\" — natural language signals task completion indicate karte hain", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek maximum iteration count set karo (jaise 10 calls) aur wahan pahunch ke stop kar do, chahe Claude aur kaam ki zaroorat indicate kare ya nahi", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Check karo ki response me assistant text content hai ya nahi — agar Claude ne explanatory text generate kiya hai, toh loop terminate ho jaana chahiye", "c": false}], "e": "`stop_reason` Claude ka explicit structured signal hai loop control ke liye: `tool_use` indicate karta hai ki Claude ek tool chalana chahta hai aur result wapas chahta hai, jabki `end_turn` indicate karta hai ki Claude ne apna response complete kar liya hai aur loop end ho jaana chahiye."}, "q71": {"q": "Production logs dikhate hain ki agent tumhare MCP tools ke outputs ko misinterpret karta hai: `get_customer` se Unix timestamps, `lookup_order` se ISO 8601 dates, aur numeric status codes (1=pending, 2=shipped). Kuch tools third-party MCP servers hain jinhe tum modify nahi kar sakte. Data format normalization ke liye sabse maintainable approach kaunsa hai? **Sabse maintainable approach kaunsa hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek PostToolUse hook use karo jo tool outputs ko intercept kare aur agent process karne se pehle formatting transformations apply kare", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Jo tools tum control karte ho unhe modify karo taaki woh human-readable formats return karein, aur third-party tools ke liye wrappers banao", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek `normalize_data` tool banao jise agent har data retrieval ke baad call kare values transform karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "System prompt me detailed format documentation add karo jo har tool ke data conventions explain kare", "c": false}], "e": "Ek PostToolUse hook ek centralized, deterministic point provide karta hai jahan saare tool outputs — third-party MCP server data samet — ko intercept aur normalize kiya ja sakta hai, agent process karne se pehle. Ye zyada maintainable hai kyunki transformations code me rehte hain aur uniformly apply hote hain, LLM interpretation pe depend karne ki bajaye."}, "q72": {"q": "Production logs dikhate hain ki agent kabhi-kabhi `get_customer` choose kar leta hai jab `lookup_order` zyada appropriate hoti, especially ambiguous queries ke liye jaise \"mujhe apni recent purchase me help chahiye\". Tumne decide kiya hai ki system prompt me few-shot examples add karke tool selection improve karo. Kaunsa approach is problem ko sabse effectively address karta hai? **Kaunsa approach sabse effective hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Har tool description me explicit \"use when\" aur \"don't use when\" guidance add karo jo ambiguous cases cover kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Tool ke hisaab se grouped examples add karo — pehle saare `get_customer` scenarios ek saath, phir saare `lookup_order` scenarios", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Specifically ambiguous scenarios pe target karke 4-6 examples add karo, har ek me rationale ke saath ki ek tool doosre plausible alternatives ke against kyun choose kiya gaya", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Har tool ke liye 10-15 clear, unambiguous requests ke examples add karo jo typical scenarios ke liye correct tool choice demonstrate karein", "c": false}], "e": "Few-shot examples ko specifically un ambiguous scenarios pe target karna jahan errors hoti hain, explicit rationale ke saath ki ek tool alternatives se better kyun hai, model ko wo comparative decision process sikhaata hai jo edge cases ke liye chahiye hota hai. Ye generic examples ya declarative rules se zyada effective hai."}, "q4": {"q": "Tumhe ek custom `/review` command chahiye standard code review ke liye, jo poori team ko available ho jab woh repository clone karein. **Command file kahan create karni chahiye?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Project repository me `.claude/commands/` me", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "`~/.claude/commands/` me", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Root `CLAUDE.md` me", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "`.claude/config.json` me", "c": false}], "e": "Project commands jo `.claude/commands/` me store hote hain, version-controlled hote hain aur automatically har kisi ko available ho jaate hain. B personal commands ke liye hai. C instructions ke liye hai, command definitions ke liye nahi. D exist hi nahi karta."}, "q5": {"q": "Tumhe ek monolith ko microservices me restructure karna hai (dozens of files, service-boundary decisions). **Kaunsa approach use karna chahiye?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Planning mode: codebase explore karo, dependencies samjho, approach design karo", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Direct execution incrementally", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Detailed up-front instructions ke saath direct execution", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Direct execution aur mushkil hone pe planning me switch", "c": false}], "e": "Planning mode bade changes, multiple possible approaches, aur architectural decisions ke liye design kiya gaya hai. B expensive rework ka risk leta hai. C assume karta hai ki tumhe structure pehle se pata hai. D reactive approach hai."}, "q6": {"q": "Ek codebase me alag-alag areas me different conventions hain (React, API, database). Tests code ke saath co-located hain. Tum chahte ho ki conventions automatically apply ho. **Kaunsa approach use karna chahiye?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "YAML frontmatter aur glob patterns wali `.claude/rules/` files", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Sab kuch root CLAUDE.md me daal do", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "`.claude/skills/` me Skills", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Har directory me CLAUDE.md", "c": false}], "e": "Glob patterns wali `.claude/rules/` (jaise `**/*.test.tsx`) file paths ke basis pe automatic convention application enable karti hai — jo distributed test files ke liye ideal hai. B model inference pe depend karta hai. C manual/on-demand hai. D tab acha kaam nahi karta jab relevant files kai directories me ho."}, "q12": {"q": "Ek pull request 14 files change karta hai ek inventory tracking module me. Saari files ka single-pass review inconsistent results deta hai: kuch files pe detailed comments, kuch pe superficial, obvious bugs miss ho jaate hain, aur contradictory feedback (ek pattern ek file me problematic flag hota hai lekin identical code doosri file me approve ho jaata hai). **Review ko kaise restructure karna chahiye?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Focused passes me split karo: har file ko individually local issues ke liye analyze karo, phir cross-file data flows ke liye ek separate integration pass chalao", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Developers ko bade PRs ko 3-4 files ke submissions me split karne ko kaho", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek higher-tier model use karo bade context window ke saath taaki saari 14 files ek hi pass me review ho sake", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Teen independent full-PR review passes chalao aur sirf woh issues report karo jo kam se kam do runs me mile ho", "c": false}], "e": "Focused passes directly root cause address karti hain — bohot saari files ek saath process karte waqt attention dilution. Per-file analysis consistent depth ensure karti hai, aur ek separate integration pass cross-file issues catch karti hai. B developers pe burden shift karta hai bina system improve kiye. C ek misconception hai: bada context attention quality fix nahi karta. D inconsistent detections ke across consensus require karke real bugs suppress kar deta hai."}, "q43": {"q": "Tumne Claude Code ko ek function implement karne ko kaha jo API responses ko internal normalized format me transform kare. Do iterations ke baad bhi, output structure abhi bhi expectations match nahi karta — kuch fields differently nested hain aur timestamps galat format me hain. Tumne requirements prose me describe ki, lekin Claude har baar unhe differently interpret karta hai. **Agle iteration ke liye sabse effective approach kaunsa hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Expected output structure describe karta hua ek JSON schema likho aur har iteration ke baad Claude ke output ko us se validate karo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Representative API responses ke liye expected transformation dikhaate hue 2-3 concrete input-output examples do", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Requirements ko zyada technical precision ke saath rewrite karo, exact field mappings, nesting rules, aur timestamp format strings specify karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Claude se poocho ki woh apni current understanding of requirements explain kare, taaki pata chale interpretations kahan diverge kar rahe hain", "c": false}], "e": "Concrete input-output examples prose descriptions ki inherent ambiguity remove kar dete hain, Claude ko exact expected transformation results dikhaakar. Ye directly root cause address karta hai — textual requirements ka misinterpretation — field nesting aur timestamp formatting ke liye unambiguous patterns provide karke."}, "q44": {"q": "Tumhe Slack ko naye notification channel ke roop me add karna hai. Existing codebase me email, SMS, aur push channels ke liye clear, established patterns hain. Lekin Slack ka API fundamentally alag integration approaches offer karta hai — incoming webhooks (simple, one-way), bot tokens (delivery confirmation aur programmatic control support karte hain), ya Slack Apps (two-way events, workspace approval chahiye). Tumhara task sirf itna kehta hai \"Slack support add karo\" bina integration method ya advanced features jaise delivery tracking specify kiye. **Is task ko kaise approach karna chahiye?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Direct execution mode me incoming webhooks use karke shuru karo, taaki existing one-way notification pattern match ho", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Planning mode me switch karo integration options aur architectural implications explore karne ke liye, phir implementation se pehle ek recommendation present karo", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Direct execution mode me existing patterns use karke ek Slack channel class scaffold karo, integration method ka decision baad ke liye defer karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Direct execution mode me bot-token approach use karke shuru karo taaki delivery confirmation possible ho", "c": false}], "e": "Slack integration ke multiple valid approaches hain jinke significantly different architectural implications hain, aur requirements ambiguous hain. Planning mode tumhe webhooks, bot tokens, aur Slack Apps ke trade-offs evaluate karne deta hai aur implementation se pehle ek approach pe align hone deta hai."}, "q45": {"q": "Tumhari CLAUDE.md file 400+ lines tak badh gayi hai jisme coding standards, testing conventions, ek detailed PR review checklist, deployment instructions, aur database migration procedures hain. Tum chahte ho ki Claude hamesha coding standards aur testing conventions follow kare, lekin PR review, deploy, aur migration guidance sirf tab apply ho jab woh tasks ho rahe ho. **Sabse effective restructuring approach kaunsa hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Saari guidance ko separate Skills files me workflow type ke hisaab se organize karo, CLAUDE.md me sirf ek brief project description chhodo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Sab kuch CLAUDE.md me rakho lekin `@import` syntax use karo category ke hisaab se separately maintained files me organize karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "CLAUDE.md ko `.claude/rules/` ke andar files me split karo path-bound glob patterns ke saath taaki har rule sirf relevant file types ke liye load ho", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Universal standards CLAUDE.md me rakho aur workflow-specific guidance (PR review, deploy, migrations) ke liye Skills banao trigger keywords ke saath", "c": true}], "e": "CLAUDE.md content har session me load hota hai, isliye coding standards aur testing conventions hamesha apply hote hain, jabki Skills on-demand invoke hote hain jab Claude trigger keywords detect karta hai — jo PR review, deployment, aur migrations jaise workflow-specific guidance ke liye ideal hai."}, "q46": {"q": "Tumhe team ke monolithic application ko microservices me restructure karna hai. Isse dozens of files me changes hote hain aur service boundaries aur module dependencies ke baare me decisions chahiye hote hain. **Kaunsa approach choose karna chahiye?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Planning mode me switch karo codebase explore karne, dependencies samajhne, aur changes karne se pehle implementation approach design karne ke liye", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Direct execution mode me shuru karo aur unexpected complexity face hone ke baad hi planning me switch karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Direct execution mode me shuru karo aur incremental changes karo, implementation ko naturally service boundaries reveal karne do", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Detailed upfront instructions ke saath direct execution use karo jo har service ki structure specify kare", "c": false}], "e": "Planning mode monolith split karne jaise complex architectural restructuring ke liye sahi strategy hai: ye safe exploration aur boundaries ke baare me informed decisions allow karta hai, kai files me potentially expensive changes commit karne se pehle."}, "q47": {"q": "Tumhari team ne ek `/analyze-codebase` skill banaya jo deep code analysis karta hai — dependency scanning, test coverage counts, aur code quality metrics. Command chalane ke baad, team members report karte hain ki session me Claude less responsive ho jaata hai aur original task ka context kho deta hai. **Full analysis capabilities rakhte hue isse sabse effectively kaise fix karein?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Skill frontmatter me `context: fork` add karo taaki analysis ek isolated subagent context me chale", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Frontmatter me `model: haiku` add karo taaki analysis ke liye ek faster, sasta model use ho", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Skill ko teen chhoti skills me split karo, har ek kam output produce kare", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Skill me instructions add karo jo results display karne se pehle sabko ek short summary me compress kar de", "c": false}], "e": "`context: fork` analysis ko ek isolated subagent context me chalata hai taaki bada output main session ke context window ko pollute na kare aur Claude original task ka track na kho de. Ye main session ko responsive rakhte hue full analysis capability preserve karta hai."}, "q48": {"q": "Tumhari team `.claude/skills/commit/SKILL.md` me ek `/commit` skill use karti hai. Ek developer isse apne personal workflow ke liye customize karna chahta hai (alag commit message format, extra checks) bina teammates ko affect kiye. **Tum kya recommend karoge?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "`~/.claude/skills/` ke neeche ek personal version banao alag naam ke saath, jaise `/my-commit`", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Project skill frontmatter me username ke basis pe conditional logic add karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "`~/.claude/skills/commit/SKILL.md` me same naam ke saath ek personal version banao", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Personal skill frontmatter me `override: true` set karo taaki ye project version se priority le", "c": false}], "e": "Personal skills project skills se same naam hone pe priority le lete hain, isliye naam `commit` reuse karna silently is developer ke liye team ke skill ko shadow kar dega — jab bhi team `/commit` improve karegi, unhe updates nahi milenge, aur unhe yaad rakhna padega ki woh same command ke neeche alag skill chala rahe hain. Personal variant ko `/my-commit` naam dena is collision ko poori tarah avoid karta hai: developer team ke maintained `/commit` ka use karta rehta hai aur unke personal workflow ke liye ek separate, clearly-named skill milti hai, dono ke beech confusion ya team updates miss hone ka koi risk nahi."}, "q49": {"q": "Tumhari team Claude Code kai mahino se use kar rahi hai. Recently, teen developers report karte hain ki Claude guidance follow karta hai \"hamesha comprehensive error handling include karo,\" lekin ek chautha developer jo abhi join hua hai kehta hai ki Claude ye follow nahi karta. Charon same repo me kaam karte hain aur unka code up-to-date hai. **Sabse likely cause aur fix kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Guidance original developers ke user-level `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` files me hai, project ke `.claude/CLAUDE.md` me nahi. Instruction ko project-level file me move karo taaki saare team members ko mile", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Naye developer ki `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` me conflicting instructions hain jo project settings ko override kar rahi hain; unhe conflicting section delete kar dena chahiye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Claude Code time ke saath per-user preferences seekhta hai; naye developer ko requirement dohraana padega jab tak Claude use \"yaad\" na kar le", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Claude Code pehli baar padhne ke baad CLAUDE.md cache kar leta hai; original developers cached versions use kar rahe hain. Sabko Claude Code cache clear karna chahiye", "c": false}], "e": "Agar guidance sirf original developers ke user-level configs me add hui thi aur project-level `.claude/CLAUDE.md` me nahi, toh naye team members ko woh nahi milegi. Isse project-level configuration me move karna ensure karta hai ki saare current aur future team members automatically guidance receive karein."}, "q50": {"q": "Tumne paaya ki 2-3 full endpoint implementation examples ko context ke roop me include karna naye API endpoints generate karte waqt consistency ko significantly improve karta hai. Lekin ye context sirf tab useful hai jab naye endpoints create ho rahe ho — na ki debugging, code review, ya API directory me kisi aur kaam ke waqt. **Kaunsa configuration approach sabse effective hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Endpoint examples aur pattern documentation project CLAUDE.md me add karo taaki woh hamesha available ho", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Har generation request me manually endpoint examples reference karo code ko prompt me copy karke", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "`.claude/rules/api/` me path-specific rules configure karo jo endpoint examples include karein aur API directory me kaam karte waqt activate ho", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Ek skill banao jo endpoint examples reference kare aur pattern-following instructions contain kare, on-demand slash command ke through invoked", "c": true}], "e": "On-demand invoke hone wali skill example context ko sirf tab load karti hai jab naye endpoints generate ho rahe ho, na ki debugging ya review jaise unrelated tasks ke dauran. Ye main context ko clean rakhta hai lekin zaroorat pade toh high-quality generation preserve karta hai."}, "q51": {"q": "Tumhari team ne ek `/migration` skill banaya jo database migration files generate karta hai. Ye migration name `$ARGUMENTS` ke through leta hai. Production me tumne teen issues dekhe: (1) developers aksar bina arguments ke skill chala dete hain, jisse files ke naam kharaab hote hain, (2) skill kabhi-kabhi unrelated prior conversations se database schema details use kar leti hai, aur (3) ek developer ne accidentally destructive test cleanup chala diya jab skill ke paas broad tool access tha. **Kaunsa configuration approach teeno problems fix karta hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "`$ARGUMENTS` ki jagah `$1` aur `$2` positional parameters use karo specific inputs enforce karne ke liye, `@` syntax ke through explicit schema file references include karo context control ke liye, aur destructive operations ke baare me warning wali frontmatter description add karo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Frontmatter me `argument-hint` add karo required parameters request karne ke liye, execution isolate karne ke liye `context: fork` use karo, aur `allowed-tools` ko file-write operations tak restrict karo", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "`/migration-create` aur `/migration-apply` skills me split karo, agar migration name missing ho toh request karne ke liye validation instructions add karo, aur har ek ke liye different `allowed-tools` scopes use karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Skill ke SKILL.md me validation instructions add karo taaki `$ARGUMENTS` ek valid name ho, prior conversation context ignore karne ke instructions add karo, aur avoid karne wale prohibited operations list karo", "c": false}], "e": "Ye teen alag configuration features use karta hai har problem address karne ke liye: `argument-hint` argument entry improve karta hai aur missing arguments kam karta hai, `context: fork` prior conversations se context leakage prevent karta hai, aur `allowed-tools` skill ko safe file-writing operations tak constrain karta hai, jo destructive actions prevent karta hai."}, "q52": {"q": "Tumhare codebase me alag conventions wale areas hain: React components functional style hooks ke saath use karte hain, API handlers async/await use karte hain specific error handling ke saath, aur database models repository pattern follow karte hain. Test files codebase me distributed hain, code ke saath (jaise `Button.test.tsx` `Button.tsx` ke paas), aur tum chahte ho ki saare tests same conventions follow karein chahe location kuch bhi ho. **Claude ko automatically correct conventions apply karwane ka sabse supported tareeka kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Saari conventions root CLAUDE.md me daalo har area ke headings ke neeche aur Claude pe rely karo ye infer karne ke liye ki kaunsa section apply hota hai", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "`.claude/skills/` me har code type ke liye skills banao, conventions ko har SKILL.md me embed karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Har subdirectory me ek separate CLAUDE.md file rakho jisme us area ki conventions ho", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "`.claude/rules/` ke neeche rule files banao YAML frontmatter ke saath jo glob patterns specify kare conventions ko file paths ke basis pe conditionally apply karne ke liye", "c": true}], "e": "YAML frontmatter aur glob patterns (jaise `**/*.test.tsx`, `src/api/**/*.ts`) wali `.claude/rules/` files deterministic, path-based convention application enable karti hain chahe directory structure kuch bhi ho. Ye distributed test files jaisi cross-cutting patterns ke liye sabse supported approach hai."}, "q53": {"q": "Tum ek custom slash command `/review` banana chahte ho jo team ki standard code review checklist chalaye. Ye har developer ko available hona chahiye jab woh repository clone ya update karein. **Command file kahan create karni chahiye?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Har developer ke home directory me `~/.claude/commands/` me", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Project repository me `.claude/commands/` ke neeche", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "`.claude/config.json` me commands ke array ke roop me", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Root project CLAUDE.md me", "c": false}], "e": "Custom slash commands ko project repository ke andar `.claude/commands/` me rakhna ensure karta hai ki woh version-controlled ho aur automatically har developer ko available ho jo repo clone ya update kare. Project-level custom commands ke liye Claude Code me yehi intended location hai."}, "q54": {"q": "Tumhari team ki CLAUDE.md 500 lines se zyada badh gayi hai jisme TypeScript conventions, testing guidance, API patterns, aur deployment procedures mix ho gaye hain. Developers ko sahi sections dhoondhna aur update karna mushkil lagta hai. **Claude Code project-level instructions ko focused topical modules me organize karne ke liye kaunsa approach support karta hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek `.claude/config.yaml` define karo jo file patterns ko CLAUDE.md ke andar specific sections se map kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "`.claude/rules/` me separate Markdown files banao, har ek ek topic cover kare (jaise `testing.md`, `api-conventions.md`)", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Instructions ko relevant subdirectories ke README.md files me split karo jo Claude automatically instructions ke roop me load kare", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Directory tree ke different levels pe multiple files banao jinka naam CLAUDE.md ho, har ek parent instructions ko override kare", "c": false}], "e": "Claude Code ek `.claude/rules/` directory support karta hai jahan tum topical guidance ke liye separate Markdown files bana sakte ho (jaise `testing.md`, `api-conventions.md`), jo teams ko bade instruction sets ko focused, maintainable modules me organize karne deta hai."}, "q55": {"q": "Tumne ek custom skill `/explore-alternatives` banaya jo team implementation approaches ko brainstorm aur evaluate karne ke liye use karti hai kisi ek choose karne se pehle. Developers report karte hain ki skill chalane ke baad, subsequent Claude responses alternatives discussion se influenced hote hain — kabhi rejected approaches reference karte hain ya exploration context retain karte hain jo actual implementation ke saath interfere karta hai. **Is skill ko sabse effectively kaise configure karna chahiye?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Skill me `!` prefix use karo exploration logic ko bash subprocess ke roop me chalane ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Skill frontmatter me `context: fork` add karo", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Do skills me split karo — `/explore-start` aur `/explore-end` — boundaries mark karne ke liye ki exploration context kab discard hona chahiye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Skill ko `.claude/skills/` ki jagah `~/.claude/skills/` me create karo", "c": false}], "e": "`context: fork` skill ko ek isolated subagent context me chalata hai taaki exploration discussions main conversation history ko pollute na karein. Ye rejected approaches aur brainstorming context ko subsequent implementation work influence karne se rokta hai."}, "q56": {"q": "Tumhari team ek GitHub MCP server add karna chahti hai PRs search karne aur CI status check karne ke liye Claude Code ke through. Six developers me se har ek ke paas apna personal GitHub access token hai. Tum credentials version control me commit kiye bina consistent tooling chahte ho poori team me. **Kaunsa configuration approach sabse effective hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Har developer ko `claude mcp add --scope user` ke through user scope me server add karwao", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek MCP server wrapper banao jo `.env` file se tokens read kare aur GitHub API calls proxy kare, phir wrapper ko project `.mcp.json` me add karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Server ko project `.mcp.json` me environment variable substitution (`${GITHUB_TOKEN}`) use karke add karo auth ke liye, aur required environment variable ko project README me document karo", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Server ko project scope me ek placeholder token ke saath configure karo, phir developers ko kaho ki apne local config me override karein", "c": false}], "e": "Environment variable substitution wala project `.mcp.json` idiomatic hai: ye MCP configuration ke liye ek single version-controlled source of truth provide karta hai jabki har developer environment variables ke through credentials supply karta hai. Variable ko document karna secrets commit kiye bina onboarding easy banata hai."}, "q57": {"q": "Tum 120-file codebase me external API calls ke around error-handling wrappers add kar rahe ho. Kaam ke teen phases hain: (1) saare call sites aur patterns discover karo, (2) collaboratively error-handling approach design karo, aur (3) wrappers ko consistently implement karo. Phase 1 me, Claude bada output generate karta hai jisme hundreds of call sites context ke saath list hote hain, jo discovery finish hone se pehle hi context window jaldi bhar deta hai. **Implementation consistency maintain karte hue task complete karne ka sabse effective approach kaunsa hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Phase 1 ke liye ek Explore subagent use karo verbose discovery output isolate karne ke liye aur ek summary return karne ke liye, phir Phases 2-3 main conversation me continue karo", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Saare phases main conversation me karo, periodically `/compact` use karte hue context usage kam karne ke liye files ke through move karte waqt", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Headless mode me `--continue` ke saath switch karo, batch calls ke beech explicit context summaries pass karte hue continuity maintain karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "CLAUDE.md me error-handling pattern define karo, phir files ko batches me multiple sessions me process karo shared memory file pe rely karte hue consistency ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "Ek Explore subagent verbose discovery output ko ek separate context me isolate karta hai aur main conversation ko sirf ek concise summary return karta hai. Ye main context window ko preserve karta hai collaborative design aur consistent implementation phases ke liye jahan retained context sabse zyada valuable hai."}, "q7": {"q": "System \"AI impact on creative industries\" research kar raha hai, lekin reports sirf visual art cover karti hain. Coordinator ne topic ko decompose kiya: \"AI in digital art,\" \"AI in graphic design,\" \"AI in photography.\" **Cause kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Synthesis agent gaps detect nahi karta", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Coordinator ne task ko bohot narrowly decompose kiya", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Web search agent thoroughly search nahi karta", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Document analysis agent non-visual sources ko filter kar deta hai", "c": false}], "e": "Logs dikhate hain ki coordinator ne \"creative industries\" ko sirf visual subtopics me decompose kiya, music, literature, aur film completely miss karte hue. Subagents ne apna kaam sahi kiya — issue ye hai ki unhe kya assign kiya gaya tha."}, "q8": {"q": "Ek web-search subagent timeout ho jaata hai ek complex topic research karte waqt. Tumhe design karna hai ki error information coordinator ko kaise wapas pass ho. **Kaunsa error propagation approach sabse acha intelligent recovery enable karta hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Structured error context coordinator ko return karo: failure type, query, partial results, aur alternatives", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Subagent ke andar automatic retries implement karo exponential backoff ke saath, phir ek generic \"search unavailable\" status return karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Subagent ke andar timeout catch karo aur ek empty result set return karo jo success mark ho", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Timeout exception ko ek top-level handler tak propagate karo jo poore workflow ko terminate kar de", "c": false}], "e": "Structured error context — failure type, executed query, partial results, aur alternatives samet — coordinator ko woh sab deta hai jo use intelligent recovery decisions lene ke liye chahiye (jaise modified query ke saath retry karna ya partial results ke saath continue karna). B ek generic status ke peeche context chhupa deta hai. C failure ko success ke roop me mask kar deta hai. D poora workflow bina zaroorat ke abort kar deta hai."}, "q9": {"q": "Synthesis agent ko aksar specific claims verify karne ki zaroorat padti hai results merge karte waqt. Currently, jab verification chahiye, synthesis agent control coordinator ko wapas de deta hai, jo web-search agent call karta hai aur phir naye results ke saath synthesis re-run karta hai. Isse per task 2-3 extra round trips add hote hain aur latency 40% badh jaati hai. Tumhara assessment dikhata hai ki 85% ye checks simple fact checks hain (dates, names, statistics), jabki 15% ko deeper investigation chahiye. **Overhead kam karte hue reliability maintain kaise karein?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Synthesis agent ko ek limited `verify_fact` tool do simple checks ke liye, aur complex verification ko coordinator ke through hi route karte raho", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Saari verification needs ko ek batch me accumulate karo aur end me coordinator ko return karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Synthesis agent ko saare web-search tools ka full access do", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Har source ke around proactively additional context cache karo", "c": false}], "e": "Ye least privilege ka principle apply karta hai: synthesis agent ko exactly wahi milta hai jo 85% common case (simple fact checks) ke liye chahiye, jabki complex investigations ke liye coordinator-mediated path preserve rehta hai. B blocking dependencies introduce karta hai (baad ke synthesis steps pehle verified facts pe depend kar sakte hain). C separation of responsibilities todta hai. D speculative caching pe rely karta hai jo needs reliably predict nahi kar sakta."}, "q13": {"q": "Ek document analysis agent discover karta hai ki do credible sources me ek key metric ke liye directly contradictory statistics hain: ek government report 40% growth batata hai, jabki ek industry analysis 12% batata hai. Dono sources credible lagte hain, aur ye discrepancy research conclusions ko materially affect kar sakta hai. Document analysis agent ko is situation ko sabse effectively kaise handle karna chahiye? **Kaunsa approach sabse effective hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Credibility heuristics apply karo sabse likely correct number choose karne ke liye, us value ke saath analysis khatam karo, aur discrepancy mention karta ek footnote add karo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Dono numbers ko analysis output me include karo unhe conflicting mark kiye bina, synthesis agent ko decide karne do ki broader context ke basis pe konsa use karein", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Analysis stop karo aur turant coordinator ko escalate karo, usse poocho ki continue karne se pehle kaunsa source zyada authoritative hai", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Dono numbers ke saath analysis complete karo, conflict ko clearly source attribution ke saath annotate karo, aur coordinator ko decide karne do ki data ko synthesis ko pass karne se pehle kaise reconcile karna hai", "c": true}], "e": "Ye approach separation of responsibilities preserve karta hai: analysis agent apna core kaam bina block kiye complete karta hai, dono conflicting values ko clear attribution ke saath preserve karta hai, aur reconciliation ko correctly coordinator ko pass karta hai, jiske paas broader context hai."}, "q14": {"q": "Web-search aur document-analysis agents ne apne tasks complete kar liye hain aur results coordinator ko return kar diye hain. Ek integrated research report banane ke liye agla step kya hai? **Sabse appropriate agla step kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Har agent apne results directly report-writing agent ko bhej de, coordinator ko bypass karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Document analysis agent web-search results request karke unhe internally merge kar le", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Coordinator dono result sets ko synthesis agent ko pass kare ek unified integration ke liye", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Coordinator dono agents ke raw outputs ko concatenate karke unhe final result ke roop me return kar de", "c": false}], "e": "Coordinator-subagent architecture me, coordinator dono result sets ko synthesis agent ko forward karta hai centralized integration ke liye, jo control preserve karta hai aur high-quality merging ensure karta hai."}, "q15": {"q": "Ek document analysis subagent PDF files process karte waqt aksar fail ho jaata hai: kuch me corrupted sections hain jo parsing exceptions trigger karte hain, kuch password-protected hain, aur kabhi-kabhi parsing library bade files pe hang ho jaati hai. Currently, koi bhi exception subagent ko turant terminate kar deti hai aur coordinator ko error return karti hai, jise decide karna padta hai ki retry karein, skip karein, ya poori task fail karein. Isse routine error handling me coordinator ki excessive involvement hoti hai. Sabse effective architectural improvement kya hai? **Sabse effective improvement kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek dedicated error-handling agent banao jo shared queue ke through saari failures monitor kare aur recovery actions decide kare, subagents ko directly restart commands bheje", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Subagent ko configure karo ki woh hamesha partial results ek success status ke saath return kare, error details ko metadata me embed karte hue; coordinator saare responses ko successful treat kare", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Coordinator ko saari documents subagent ko bhejne se pehle validate karwao, un documents ko reject karte hue jo failures cause kar sakte hain", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Subagent me transient failures ke liye local recovery implement karo aur sirf woh errors coordinator ko escalate karo jinhe woh khud resolve nahi kar sakta, attempted steps aur partial results samet", "c": true}], "e": "Errors ko lowest level pe handle karo jo unhe resolve kar sake. Local recovery coordinator ka workload kam karta hai jabki truly unrecoverable issues ko full context aur partial progress ke saath escalate bhi karta rehta hai."}, "q16": {"q": "\"AI impact on creative industries\" pe system chalane ke baad, tumne dekha ki har subagent successfully complete hota hai: web-search agent relevant articles dhoondhta hai, document analysis agent unhe correctly summarize karta hai, aur synthesis agent coherent text produce karta hai. Lekin final reports sirf visual art cover karti hain aur music, literature, aur film completely miss kar deti hain. Coordinator logs me, tum dekhte ho ki isne topic ko teen subtasks me decompose kiya: \"AI in digital art,\" \"AI in graphic design,\" aur \"AI in photography.\" Sabse likely root cause kya hai? **Sabse likely root cause kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Synthesis agent ke paas coverage gaps detect karne ke instructions nahi hain", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Document analysis agent overly strict relevance criteria ki wajah se non-visual sources filter kar deta hai", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Coordinator ka task decomposition bohot narrow hai, subagents ko aisa kaam assign karta hai jo saare relevant areas cover nahi karta", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Web-search agent ki queries insufficient hain aur unhe zyada sectors cover karne ke liye broaden karna chahiye", "c": false}], "e": "Coordinator ne ek broad topic ko sirf visual-art subtasks me decompose kiya, music, literature, aur film ko completely miss karte hue. Kyunki subagents ne apne assignments correctly execute kiye, narrow decomposition hi obvious root cause hai."}, "q17": {"q": "Web-search subagent 5 me se sirf 3 requested source categories ke results return karta hai (competitor sites aur industry reports succeed hote hain, lekin news archives aur social feeds timeout ho jaate hain). Document analysis subagent successfully saari provided documents process kar leta hai. Synthesis subagent ko mixed-quality upstream inputs se ek summary produce karna hai. Sabse effective error-propagation strategy kya hai? **Sabse effective error-propagation strategy kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Sirf successful sources use karke synthesis continue karo aur bina mention kiye ki kaunsa data unavailable tha, ek output produce karo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Synthesis subagent coordinator ko ek error return kare, jo incomplete data ki wajah se ek full retry ya task failure trigger kare", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Synthesis subagent coordinator se pooche ki synthesis shuru karne se pehle timed-out sources ko longer timeout ke saath retry kare", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Synthesis output ko coverage annotations ke saath structure karo jo indicate kare ki kaunse conclusions well-supported hain aur kahan gaps hain unavailable sources ki wajah se", "c": true}], "e": "Coverage annotations transparency ke saath graceful degradation implement karte hain, completed work se value preserve karte hue jabki uncertainty ko propagate karte hain taaki confidence ke baare me informed decisions liye ja sakein."}, "q18": {"q": "Document analysis subagent ek corrupted PDF file encounter karta hai jise woh parse nahi kar sakta. System ki error handling design karte waqt, is failure ko handle karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai? **Kaunsa approach sabse effective hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Coordinator agent ko context ke saath ek error return karo, usse decide karne do ki kaise aage badhein", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Corrupted document ko silently skip karo aur baaki files process karna continue karo, workflow interrupt hone se bachne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Document parse karne ki teen baar automatically retry karo exponential backoff ke saath, failure report karne se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Ek exception throw karo jo poora research workflow terminate kar de", "c": false}], "e": "Coordinator agent ko context ke saath error return karna sabse effective approach hai kyunki isse coordinator ko informed decision lene deta hai — file skip karna, alternative parsing method try karna, ya user ko notify karna — jabki failure me visibility bhi maintain rehti hai."}, "q19": {"q": "Production logs ek persistent pattern dikhate hain: requests jaise \"uploaded quarterly report analyze karo\" 45% time web-search agent ko route hoti hain document analysis agent ki jagah. Tool definitions review karte waqt, tum paate ho ki web-search agent ke paas ek tool `analyze_content` hai jo \"content analyze karta hai aur key information extract karta hai\" describe kiya gaya hai, jabki document analysis agent ke paas ek tool `analyze_document` hai jo \"documents analyze karta hai aur key information extract karta hai\" describe kiya gaya hai. Is misrouting problem ko kaise fix karein? **Misrouting problem ko kaise fix karein?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek pre-routing classifier add karo jo detect kare ki user uploaded files reference kar raha hai ya web content, coordinator delegation decide karne se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Web-search tool ka naam `extract_web_results` rename karo aur description update karo \"web search aur URLs se retrieve ki gayi information process karta aur return karta hai\"", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Coordinator prompt me few-shot examples add karo correct routing dikhaate hue: \"User uploads a quarterly report → document analysis agent\" aur \"User asks about a web page → web-search agent\"", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Document analysis tool description ko usage examples ke saath expand karo jaise \"Uploaded PDFs, Word docs, aur spreadsheets ke liye use karo,\" web-search tool ko unchanged rakhte hue", "c": false}], "e": "Web-search tool ka naam `extract_web_results` rename karna aur description ko explicitly web search aur URLs reference karne ke liye update karna, dono tool names aur descriptions ke beech semantic overlap ko eliminate karke root cause remove karta hai. Ye har tool ka purpose unambiguous banata hai, coordinator ko document analysis aur web search reliably distinguish karne dete hue."}, "q20": {"q": "Ek colleague propose karta hai ki document analysis agent ko apne results directly synthesis agent ko bhejne chahiye, coordinator ko bypass karte hue. Coordinator ko subagents ke beech saari communication ke central hub ke roop me rakhne ka main advantage kya hai? **Main advantage kya hai coordinator ko central hub rakhne ka?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Coordinator saari interactions observe kar sakta hai, errors uniformly handle kar sakta hai, aur decide kar sakta hai ki har subagent ko kaunsi information milni chahiye", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Coordinator subagents ko multiple requests batch karta hai, total API calls aur overall latency kam karta hue", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Coordinator ke through routing automatic retry logic enable karta hai jo direct inter-agent calls support nahi kar sakti", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Subagents isolated memory use karte hain, aur direct communication ke liye complex serialization chahiye hogi jo sirf coordinator hi perform kar sakta hai", "c": false}], "e": "Coordinator pattern saari interactions me centralized visibility deta hai, poore system me uniform error handling, aur har subagent ko kaunsi information mile iska fine-grained control — ye ek star-shaped communication topology ke primary advantages hain."}, "q21": {"q": "Web-search subagent timeout ho jaata hai ek complex topic research karte waqt. Tumhe design karna hai ki is failure ke baare me information coordinator ko kaise return ho. Kaunsa error-propagation approach sabse acha intelligent recovery enable karta hai? **Kaunsa error-propagation approach sabse acha intelligent recovery enable karta hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Structured error context coordinator ko return karo, jisme failure type, executed query, koi bhi partial results, aur potential alternative approaches shamil ho", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Subagent ke andar timeout catch karo aur ek empty result set return karo jo successful mark ho", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Subagent ke andar automatic exponential-backoff retries implement karo, sirf retries exhaust hone ke baad ek generic \"search unavailable\" status return karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Timeout exception ko directly top-level handler tak propagate karo, poora research workflow terminate karte hue", "c": false}], "e": "Structured error context return karna — failure type, executed query, partial results, aur alternative approaches samet — coordinator ko wo sab deta hai jo intelligent recovery decisions lene ke liye chahiye (jaise modified query ke saath retry karna ya partial results ke saath continue karna). Ye informed coordination-level decision-making ke liye maximum context preserve karta hai."}, "q22": {"q": "Apne system design me, tumne document analysis agent ko ek general-purpose tool `fetch_url` diya taaki woh URL se documents download kar sake. Production logs dikhate hain ki ye agent ab frequently search engine results pages download karta hai ad hoc web search perform karne ke liye — jo behavior web-search agent ke through route hona chahiye — inconsistent results cause karte hue. Kaunsa fix sabse effective hai? **Kaunsa fix sabse effective hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "`fetch_url` ko ek `load_document` tool se replace karo jo validate kare ki URLs document formats point karte hain", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Document analysis agent se `fetch_url` remove karo aur saari URL fetching ko coordinator ke through web-search agent tak route karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Filtering implement karo jo `fetch_url` calls ko known search engine domains ke against block kare, baaki URLs allow karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Document analysis agent prompt me instructions add karo ki `fetch_url` sirf document URLs download karne ke liye use hona chahiye, search karne ke liye nahi", "c": false}], "e": "Ek general-purpose tool ko document-specific tool se replace karna jo URLs ko document formats ke against validate kare, interface level pe capability constrain karke root cause fix karta hai. Ye least privilege ka principle follow karta hai, undesired search behavior ko sirf discourage karne ke bajaye impossible bana deta hai."}, "q23": {"q": "Ek broad topic research karte waqt, tum dekhte ho ki web-search agent aur document analysis agent same subtopics investigate karte hain, jisse unke outputs me substantial duplication hoti hai. Token usage lagbhag double ho jaata hai bina research breadth ya depth me proportional increase ke. Isse address karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai? **Isse address karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Dono agents ko parallel me finish hone do, phir coordinator overlapping results deduplicate kare unhe synthesis agent ko pass karne se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Coordinator delegate karne se pehle explicitly research space ko partition kare, har agent ko distinct subtopics ya source types assign karte hue", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek shared-state mechanism implement karo jahan agents apna current focus area log karein taaki dusre agents execution ke dauran dynamically duplication avoid kar sakein", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Sequential execution pe switch karo jahan document analysis sirf web search complete hone ke baad chale, web-search results ko context ke roop me use karte hue duplication avoid karne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "Coordinator ko explicitly research space partition karwana delegate karne se pehle sabse effective hai kyunki ye root cause address karta hai — unclear task boundaries — kisi bhi kaam shuru hone se pehle. Ye parallelism preserve karta hai jabki duplicated effort aur wasted tokens prevent karta hai."}, "q24": {"q": "Research ke dauran, web-search subagent teen source categories query karta hai different outcomes ke saath: academic databases 15 relevant papers return karti hain, industry reports \"0 results\" return karti hain, aur patent databases \"Connection timeout\" return karti hain. Coordinator ko error propagation design karte waqt, kaunsa approach sabse achhe recovery decisions enable karta hai? **Kaunsa approach sabse acche recovery decisions enable karta hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Results ko ek single success-percentage metric me aggregate karo (jaise \"67% source coverage\") detailed logs ke saath demand pe available", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "\"timeout\" aur \"0 results\" dono ko failures ke roop me report karo jinhe coordinator intervention chahiye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Transient failures internally retry karo aur sirf persistent errors report karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Access failures (timeout) ko distinguish karo jinhe retry decision chahiye, valid empty results (\"0 results\") se jo successful queries represent karte hain", "c": true}], "e": "Ek timeout (access failure) aur \"0 results\" (valid empty result) semantically different outcomes hain jinhe different responses chahiye. Unhe distinguish karna coordinator ko patent database retry karne deta hai jabki industry reports \"0 results\" ko ek valid, informative finding ke roop me accept karta hai."}, "q25": {"q": "Production monitoring inconsistent synthesis quality dikhati hai. Jab aggregated results ~75K tokens ke hote hain, synthesis agent reliably first 15K tokens (web-search headlines/snippets) aur last 10K tokens (document analysis conclusions) se cite karta hai, lekin aksar middle ke 50K tokens me critical findings miss kar deta hai — chahe woh directly research question ka answer kyun na de. Aggregated input ko kaise restructure karein? **Aggregated input ko kaise restructure karein?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Saare subagent outputs ko 20K tokens se kam me summarize karo aggregation se pehle, taaki content model ki reliable processing range me rahe", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Subagent results ko incrementally synthesis agent ko stream karo, pehle web-search results ko completion tak process karte hue, phir document analysis results add karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Aggregated input ki shuruat me ek key-findings summary rakho aur detailed results ko explicit section headings ke saath organize karo aasaan navigation ke liye", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Rotation implement karo jo alternate kare ki kaunsa subagent ka result pehle appear karta hai research tasks ke across, taaki dono sources ko time ke saath equal top positioning mile", "c": false}], "e": "Shuruat me ek key-findings summary rakhna primacy effects leverage karta hai taaki critical information sabse reliably processed position me rahe. Explicit section headings poore me add karna model ko mid-input content navigate karne me madad karta hai, directly \"lost in the middle\" phenomenon mitigate karte hue."}, "q26": {"q": "Testing me, web-search agent (85K tokens page content samet) aur document analysis agent (70K tokens chains of thought samet) ka combined output total 155K tokens hai, lekin synthesis agent 50K tokens se kam inputs pe sabse achha perform karta hai. Kaunsa solution sabse effective hai? **Kaunsa solution sabse effective hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Upstream agents ko modify karo taaki woh verbose content aur reasoning ki jagah structured data (key facts, quotes, relevance scores) return karein", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek intermediate summarization agent add karo jo synthesis ko pass karne se pehle findings condense kare", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Synthesis agent ko findings ko sequential batches me process karwao, calls ke beech state maintain karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Findings ko ek vector database me store karo aur synthesis agent ko search tools do apne kaam ke dauran query karne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "Upstream agents ko modify karke structured data return karwana root cause fix karta hai token volume ko source pe kam karke jabki essential information preserve karte hue. Ye bulky page content aur reasoning traces pass karne se bachta hai jo tokens inflate karte hain bina synthesis step improve kiye."}, "q27": {"q": "Testing me, tum dekhte ho ki synthesis agent ko aksar specific claims verify karne ki zaroorat padti hai results merge karte waqt. Currently, jab verification chahiye, synthesis agent control coordinator ko return kar deta hai, jo web-search agent call karta hai aur phir results ke saath synthesis re-invoke karta hai. Isse per task 2-3 extra loops add hote hain aur latency 40% badh jaati hai. Tumhara assessment dikhata hai ki 85% ye verifications simple fact checks hain (dates, names, stats), jabki 15% ko deeper research chahiye. Kaunsa approach system reliability preserve karte hue overhead sabse effectively kam karta hai? **Sabse effective approach kaunsa hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Synthesis agent ko saare web-search tools ka access do taaki woh koi bhi verification need directly handle kar sake bina coordinator loops ke", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Synthesis agent ko saari verification needs accumulate karwao aur unhe end me ek batch ke roop me coordinator ko return karwao, jo phir unhe ek saath web-search agent ko bheje", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Web-search agent ko proactively har source ke around extra context cache karwao initial research ke dauran, is anticipation me ki synthesis ko verification chahiye hogi", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Synthesis agent ko ek limited-scope `verify_fact` tool do simple checks ke liye, jabki complex verifications ko coordinator ke through web-search agent tak route karo", "c": true}], "e": "Ek limited-scope fact-verification tool synthesis agent ko 85% simple checks directly handle karne deta hai, zyada tar loops eliminate karte hue, jabki 15% complex verifications ke liye coordinator delegation path preserve rehta hai. Ye least privilege apply karta hai jabki latency significantly kam karta hai."}, "q10": {"q": "Ek pipeline `claude \"Analyze this pull request for security issues\"` chalata hai, lekin ye interactive input ke wait me hang ho jaata hai. **Sahi approach kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "`-p` flag use karo: `claude -p \"Analyze this pull request for security issues\"`", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "`CLAUDE_HEADLESS=true` set karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "`/dev/null` se stdin redirect karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "`--batch` use karo", "c": false}], "e": "`-p` (ya `--print`) Claude Code ko non-interactive mode me chalane ka documented tareeka hai. Ye prompt process karta hai, stdout pe print karta hai, aur exit ho jaata hai. Baaki options ya toh non-existent features hain ya Unix workarounds."}, "q11": {"q": "Team automated analysis ke liye API cost kam karna chahti hai. Claude currently do workflows real time me serve karta hai: (1) ek blocking pre-merge check jo developers ke PR merge karne se pehle complete hona chahiye, aur (2) ek tech-debt report jo overnight generate hoti hai morning review ke liye. Ek manager propose karta hai dono ko Message Batches API pe move karke 50% save kiya jaaye. **Is proposal ko kaise evaluate karein?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Batch processing sirf tech-debt reports ke liye use karo; real-time calls pre-merge checks ke liye rakho", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Dono workflows ko batch processing me move karo aur completion ke liye poll karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Dono ke liye real-time calls rakho batch results ordering me issues avoid karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Dono ko batch processing me move karo aur agar batch time zyada le toh real time pe fallback rakho", "c": false}], "e": "Message Batches API 50% save karta hai, lekin processing time 24 hours tak le sakta hai bina guaranteed latency SLA ke. Isse blocking pre-merge checks ke liye unsuitable ban jaata hai jahan developers wait kar rahe hote hain, lekin overnight batch workloads jaise tech-debt reports ke liye ideal hai."}, "q28": {"q": "Tumhara CI pipeline Claude Code CLI chalata hai (`--print` mode me) CLAUDE.md use karke code review ke liye project context provide karne ke liye, aur developers generally reviews ko substantive paate hain. Lekin woh report karte hain ki findings ko workflow me integrate karna mushkil hai — Claude narrative paragraphs output karta hai jinhe manually PR comments me copy karna padta hai. Team chahti hai ki har finding ek separate inline PR comment ke roop me code me relevant jagah pe automatically post ho, jiske liye structured data chahiye — file path, line number, severity level, aur suggested fix. Kaunsa approach sabse effective hai? **Kaunsa approach sabse effective hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "CLAUDE.md me ek \"Output Format for Review\" section add karo structured findings ke examples ke saath taaki Claude project context se expected format seekh le", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "CLI flags `--output-format json` aur `--json-schema` use karo structured findings enforce karne ke liye, phir output ko parse karo inline comments post karne ke liye GitHub API ke through", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Review prompt me explicit formatting instructions include karo jo require kare ki har finding ek parseable template follow kare jaise `[FILE:path] [LINE:n] [SEVERITY:level] ...`", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Narrative review format rakho lekin ek summarization step add karo jo Claude use karke findings ka ek structured JSON summary generate kare", "c": false}], "e": "`--output-format json` ko `--json-schema` ke saath use karna CLI level pe structured output enforce karta hai, well-formed JSON guarantee karte hue required fields (file path, line number, severity, suggested fix) ke saath jo reliably parse ho sakte hain aur GitHub API ke through inline PR comments ke roop me post ho sakte hain."}, "q29": {"q": "Tumhari team code suggestions generate karne ke liye Claude Code use karti hai, lekin tum ek pattern notice karte ho: non-obvious issues — performance optimizations jo edge cases break karte hain, cleanups jo unexpectedly behavior change kar dete hain — sirf tab pakde jaate hain jab koi doosra team member PR review karta hai. Generation ke dauran Claude ka reasoning dikhata hai ki usne ye cases consider kiye the lekin conclude kiya ki uska approach correct tha. Kaunsa approach is self-check limitation ka root cause directly address karta hai? **Kaunsa approach root cause ko directly address karta hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek second independent Claude Code instance chalao changes review karne ke liye bina generator ke reasoning tak access ke", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Generation stage ke liye extended thinking mode enable karo taaki suggestions produce karne se pehle zyada thorough deliberation ho sake", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Generation prompt me explicit self-review instructions add karo Claude se apne khud ke suggestions ko critique karne ko kehte hue finalize karne se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Prompt context me full test files aur documentation include karo taaki Claude generation ke dauran expected behavior ko behtar samajh sake", "c": false}], "e": "Ek second independent Claude Code instance bina generator ke reasoning tak access ke, root cause ko directly address karta hai confirmation bias avoid karke. Ye \"fresh eyes\" perspective human peer review jaisa hai, jahan doosra reviewer wo issues pakadta hai jo author ne rationalize kiye the."}, "q30": {"q": "Tumhara code review component iterative hai: Claude changed file analyze karta hai, phir related files (imports, base classes, tests) request kar sakta hai tool calls ke through context samajhne ke liye final feedback dene se pehle. Tumhari application ek tool define karti hai jo Claude ko file contents request karne deta hai; Claude tool call karta hai, results paata hai, aur analysis continue karta hai. Tum batch processing evaluate kar rahe ho API cost kam karne ke liye. Is workflow ke liye batch processing consider karte waqt primary technical limitation kya hai? **Primary technical limitation kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Batch processing me correlation IDs include nahi hote outputs ko input requests se map back karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Asynchronous model mid-request tool execute nahi kar sakta aur results return nahi kar sakta Claude ko analysis continue karne ke liye", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Batch API request parameters me tool definitions support nahi karti", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "24 hours tak ki batch processing latency pull request feedback ke liye bohot slow hai, chahe workflow otherwise function karta ho", "c": false}], "e": "Ek \"fire-and-forget\" asynchronous Batch API model ke paas koi mechanism nahi hai ek tool call ko request ke dauran intercept karne, tool execute karne, aur results return karne ka Claude ko analysis continue karne ke liye. Ye fundamentally incompatible hai iterative tool-calling workflows ke saath jinhe multiple tool request/response rounds chahiye ek single logical interaction ke andar."}, "q31": {"q": "Tumhara CI/CD system teen Claude-based analyses chalata hai: (1) fast style checks har PR pe jo merging ko block karte hain completion tak, (2) comprehensive weekly security audits poore codebase ke, aur (3) nightly test-case generation recently changed modules ke liye. Message Batches API 50% savings offer karta hai lekin processing 24 hours tak le sakta hai. Tum API cost optimize karna chahte ho ek acceptable developer experience maintain karte hue. Kaunsa combination har task ko sahi API approach se match karta hai? **Kaunsa combination sahi hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Teeno tasks ke liye Message Batches API use karo 50% savings maximize karne ke liye, pipeline ko batch completion ke liye poll karne configure karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "PR style checks ke liye synchronous calls use karo; weekly security audits aur nightly test generation ke liye Message Batches API use karo", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Teeno tasks ke liye synchronous calls use karo consistent response times ke liye, prompt caching pe rely karte hue costs kam karne ke liye workloads ke across", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "PR style checks aur nightly test generation ke liye synchronous calls use karo; sirf weekly security audits ke liye Message Batches API use karo", "c": false}], "e": "PR style checks developers ko block karte hain aur immediate responses chahiye synchronous calls ke through, jabki weekly security audits aur nightly test generation scheduled tasks hain flexible deadlines ke saath jo 24-hour batch window tolerate kar sakte hain — dono ke liye 50% savings capture karte hue."}, "q32": {"q": "Tumhare automated reviews real issues dhoondh lete hain, lekin developers report karte hain ki feedback actionable nahi hai. Findings me phrases hote hain jaise \"complex ticket routing logic\" ya \"potential null pointer\" bina specify kiye ki exactly kya change karna hai. Jab tum detailed instructions jaise \"hamesha concrete fix suggestions include karo\" add karte ho, model phir bhi inconsistent output produce karta hai — kabhi detailed, kabhi vague. Kaunsi prompting technique sabse reliably consistently actionable feedback produce karti hai? **Sabse reliable prompting technique kaunsi hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Instructions ko aur refine karo feedback format ke har part ke liye zyada explicit requirements ke saath (location, issue, severity, proposed fix)", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Context window expand karo zyada surrounding codebase include karne ke liye taaki model ke paas concrete fixes propose karne ke liye kaafi information ho", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek two-pass approach implement karo jahan ek prompt issues identify kare aur doosra fixes generate kare, specialization allow karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Prompt me 3-4 few-shot examples add karo exact required format dikhaate hue: identified issue, location in code, concrete fix suggestion", "c": true}], "e": "Few-shot examples sabse effective technique hain consistent output format achieve karne ke liye jab instructions akele variable results produce karte hain. 3-4 examples provide karna jo exact desired structure dikhaate hain (issue, location, concrete fix), model ko ek concrete pattern deta hai follow karne ke liye, jo abstract instructions se zyada reliable hai."}, "q33": {"q": "Tumhare CI pipeline me do Claude-based code review modes hain: ek pre-merge-commit hook jo PR merge ko block karta hai completion tak, aur ek \"deep analysis\" jo overnight chalta hai, batch completion ke liye poll karta hai, aur PR ko detailed suggestions post karta hai. Tum API cost kam karna chahte ho Message Batches API use karke, jo 50% savings offer karta hai lekin polling chahiye aur 24 hours tak le sakta hai. Kaunsa mode batch processing use karna chahiye? **Kaunsa mode batch processing use karna chahiye?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Sirf pre-merge-commit hook", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Sirf deep analysis", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Dono modes", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Koi bhi mode nahi", "c": false}], "e": "Deep analysis batch processing ke liye ek ideal candidate hai kyunki ye already overnight chalta hai, delay tolerate karta hai, aur ek polling model use karta hai results publish karne se pehle — jo Message Batches API ke asynchronous, polling-based architecture se match karta hai 50% savings capture karte hue."}, "q34": {"q": "Tumhara automated review comments aur docstrings analyze karta hai. Current prompt Claude ko instruct karta hai \"check karo ki comments accurate aur up to date hain.\" Findings aksar acceptable patterns flag kar deti hain (TODO markers, simple descriptions) jabki un comments ko miss kar deti hain jo aisa behavior describe karti hain jo code ab implement hi nahi karta. Kaunsa change is inconsistent analysis ke root cause ko address karta hai? **Kaunsa change root cause ko address karta hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "`git blame` data include karo taaki Claude un comments ko identify kar sake jo recent code changes se pehle ke hain", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Misleading comments ke few-shot examples add karo model ko codebase me similar patterns recognize karne me madad ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "TODO, FIXME, aur descriptive comment patterns ko filter karo analysis se pehle noise kam karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Explicit criteria specify karo: comments ko sirf tab flag karo jab woh claimed behavior code ke actual behavior se contradict kare", "c": true}], "e": "Explicit criteria — comments ko sirf tab flag karna jab claimed behavior actual code behavior se contradict kare — directly root cause address karta hai ek vague instruction ko ek precise definition se replace karke ki problem kya hota hai. Ye acceptable patterns pe false positives aur truly misleading comments ko misses kam karta hai."}, "q35": {"q": "Tumhara automated code review system inconsistent severity ratings dikhata hai — similar issues jaise null pointer risks kuch PRs me \"critical\" rate hote hain lekin doosron me sirf \"medium.\" Developer surveys growing distrust dikhate hain — bohot log findings dismiss karna shuru kar dete hain bina padhe kyunki \"aadhi galat hain.\" High-false-positive categories accurate categories me trust erode karti hain. Kaunsa approach developer trust ko sabse acche se restore karta hai system improve karte hue? **Kaunsa approach developer trust ko sabse acche se restore karta hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "High-false-positive categories (style, naming, documentation) ko temporarily disable karo aur sirf high-precision categories rakho prompts improve karte hue", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Saari categories enabled rakho lekin har finding ke saath confidence scores dikhao taaki developers decide kar sakein ki kya investigate karna hai", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Saari categories enabled rakho aur few-shot examples add karo har category ke liye accuracy improve karne ke liye agle kuch hafton me", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Saari categories me uniform strictness reduction apply karo overall false-positive rate kam karne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "High-false-positive categories ko temporarily disable karna turant trust erosion rokta hai noisy findings remove karke jo developers ko sab kuch dismiss karne ki taraf le jaate hain, jabki high-precision categories jaise security aur correctness se value preserve karta hai. Ye problematic categories ke prompts improve karne ke liye bhi space create karta hai unhe dobara enable karne se pehle."}, "q36": {"q": "Tumhara automated review har PR ke liye test-case suggestions generate karta hai. Ek PR review karte waqt jo course completion tracking add karta hai, Claude 10 test cases suggest karta hai, lekin developer feedback dikhata hai ki 6 duplicate scenarios hain jo already existing test suite me cover ho chuke hain. Kaunsa change duplicate suggestions ko sabse effectively kam karta hai? **Kaunsa change sabse effective hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Existing test file ko context me include karo taaki Claude determine kar sake ki kaunse scenarios already covered hain", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Requested suggestions ki sankhya 10 se 5 kar do, ye assume karte hue ki Claude sabse valuable cases ko pehle prioritize karega", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Instructions add karo jo Claude ko direct kare ki woh sirf edge cases aur error conditions pe focus kare, success paths pe nahi", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Post-processing implement karo jo suggestions filter kare jinke descriptions existing test names se keyword overlap match karein", "c": false}], "e": "Existing test file ko include karna duplication ke root cause ko fix karta hai: Claude sirf tab already-covered scenarios suggest karne se bach sakta hai jab use pata ho ki kaunse tests already exist karte hain. Ye Claude ko genuinely naye, valuable tests propose karne ke liye zaroori information deta hai."}, "q37": {"q": "Ek initial automated review 12 findings identify karne ke baad, ek developer naye commits push karta hai issues address karne ke liye. Review ko dobara chalane se 8 findings milti hain, lekin developers report karte hain ki 5 duplicate hain previous comments jo code pe hain jo naye commits me already fix ho chuka hai. Is redundant feedback ko eliminate karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai thoroughness maintain karte hue? **Redundant feedback eliminate karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Review sirf tab chalao jab PR create ho aur final pre-merge state me ho, intermediate commits skip karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek post-processing filter add karo jo previous findings match karne wali findings ko file paths aur issue descriptions ke basis pe remove kare comments post karne se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Review scope ko sirf most recent push me changed files tak restrict karo, earlier commits ki files exclude karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Previous review findings ko context me include karo aur Claude ko instruct karo ki woh sirf naye ya abhi bhi unresolved issues report kare", "c": true}], "e": "Prior review findings ko context me include karna Claude ko naye problems ko un se distinguish karne deta hai jo recent commits me already address ho chuke hain. Ye review thoroughness preserve karta hai jabki Claude ke reasoning ka use karta hai fixed code pe redundant feedback avoid karne ke liye."}, "q38": {"q": "Tumhara pipeline script `claude \"Analyze this pull request for security issues\"` chalata hai, lekin job indefinitely hang ho jaati hai. Logs dikhate hain ki Claude Code interactive input ke wait me hai. Automated pipeline me Claude Code chalane ka sahi approach kya hai? **Sahi approach kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek `--batch` flag add karo: `claude --batch \"Analyze this pull request for security issues\"`", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "`-p` flag add karo: `claude -p \"Analyze this pull request for security issues\"`", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "`/dev/null` se stdin redirect karo: `claude \"Analyze this pull request for security issues\" < /dev/null`", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "`CLAUDE_HEADLESS=true` environment variable set karo command chalane se pehle", "c": false}], "e": "`-p` (ya `--print`) flag Claude Code ko non-interactively chalane ka documented tareeka hai. Ye prompt process karta hai, result stdout pe print karta hai, aur exit ho jaata hai bina user input ka wait kiye — CI/CD pipelines ke liye ideal."}, "q39": {"q": "Ek pull request 14 files change karta hai ek inventory tracking module me. Ek single-pass review jo saari files ko ek saath analyze karta hai, inconsistent results deta hai: kuch files pe detailed feedback lekin kuch pe shallow comments, obvious bugs miss ho jaate hain, aur contradictory feedback (ek pattern ek file me flag hota hai lekin identical code same PR ki doosri file me approve ho jaata hai). Review ko kaise restructure karein? **Review ko kaise restructure karein?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Teen independent full-PR review passes chalao aur sirf woh issues flag karo jo teen me se kam se kam do runs me appear ho", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Focused passes me split karo: har file ko individually local issues ke liye review karo, phir cross-file data flows examine karne ke liye ek separate integration-oriented pass chalao", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Developers ko require karo ki woh bade PRs ko chhote 3-4 files ke submissions me split karein automated review chalane se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Ek bade model pe switch karo bigger context window ke saath taaki woh saari 14 files ko ek pass me sufficient attention de sake", "c": false}], "e": "Focused per-file passes root cause address karti hain — attention dilution — consistent depth aur reliable local issue detection ensure karte hue. Ek separate integration-oriented pass phir cross-file concerns cover karta hai jaise dependency aur data-flow interactions."}, "q40": {"q": "Tumhara automated code review average 15 findings per pull request deta hai, aur developers 40% false-positive rate report karte hain. Bottleneck investigation time hai: developers ko har finding pe click karna padta hai Claude ka rationale padhne ke liye ye decide karne se pehle ki fix karein ya dismiss karein. Tumhari CLAUDE.md me already acceptable patterns ke liye comprehensive rules hain, aur stakeholders ne reject kar diya kisi bhi approach ko jo findings ko developers ko dikhane se pehle filter kare. Kaunsa change investigation time ko sabse acche se address karta hai? **Kaunsa change investigation time ko sabse acche se address karta hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Claude ko require karo ki woh apna rationale aur confidence estimate directly har finding me include kare", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek post-processor add karo jo finding patterns analyze kare aur automatically un findings ko suppress kare jo historical false-positive signatures match karti hain", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Findings ko \"blocking issues\" vs \"suggestions\" me categorize karo, level ke hisaab se different review requirements ke saath", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Claude ko configure karo sirf high-confidence findings dikhane ke liye, uncertain flags ko developers ko dikhane se pehle filter karte hue", "c": false}], "e": "Rationale aur confidence ko directly har finding me include karna investigation time kam karta hai developers ko quickly triage karne dete hue bina har finding kholne ke. Ye \"no filtering\" constraint ko satisfy karta hai kyunki saari findings visible rehti hain jabki developer decision-making accelerate hoti hai."}, "q41": {"q": "Tumhare automated code review ke analysis dikhate hain ki false-positive rates category ke hisaab se bahut differ karti hain: security/correctness findings me 8% false positives hain, performance findings me 18%, style/naming findings me 52%, aur documentation findings me 48%. Developer surveys growing distrust dikhate hain — bohot log findings dismiss karna shuru kar dete hain bina padhe kyunki \"aadhi galat hain.\" High-false-positive categories accurate categories me trust erode karti hain. Kaunsa approach developer trust ko sabse acche se restore karta hai system improve karte hue? **Kaunsa approach developer trust ko sabse acche se restore karta hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "High-false-positive categories (style, naming, documentation) ko temporarily disable karo aur sirf high-precision categories rakho prompts improve karte hue", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Saari categories enabled rakho lekin har finding ke saath confidence scores dikhao taaki developers decide kar sakein ki kya investigate karna hai", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Saari categories enabled rakho aur few-shot examples add karo har category ke liye accuracy improve karne ke liye agle kuch hafton me", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Saari categories me uniform strictness reduction apply karo overall false-positive rate kam karne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "High-false-positive categories ko temporarily disable karna turant trust erosion rokta hai noisy findings remove karke jo developers ko sab kuch dismiss karne ki taraf le jaate hain, jabki high-precision categories jaise security aur correctness se value preserve karta hai. Ye problematic categories ke prompts improve karne ke liye bhi space create karta hai unhe dobara enable karne se pehle."}, "q42": {"q": "Tumhari team automated analysis ke liye API costs kam karna chahti hai. Currently, synchronous Claude calls do workflows support karte hain: (1) ek blocking pre-merge check jo developers ke merge karne se pehle complete honi chahiye, aur (2) ek technical debt report jo overnight generate hoti hai agle din morning review ke liye. Tumhara manager propose karta hai dono ko Message Batches API pe move karke 50% save kiya jaaye. Is proposal ko kaise evaluate karein? **Is proposal ko kaise evaluate karein?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Dono ko batch processing me move karo synchronous calls pe fallback ke saath agar batches zyada time len", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Dono workflows ko batch processing me status polling ke saath move karo completion verify karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Batch processing sirf technical debt reports ke liye use karo; synchronous calls pre-merge checks ke liye rakho", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Dono workflows ke liye synchronous calls rakho batch result ordering me issues avoid karne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "Message Batches API processing 24 hours tak le sakti hai bina latency SLA ke, jo overnight technical debt reports ke liye acceptable hai lekin blocking pre-merge checks ke liye unacceptable hai jahan developers wait kar rahe hote hain. Ye har workflow ko latency requirements ke basis pe sahi API se match karta hai."}, "q73": {"q": "Tumhara `remove_team_member` tool ek `dry_run: boolean` parameter use karta hai impacts preview karne ke liye execution se pehle. Production monitoring dikhati hai ki agent preview step ko bypass kar deta hai `dry_run=false` directly call karke. Tumhe ensure karna hai ki har removal se pehle ek preview ho jo user explicitly confirm kare. **Sabse reliable approach kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Server-side validation add karo jo `dry_run=false` ko sirf tab allow kare jab same parameters wali ek `dry_run=true` call pichhle 60 seconds me hui ho", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Tool ko confirmation required ke roop me annotate karo aur orchestration layer configure karo ki woh user se approval maange kisi bhi annotated tool ki call forward karne se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Tool description me detailed instructions aur few-shot examples add karo jo require karein ki agent hamesha pehle `dry_run=true` ke saath call kare aur dobara call karne se pehle user confirmation ka wait kare", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Do tools se replace karo: `preview_remove_member` impact details aur ek single-use confirmation token return kare; `execute_remove_member` ko us token ki zaroorat ho, execution ko preview se bind karte hue", "c": true}], "e": "Do-tool token-binding approach architecturally impossible bana deta hai bina prior preview ke execute karna — execute tool literally ek token maangta hai jo sirf preview tool generate kar sakta hai. Ye ek hi approach hai jo constraint ko code level pe enforce karta hai, LLM ke instructions follow karne (C), timing heuristics (A), ya orchestration infrastructure (B) pe rely karne ki jagah."}, "q74": {"q": "Production monitoring dikhati hai ki tumhara `search_catalog` tool 12% time fail hota hai: 8% network timeouts hain jo retry karne pe succeed ho jaate hain, aur 4% query syntax errors hain jo chahe kitni bhi retry karo kabhi succeed nahi hote. Currently dono error types identically return hote hain, jisse retries waste hoti hain. **Tool ki error handling ko kaise modify karna chahiye?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "System prompt me few-shot examples add karo jo dikhaye ki network errors ko syntax errors se kaise distinguish karein", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Saare errors pe uniformly exponential backoff retry logic apply karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Tool ke andar network timeouts ke liye automatic retry implement karo backoff ke saath; syntax errors ko turant parameter validation details ke saath return karo", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Saare errors ko ek `retryable` boolean flag aur error type details ke saath return karo", "c": false}], "e": "Tool level pe transient errors ke liye retries handle karna sahi abstraction boundary hai — tool ko error type ka definitive knowledge hai aur woh deterministic retry logic implement kar sakta hai bina agent pe rely kiye ek flag interpret karne (D) ya prompt-level instructions follow karne (A) ke liye. Uniform backoff (B) syntax errors pe time waste karta hai jo kabhi succeed nahi honge."}, "q75": {"q": "Investment strategy pe kai turns discuss karte hue, ek user ne kaha \"Mera risk tolerance bohot kam hai\" aur baad me \"Main apne returns maximize karna chahta hoon.\" Ab woh poochte hain: \"Mujhe kis me invest karna chahiye?\" **Kaunsa approach sabse acche se ensure karta hai ki recommendation user ki actual priority se align ho?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Contradiction surface karo aur user se clarify karne ko kaho ki kya zyada matter karta hai", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Dono scenarios ke liye separate recommendations do", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Sabse recently stated preference ke saath aage badho", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Conflict address kiye bina ek balanced portfolio recommend karo", "c": false}], "e": "Jab user preferences ek doosre se directly contradict karti hain, conflict surface karna aur clarification maangna hi ek tareeka hai guarantee karne ka ki recommendation user ki true intent se align ho. Koi bhi doosra approach ek assumption banata hai jo galat ho sakta hai — returns maximize karna aur low risk tolerance fundamentally incompatible goals hain jinhe ek human decision chahiye."}, "q76": {"q": "Users conversation ke multiple turns me playlist preferences refine karte hain. Ek user ke \"Mujhe jazz pasand hai\" kehne ke do messages baad, Claude poochta hai \"Aapko kaunse genres pasand hain?\" **Sabse likely cause kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Claude ko conversation memory maintain karne ke liye ek vector database connection chahiye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Model ka context window exceed ho gaya hai", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Claude API ko ek `session_id` parameter chahiye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Tumhari application `messages` array me prior messages include nahi kar rahi", "c": true}], "e": "Claude ke paas koi server-side memory nahi hai — har API call stateless hai. Bina har request ke `messages` array me poori conversation history include kiye, Claude ko prior turns ka koi knowledge nahi hota. Vector databases (A) aur `session_id` (C) Claude ke architecture ka hissa nahi hain; context window overflow (B) do-message exchanges ke liye impossible hai."}, "q77": {"q": "40-minute wale cooking session ke baad, conversation 78,000 tokens tak pahunch jaati hai. History me allergies, recipe scaling, clarified cooking terms, aur general discussion hain. Tumhe tokens kam karne hain important information preserve karte hue. **Kaunsa approach preservation aur token reduction ke beech sabse acha balance karta hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Poori conversation history ko summarize karo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Sirf sabse recent 20,000 tokens rakho", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Critical structured data (allergies, quantities, preferences) extract karo, general discussion summarize karo, aur recent exchanges verbatim rakho", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Poori conversation ko externally store karo aur semantic search ke through relevant parts retrieve karo", "c": false}], "e": "Hybrid approach sabse lowest cost pe sabse highest-value information preserve karta hai. Allergies aur recipe quantities jaise critical facts ek compact structured block me extract kiye jaate hain (summarization ke dauran hone wala precision loss prevent karte hue), general discussion summarize hoti hai, aur recent exchanges verbatim rakhe jaate hain conversational coherence ke liye. Options A aur B critical dietary information kho sakte hain; D ek single cooking session ke liye architectural overkill hai."}, "q78": {"q": "Users report karte hain ki extended conversations ke dauran assistant earlier topics aur preferences ka track kho deta hai. Tumhari current implementation sirf last 25 message pairs rakhti hai. **Sabse effective solution kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Hybrid approach: older messages ko summarize karo jabki recent ones ko verbatim rakho", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Poori conversation history pe vector similarity search", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Window ko 50 message pairs tak badhao", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Har turn dropped messages ko summarize karo aur running summary prepend karo", "c": false}], "e": "Hybrid approach problem ke dono dimensions ko address karta hai: exact recent context retain karna (conversational coherence ke liye critical) jabki earlier preferences ka ek compressed representation maintain karna (pairs drop hone pe total loss prevent karte hue). Window badhana (C) simply same problem delay karta hai. Vector search (B) important context miss kar sakta hai jo current query ke semantically similar na ho. Full per-turn summarization (D) overhead add karta hai aur summarization errors accumulate karta hai."}, "q79": {"q": "Users report karte hain ki jab conversations 50 turns se zyada ho jaati hain toh latency badh jaati hai aur costs badh jaate hain. **Primary cause kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Poori conversation history har API request ke saath include ki jaati hai", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Model progressively longer responses generate karta hai", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "History badhne pe database operations slow ho jaate hain", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Model ek internal user profile banata hai jise zyada processing chahiye", "c": false}], "e": "Claude ka API fully stateless hai — har request ko `messages` array me complete conversation history include karni hoti hai. Jaise-jaise conversations badhti hain, har request zyada tokens carry karti hai, jo directly processing latency aur cost dono badha deta hai. Model calls ke beech koi internal state maintain nahi karta (D galat hai), aur response length inherently conversation length se linked nahi hai (B)."}, "q80": {"q": "Teen mahine ke weekly sessions ke baad, conversation history 85,000 tokens tak badh jaati hai. Jab ek user poochta hai \"Isolation ke theme ke baare me humne kya conclude kiya tha?\", assistant generic answers deta hai previous discussions reference karne ki bajaye. **Sabse effective approach kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Rolling window truncation", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Progressive summarization jo key conclusions capture kare", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Semantic embeddings ke saath relevant exchanges ka retrieval", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Discussion conclusions mark karne wale structured XML tags add karo", "c": false}], "e": "Conversation history pe semantic search ek hi approach hai jo teen mahine ki discussion tak scale kar sakta hai jabki demand pe specific relevant exchanges surface kar sake. Rolling window (A) zyaadatar history discard kar dega. Progressive summarization (B) discussions ko abstractions me compress karta hai jo specific conclusions kho deta hai jo users pooch rahe hain. XML tags (D) ko saara past content restructure karna padega aur ye is scale pe retrieval problem solve nahi karta."}, "q81": {"q": "QA testing ke dauran, Claude pehle 10-15 turns tak system prompt guidelines follow karta hai, lekin baad ke responses deviate ho jaate hain. Conversation abhi bhi token limits ke andar hai. **Best solution kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Behavioral guidelines ko first user message me move karo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "20 turns ke baad ek naya conversation shuru karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Conversation breakpoints pe guidelines reinforce karne wale user-role messages insert karo", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Post-response validation use karo non-compliant responses regenerate karne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "Behavioral reminders ka periodic injection directly instruction drift ka mukabla karta hai constraints ko regular intervals pe re-establish karke jaise conversation history accumulate hoti hai. Guidelines ko first user message me move karna (A) unki authority kam kar deta hai. Naya conversation shuru karna (B) context destroy kar deta hai. Post-response validation (D) corrective hai preventive nahi, aur significant latency add karta hai."}, "q82": {"q": "Tumhare AI tutor ke paas ek 2,800-token system prompt hai jo teaching methodology aur adaptation rules define karta hai. 12 turns ke baad, assistant proficiency levels ignore karna shuru kar deta hai. **Sabse effective fix kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Har 4-5 turns me reminders inject karo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Verbose rules ko few-shot examples se replace karo jo proficiency-level adaptation demonstrate karein", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Critical rules ko system prompt ke end me rakho", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Responses evaluate karo aur difficulty level mismatch hone pe regenerate karo", "c": false}], "e": "Ek 2,800-token system prompt declarative rules ke saath drift ke liye vulnerable hai kyunki abstract rules ko model ko har turn pe unke baare me reason karna padta hai. Verbose rules ko concrete few-shot examples se replace karna jo correct proficiency-level adaptation demonstrate karte hain, model ko clear behavioral patterns deta hai match karne ke liye — ye abstract instructions se zyada reliably kai turns tak follow hota hai. Reminder injection (A) madad karta hai lekin symptoms address karta hai; end-placement (C) initially madad karta hai lekin turn-level drift ke saath nahi; regeneration (D) expensive aur corrective hai."}, "q83": {"q": "Tumhare assistant ko ek enthusiastic tone maintain karna hai, apni reasoning explain karni hai, aur clarifying questions poochne hain. Ye behavioral guidelines kahan define honi chahiye? **Ye behavioral guidelines kahan define honi chahiye?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Har user message ke start me prepend ki jaayein", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "System prompt me", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "First assistant message me", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Environment variables me", "c": false}], "e": "System prompt specifically persistent behavioral constraints aur guidelines ke liye design kiya gaya hai jo poori conversation me apply hote hain. Har user message me prepend karna (A) redundant overhead hai. First assistant message (C) unreliable hai kyunki model apne khud ke prior statements se deviate kar sakta hai. Environment variables (D) ka model behavior pe koi effect nahi hota."}, "q84": {"q": "Users repetitive response openings report karte hain jaise \"Certainly!\" aur \"I'd be happy to help!\" **Sabse effective approach kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek partial assistant message append karo ek direct response opening ke saath", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Temperature setting kam karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Responses ko post-process karo greetings remove karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "System prompt instructions add karo un phrases ko avoid karne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "Assistant ke response ko ek direct answer ki shuruat ke saath prefill karna, generation level pe hi greeting patterns rokta hai — model prefill se continue karta hai naye opening phrases generate karne ki jagah. System prompt instructions (D) madad kar sakti hain lekin kam reliable hain kyunki model phir bhi variants produce kar sakta hai. Post-processing (C) ek fragile workaround hai. Temperature (B) randomness control karta hai, specific phrase patterns ko nahi."}, "q85": {"q": "Ek webhook tumhare system ko notify karta hai ki user ka package ship ho gaya hai jabki user actively chat kar raha hai. Tum chahte ho ki assistant ise naturally next response me incorporate kare. **Best approach kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Shipping status ko system prompt me add karo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek immediate synthetic user message bhejo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Assistant ko har turn ek status tool call karne ke liye force karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Status update ko agle user message me prefix ke roop me append karo", "c": true}], "e": "Status update ko agle user message me prefix karna real-time context ko ek natural conversation boundary pe inject karta hai bina flow disrupt kiye. System prompt modify karna (A) session rebuild karne ki zaroorat padti hai ya architecturally cumbersome hai. Ek synthetic user message (B) natural dialogue flow break kar sakta hai aur attribution confuse kar sakta hai. Har turn ek tool call force karna (C) wasteful hai jab events rare ho."}, "q86": {"q": "Users frequently requests bhejte hain jaise \"Party ke liye ek venue book karo.\" Assistant 4+ clarifying questions poochta hai, jisse 35% abandonment hoti hai. **Kaunsa approach trade-off ko sabse acche se improve karta hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Hidden defaults ke saath aage badho", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Saare clarifying questions ek compound message me poocho", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Assumptions explicitly state karo aur aage badho corrections invite karte hue", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Ek structured intake form use karo", "c": false}], "e": "Assumptions ko explicitly state karke aage badhna, user ko turant ek useful response deta hai jabki unki galat assumptions correct karne ki ability preserve karta hai. Hidden defaults (A) user ko unaware chhod deta hai ki kya assume kiya gaya. Ek compound question list (B) phir bhi user se upfront effort maangti hai. Ek structured form (D) aur zyada friction add karta hai, kam nahi — jo abandonment kam karne ke goal ko contradict karta hai."}, "q87": {"q": "Tumhara assistant ek contractor-persona system prompt use karta hai. Early turns rules follow karti hain, lekin turn 7 tak assistant generic advice dene lagta hai. Conversation length sirf 2,500 tokens hai. **Sabse likely cause kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "System prompts sirf initial behavior establish karte hain", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Turns accumulate hone pe model attention weaken ho jaati hai", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Accumulated assistant responses system prompt ki influence dilute kar deti hain", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "System prompt sirf ek baar bheja jaata hai", "c": false}], "e": "Jaise-jaise assistant responses conversation history me accumulate hoti hain, system prompt ke behavioral constraints reflect karne wale text ka proportion, growing assistant-generated content ke against kam hota jaata hai. Model increasingly apne khud ke prior outputs se pattern-match karta hai system prompt ki bajaye, drift ko compound karte hue chahe token length chhota hi kyun na ho. System prompt har API call me include hota hai (D standalone explanation ke roop me galat hai), aur model attention degradation (B) 2,500 tokens pe operate nahi karta."}, "q88": {"q": "Users vague requests bhejte hain jaise \"Kya aap report me help kar sakte ho?\" Assistant multiple questions poochke respond karta hai (kaunsi report? kaisi help? deadline?), jisse 40% abandonment hoti hai. **Best solution kya hai?**", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Reasonable assumptions banao, unhe explicitly state karo, aur adjust karne ka offer do", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ambiguity ko ek chhote model se classify karo respond karne se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Predefined interpretations use karo assumptions state kiye bina", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Assistant ko har turn ek clarifying question tak limit karo", "c": false}], "e": "Reasonable stated assumptions ke saath aage badhna back-and-forth ko completely eliminate kar deta hai jabki user ko informed aur control me rakhta hai. Predefined silent interpretations (C) users ko confused chhod deti hain jab response unki intent match nahi karta. Ek single-question limit (D) ko phir bhi back-and-forth ke turns chahiye hote hain. Ek chhota classification model (B) latency aur infrastructure complexity add karta hai bina core UX problem solve kiye."}};
const PREGEN_HI_CCARF = {"c1": {"q": "Ek developer agent ko investigate karne ko bolta hai ki ek specific API endpoint kabhi-kabhi 500 responses kyun deta hai. Codebase me 200+ files hain aur developer ko nahi pata konse components involved hain. Agent ko error trace karna hai routing, middleware, business logic, aur database layers ke through.\n\nKaunsa task decomposition approach sabse effective hoga?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Agent se pehle ek comprehensive plan banwao jo saare code paths ko documented components ke through map kare, koi bhi exploration ya code reading shuru karne se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Char layers ke file system pe parallel worker agents chalao, phir unki findings ko combine karke poora error path reconstruct karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Investigation steps ka ek fixed sequence upfront define karo — pehle error handlers ke liye grep karo, phir middleware examine karo, phir database queries check karo, phir middleware-woven code examine karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Agent ko dynamically investigation subtasks generate karne do based on jo woh har step pe discover karta hai, apna exploration plan adapt karte hue jaise-jaise error path ke baare me nayi information emerge hoti hai", "c": true}], "e": "Debugging apni nature se adaptive hoti hai — har file jo tum padhte ho agle sabse useful step ko badal deti hai. Agent ko evidence follow karne do. Baaki: A) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | B) Isse coordination overhead badhta hai aur justified nahi hai jab tak kaam clearly independent subtasks me separable na ho. | C) Surface-level searching yahan bohot narrow hai kyunki task ko simple text matching se zyada rich structural understanding chahiye."}, "c3": {"q": "Ek engineer ne kal Claude Code use karke ek legacy monolith me authentication flows investigate kiye the, ek 2-hour session me significant context build karte hue. Aaj woh us specific investigation ko continue karna chahti hai. Usne tab se teen aur codebases pe kaam kiya hai aur use pata hai ki session ka naam \"auth-deep-dive\" tha.\n\nUse kaise resume karna chahiye?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "`--continue` use karo jahan sabse recent conversation chhoda tha wahin se pick up karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "`--resume auth-deep-dive` use karo us specific session ko naam se load karne ke liye", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "`--session-id` use karo kal ke session transcript file se UUID ke saath", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Fresh shuru karo aur same files dobara padho", "c": false}], "e": "`--resume` ek specific session ko naam se resume karne deta hai. `--continue` sirf sabse recent conversation continue karta hai (na ki 2 din pehle wali session), aur `--session-id` ko ek specific UUID chahiye, naam nahi. Baaki: A) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | C) Poora transcript dump karna noise add karta hai aur agle actor ke liye key facts jaldi dhoondhna mushkil banata hai. | D) Fresh shuru karna useful context waste kar deta hai jo scenario preserve karna chahta hai, isliye underlying problem solve kiye bina cost add karta hai."}, "c4": {"q": "Ek engineer ka exploration subagent 30 minute lagakar ek legacy payment system analyze kar raha tha, 47 files padh ke aur data flows document karke. Session interrupt ho gaya jab engineer ka connection drop ho gaya. Jab woh door tha, ek teammate ne ek PR merge kiya jisne do utility functions rename kar diye. Engineer wahi exploration continue karna chahta hai.\n\nSabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek fresh subagent launch karo aur initial prompt me prior transcript include karo context ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek fresh subagent launch karo prior findings ke ek summary ke saath", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Subagent ko uske previous transcript se resume karo aur use renamed functions ke baare me inform karo", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Subagent ko uske previous transcript se resume karo bina changes mention kiye — architecture understanding valid rehti hai", "c": false}], "e": "Purane transcript se continue karna renamed functions ki updated information ke saath optimal hai: accumulated 30 minutes ka architectural context intact rakhta hai, jabki agents ko specific changes ke baare me notify karke scratch se re-analyze karne se bachata hai. Baaki: A) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | B) Ye coordination boundary ko clearer nahi banata, isliye workflow phir bhi fragile ya inefficient rahega. | D) Naye changes ko explicitly incorporate kiye bina resume karna stale assumptions ko agle step me carry forward karne ka risk leta hai."}, "c31": {"q": "Document analysis agent ke paas ek single `analyze_document` tool hai jo ek document aur ek free-text instruction parameter leta hai. Evaluation ke dauran, requests jaise \"key financial metrics extract karo\" aksar narrative summaries return karte hain, jabki \"methodology summarize karo\" kabhi-kabhi raw data tables return karta hai. Synthesis agent report karta hai ki 35% analysis results ko clarified instructions ke saath re-requests chahiye hote hain.\n\nReliability improve karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Coordinator ko har analysis request pre-classify karwao instructions document analysis agent ko pass karne se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Generic tool ko purpose-specific tools me split karo — `extract_data_points`, `summarize_content`, `verify_claim_against_source` — har ek ke defined input/output contracts ke saath", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Tool description ko detailed examples ke saath enhance karo jo dikhaye ki different instruction phrasings ko different output formats me kaise map karna hai", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Single tool rakho lekin ek `analysis_type` enum parameter add karo jo extraction, summarization, aur verification modes ke beech explicit selection require kare", "c": false}], "e": "Generic `analyze_document` free-text instructions ke saath ambiguous aur inconsistent outputs deta hai. Specialized tools me split karna defined input/output contracts ke saath ambiguity completely eliminate karta hai, ensure karte hue ki agent hamesha correct output format receive kare. Baaki: A) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | C) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte. | D) Sab kuch ek path me collapse karna precision kam karta hai aur usually system ko control karna zyada mushkil banata hai, aasan nahi."}, "c32": {"q": "Coordinator agent ke paas saare char specialized subagents ke liye AgentFunctions configured hain, har ek appropriate descriptions aur restrictions ke saath. Testing ke dauran, tum paate ho ki coordinator kabhi-kabhi delegate karne me fail ho jaata hai — woh likhta hai \"I'll ask the web search agent to find sources\" bina actually usko invoke kiye.\n\nSabse likely cause kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "AgentFunctions correctly configured hain, lekin coordinator ke system prompt me ek statement hai jo use available subagent types jaanne se rokta hai", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Coordinator ki allowedTools configuration me \"Task\" include nahi hai, isliye woh delegation describe toh kar sakta hai lekin actually us tool ko invoke nahi kar sakta jo subagents spawn karne ke liye zaroori hai", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Coordinator ki max_tokens setting bohot low hai, jisse Task tool invocation truncate ho jaata hai subagent parameter specify hone se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Coordinator se subagent context limit descriptions kaafi context nahi deti; tumhe coordinator aur tool descriptions ke beech explicit context content configure karna hoga", "c": false}], "e": "Coordinator delegation describe kar sakta hai (text generate karke), lekin actually subagents invoke nahi kar sakta kyunki 'Task' tool allowed tools configuration me nahi hai. Ye multi-agent setup me ek common configuration error hai. Baaki: A) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | C) Ye coordination boundary ko clearer nahi banata, isliye workflow phir bhi fragile ya inefficient rahega. | D) Ye coordination boundary ko clearer nahi banata, isliye workflow phir bhi fragile ya inefficient rahega."}, "c33": {"q": "\"Renewable energy adoption\" research karte waqt, web search agent recent statistics return karta hai (2024: 35% adoption) jabki document analysis agent internal reports se data extract karta hai (2022: 18% adoption). Synthesis agent galti se inhe contradictory sources flag kar deta hai, ye recognize karne ki jagah ki data time ke saath growth dikhata hai.\n\nKaunsa change synthesis agent ko aise temporal differences correctly interpret karne me sabse acche se enable karega?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Web search agent ko configure karo ki woh sirf pichle 6 mahino ke results return kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Synthesis agent ko instruct karo ki woh hamesha sabse recent data ko authoritative treat kare aur older findings ko ek separate historical appendix me rakhe", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Subagents ko require karo ki woh apne structured outputs me publication ya data collection dates include karein", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Ek conflict resolution agent add karo jo automatically older data discard kare jab same metric ke liye newer data available ho", "c": false}], "e": "Synthesis agent data ko misread karta hai kyunki use kabhi dates dikhti hi nahi. Har data point ko structured output me apna khud ka timestamp carry karwana synthesis ko trends ke baare me reason karne deta hai, contradictions ki jagah."}, "c34": {"q": "Tumhara multi-agent research pipeline 28 me se 12 documents process karne ke baad crash ho gaya. Web search agent ne relevant sources identify kar liye the, document analysis agent ne partially extraction complete kar liya tha, aur synthesizer ne pattern identification shuru kar diya tha. Tumhe processing resume karna hai bina kaam repeat kiye ya prior findings ki fidelity khoye.\n\nAgent state restore karte waqt kaunsa state management approach information fidelity aur context efficiency ke beech sabse acha balance karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Har agent ek structured report ek known location me persist kare. Resume karte waqt, coordinator reports load kare aur relevant state agent prompts me inject kare", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Har agent apna khud ka persistent state file maintain kare aur har session ki shuruat me independently reload kare", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Saare agent outputs ek shared vector store me index karo. Resume karte waqt, har agent semantic search use karke store query kare relevant prior findings retrieve karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Coordinator ka conversation log persist karo jisme saari task delegations aur responses ho, ise resume karte waqt agents ko provide karo", "c": false}], "e": "Structured reports known locations me persist hote hain, jisse coordinator resume karte waqt state load karke agent prompts me inject kar sakta hai. Ye raw conversation logs (bohot verbose) ya vector stores (zaroorat se zyada complicated) se zyada efficient hai. Baaki: B) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | C) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | D) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai."}, "c36": {"q": "Coordinator web search subagent ko detailed step-by-step instructions deta hai, exact search queries, source quality criteria (coverage breadth, source diversity), aur content type classifications specify karte hue. Coordinator kabhi-kabhi challenges face karta hai jaha instructions fail ho jaate hain jab subagent unexpected situations encounter karta hai.\n\nSubagent adaptability improve karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek task classification step implement karo jaha coordinator requests ko \"analytical\" vs \"exploratory\" categorize kare aur har category ke liye alag instruction sets use kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Detailed instructions me explicit fallback directives add karo: \"agar specified searches fail ho, alternative queries try karo failure report karne se pehle\"", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Procedural detail ko completely remove kar do, simple goals ke saath delegate karo jaise \"research it thoroughly\" aur subagent ki general capabilities pe rely karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Research goals aur quality criteria (coverage breadth, source diversity, content type) specify karo procedural instructions ki jagah, subagent ko execution decide karne do", "c": true}], "e": "Step-by-step instructions bohot rigid hain, jisse subagent unexpected situations encounter karte waqt adapt nahi kar paata. Goals aur quality criteria specify karna subagent ko unforeseen situations handle karne ke liye judgment use karne deta hai. Baaki: A) Ye coordination boundary ko clearer nahi banata, isliye workflow phir bhi fragile ya inefficient rahega. | B) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | C) Ye coordination boundary ko clearer nahi banata, isliye workflow phir bhi fragile ya inefficient rahega."}, "c37": {"q": "Ek user apne research system ko single web search agent se aage expand kar raha hai specialized data sources add karke. Woh ek financial API agent add karta hai jo structured JSON return karta hai (revenue, margins, growth rates); ek news monitoring agent jo recent developments ke prose summaries return karta hai; aur ek patent analysis agent jo technology areas ki structured lists return karta hai. Synthesis agent inhe executive briefings me combine karta hai. Currently, ye sab kuch bullet points me convert kar deta hai, jisse financial comparisons apni tabular clarity kho dete hain aur news summaries apna narrative flow kho dete hain.\n\nKaunsa change briefing quality ko sabse zyada improve karega?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Subagents aur synthesis ke beech ek format conversion layer add karo jo saare outputs ko ek common intermediate representation me transform kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Saare subagent outputs ko JSON me standardize karo claim, evidence, source, aur confidence ke fields ke saath", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Saare subagent outputs ko prose summaries me standardize karo inline citations ke saath", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Synthesis agent ko update karo taaki woh har content type ko appropriately render kare — financial data ko tables ke roop me, news ko prose ke roop me", "c": true}], "e": "Problem ye hai ki synthesis agent sab kuch bullet points me convert kar deta hai. Sabse direct solution hai synthesis agent ko update karna taaki woh har content type ko properly render kare: financial data → tables, news → prose. Layers add karne ya outputs standardize karne ki zaroorat nahi. Baaki: A) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | B) Ye phir bhi fragile text-generation behavior pe rely karta hai, structure ko zyada reliable tarike se enforce karne ki bajaye. | C) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai."}, "c38": {"q": "Web search agent ne ek research topic ke liye kai relevant sources gather kar liye hain. Document analysis agent ko ab in sources ko examine karna hai.\n\nIn do specialized subagents ke beech typically information kaise flow karti hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Web search agent directly document analysis agent ko invoke karta hai, discovered sources ko parameters ke roop me pass karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Dono agents ek shared memory store access karte hain jaha web search agent findings likhta hai aur document analysis agent unhe padhta hai", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Agents ek event-driven message queue ke through communicate karte hain, document analysis agent web search completion events subscribe karta hai", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Coordinator agent web search agent ka output receive karta hai aur relevant findings ko prompt me include karta hai jab document analysis agent ko invoke karta hai", "c": true}], "e": "Coordinator wali multi-agent architecture me, information coordinator ke through flow karti hai: web search agent output coordinator ko return karta hai, coordinator relevant findings ko prompt me include karta hai jab document analysis agent invoke karta hai. Subagents aapas me directly communicate nahi karte. Baaki: A) Ye coordination boundary ko clearer nahi banata, isliye workflow phir bhi fragile ya inefficient rahega. | B) Ye infrastructure add karta hai lekin question me describe kiya gaya failure mode directly solve nahi karta. | C) Ye infrastructure ya indirection add karta hai, lekin sawaal actually ek simpler coordination pattern choose karne ke baare me hai jo current workflow fit kare."}, "c39": {"q": "Web search agent aur document analysis agent apne tasks complete karne ke baad, coordinator synthesis agent ko invoke karta hai. Lekin, synthesis agent respond karta hai ki woh task complete nahi kar sakta kyunki koi research findings provide nahi ki gayi.\n\nIs issue ka sabse likely cause kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Synthesis agent ko tools chahiye jo directly doosre agents ki conversation histories se results fetch kar sakein", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Synthesis agent ka context window itna bada nahi hai ki dono pichle agents ke combined outputs hold kar sake", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Coordinator ne pichle agents ke outputs synthesis agent ke prompt me include nahi kiye", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Subagents ko ek single API connection share karna hai taaki invocations ke beech automatic context sharing enable ho", "c": false}], "e": "Subagents automatically context share nahi karte. Coordinator ko proactively pichle agents ke outputs prompt me include karna hota hai jab synthesis agent invoke kare. Ye multi-agent orchestration me sabse common error hai. Baaki: A) Ye coordination boundary ko clearer nahi banata, isliye workflow phir bhi fragile ya inefficient rahega. | B) Ye coordination boundary ko clearer nahi banata, isliye workflow phir bhi fragile ya inefficient rahega. | D) Ye coordination boundary ko clearer nahi banata, isliye workflow phir bhi fragile ya inefficient rahega."}, "c40": {"q": "Production me, final reports me aksar bina proper source attribution ke claims hote hain. Investigation dikhati hai ki jabki web search aur document analysis agents apne outputs me correctly citations attach karte hain, synthesis agent findings combine karte waqt track kho deta hai ki konsi sources konse conclusions support karti hain.\n\nSabse effective architectural change kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Saare subagent interactions ki complete transcripts maintain karo aur ek citation-resolution agent add karo jo logs analyze karke report generation se pehle attributions determine kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Coordinator ko har handoff se pehle text me source identifier prefixes inject karwao, phir report generation ke waqt in prefixes ko parse karke citations reconstruct karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek verification step add karo jaha report generator semantic similarity matching use kare original sources ke against ye determine karne ke liye ki konse claims konse documents se aaye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Saare subagents ko structured claim-source mappings output karne require karo jise synthesis agent multiple sources se findings combine karte waqt preserve aur merge karna zaroori ho", "c": true}], "e": "Failure synthesis stage pe information loss hai, isliye fix hai attribution ko structured data ke roop me end-to-end carry karna: subagents explicit claim-source mappings emit karte hain aur synthesis agent unhe preserve aur merge karna zaroori hai. Ye Anthropic ki multi-agent best practice se match karta hai — structured outputs, fragile text-prefix conventions (A), costly post-hoc log analysis (B), ya unreliable semantic-similarity reconstruction (D) ki jagah. Baaki: A) Poora transcript dump karna noise add karta hai aur agle actor ke liye key facts jaldi dhoondhna mushkil banata hai. | B) Ye phir bhi fragile text-generation behavior pe rely karta hai, structure ko zyada reliable tarike se enforce karne ki bajaye."}, "c41": {"q": "Production monitoring dikhati hai ki follow-up queries jaise \"market trends ke baare me humne kya seekha summarize karo\" consistently 40+ seconds lete hain. Investigation reveal karti hai ki coordinator har summarization request ke liye synthesis subagent spawn karta hai, 80K+ tokens accumulated findings pass karte hue. Coordinator ke paas already ye findings uske context me hain research orchestrate karne se.\n\nIn follow-up summaries ke liye response time improve karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Multiple granularities pe summaries pre-generate aur cache karo jab bhi naye findings accumulate hon", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Synthesis subagent ko reduced context ke saath spawn karo aur use coordinator se specific findings on-demand request karne do", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Synthesis subagent pe prompt caching enable karo taaki same research findings baar-baar transfer karne ka overhead kam ho", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Coordinator ko straightforward summarization requests directly handle karwao apne existing context use karke, subagent spawning ko complex analysis ke liye reserve karte hue", "c": true}], "e": "Coordinator ke paas already findings hain uske context me orchestration process se. Sirf summarize karne ke liye synthesis subagent spawn karna overkill hai (80K+ token transfer overhead). Ye simply sabse efficient tareeka hai coordinator ke liye khud summary requests handle karne ka. Baaki: A) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | B) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | C) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c42": {"q": "Web search agent 25 sources dhoondhne (120K tokens raw content) ke baad, document analysis agent key insights extract karta hai (15K tokens), aur synthesis agent ek coherent narrative draft produce karta hai (3K tokens), coordinator ko report generation agent ko context pass karna hai final output ke liye proper source citations ke saath.\n\nKaunsa context-passing strategy completeness aur efficiency ka sabse acha balance deta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Sirf synthesis draft pass karo aur ek separate post-processing pipeline chalao jo claims ko sources se match kare aur citations insert kare report generate hone ke baad", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Saare pichle stages ka ek condensed summary pass karo jo main findings preserve kare aur unhe sources ko sirf naam se attribute kare", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Synthesis draft pass karo ek structured source index ke saath jo key claims ko unke source URLs aur relevant excerpts se map kare", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Saare pichle agents ka full accumulated context pass karo", "c": false}], "e": "Synthesis draft (3K tokens) + source index mapping claims to URLs/excerpts pass karna report generator ke liye kaafi information deta hai bina poore 150K+ tokens raw content transfer kiye. Source index accurate citations ensure karta hai. Baaki: A) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | B) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | D) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai."}, "c43": {"q": "Multiple precedents cite karne wale complex legal cases analyze karte waqt, document analysis subagent har ek ko sequentially process karta hai. Ek landmark case jo 12 precedents cite karta hai completely analyze karne me 3 minutes se zyada leta hai.\n\nCoordinator ki system monitor aur debug karne ki ability preserve karte hue is latency ko kam karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Document analysis subagent ko apne khud ke specialized subagents dynamically spawn karne enable karo jab woh bohot saari citations wale cases encounter kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek recursive agent hierarchy banao jaha analysis agents kaam ko child agents me subdivide karein jab tak single-precedent granularity tak na pahunch jaayein", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Coordinator ko parallel document analysis subagents spawn karwao, har ek precedents ka ek subset handle kare, phir synthesis se pehle results aggregate karo", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Ek message queue implement karo jaha precedent analysis tasks asynchronously worker agents ke ek pool ke through process ho", "c": false}], "e": "Anthropic ka recommended multi-agent design orchestrator-worker pattern hai ek flat hierarchy ke saath: coordinator khud parallel subagents spawn karta hai aur unke results aggregate karta hai, jo parallelism ke through latency kam karta hai jabki saare spawning, monitoring, aur debugging ko ek hi jagah centralized rakhta hai. Options B aur C nested/recursive agent hierarchies banate hain jo observability aur debuggability ko severely degrade kar dete hain, aur D asynchronous queue infrastructure introduce karta hai jo kaam ko coordinator ki direct visibility se decouple kar deta hai. Baaki: A) Isse coordination overhead badhta hai aur justified nahi hai jab tak kaam clearly independent subtasks me separable na ho. | B) Ye coordination boundary ko clearer nahi banata, isliye workflow phir bhi fragile ya inefficient rahega. | D) Ye coordination boundary ko clearer nahi banata, isliye workflow phir bhi fragile ya inefficient rahega."}, "c44": {"q": "Production me, tum complex queries ko specialized subagents me distribute kar rahe ho. Query distribution uneven hai aur evolve ho raha hai jaise-jaise users nayi applications discover karte hain.\n\nQuery complexity ke liye optimize karne ka sabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Pattern-based routing implement karo jo queries ko factual vs analytical patterns ke basis pe categorize kare aur har ek ko ek predefined subagent combination se map kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Coordinator ko har query dynamically analyze karwao aur query ki complexity aur routing characteristics ke basis pe selectively subagents route karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Factual questions ke liye ek fast-track path banao jo subagents ko completely bypass kare, sirf analytical queries ko complete pipeline se route karte hue", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Labeled historical data ke basis pe ek query complexity classifier train karo optimal subagent combination predict karne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "Distribution queries ke liye jo mostly factual/simple hain, ek fast-track path banao jo simple factual questions ke liye subagents bypass kare, sirf analytical queries ko full pipeline se route karte hue. Ye method majority queries ke liye latency aur cost kam karta hai. Baaki: A) Ye coordination boundary ko clearer nahi banata, isliye workflow phir bhi fragile ya inefficient rahega. | B) Isse coordination overhead badhta hai aur justified nahi hai jab tak kaam clearly independent subtasks me separable na ho. | D) Ye coordination boundary ko clearer nahi banata, isliye workflow phir bhi fragile ya inefficient rahega."}, "c45": {"q": "Synthesis agent web search aur document analysis agents se summarized findings receive karta hai, phir report generator ko ek consolidated summary pass karta hai. Testing ke dauran, tumhe pata chalta hai ki generated reports bina proper citations ke factual claims karte hain — report generator statements ko unke original sources se attribute nahi kar sakta kyunki wo metadata summarization steps ke dauran kho gaya tha.\n\nFinal reports me proper source attribution ensure karne ka sabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Har agent ko structured data output karwao jo content summaries ko source metadata (URLs, document names, page numbers) se alag rakhe", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Summarization skip karo aur web search aur document analysis se full raw outputs directly report generator ko pass karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Synthesis agent ko instruct karo ki woh source references ko apne summary text ke andar inline embed kare ek consistent citation format use karke", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Report generator ko web search agent query karwao final report me claims ke liye sources re-locate karne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "Loss ke baad attribution fix karne ki bajaye, har agent ko structured data output karna chahiye separate content summaries aur source metadata (URLs, document names, page numbers) ke saath. Ye ensure karta hai ki metadata summarization steps ke through kho na jaaye."}, "c54": {"q": "Jab agent `lookup_order` call karta hai aur order details receive karta hai jo dikhata hai ki item 45 din pehle purchase hua tha, agentic loop kaise determine karta hai ki agla `process_refund` call karna hai ya `escalate_to_human`?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Order details conversation me add ho jaate hain aur model reason karta hai ki kaunsa action lena hai", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Agent ek pre-configured decision tree follow karta hai jo order attributes ko specific tool calls se map karta hai", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Agent request ki shuruat me planned ek tool sequence ke baaki steps execute karta hai", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Orchestration layer automatically order ke status field ke basis pe agle tool ko route karta hai", "c": false}], "e": "Claude ke agentic loop me, tool result return karne ke baad, order details conversation context me add ho jaate hain aur model us information ke basis pe agle action ke baare me reason karta hai. Koi hardcoded decision tree ya orchestration layer nahi hai jo automatically route kare."}, "c63": {"q": "Coordinator agent ke paas saare char specialized subagents ke liye AgentDefinitions configured hain, har ek appropriate descriptions, prompts, aur tool restrictions ke saath. Testing ke dauran, tum notice karte ho ki coordinator correctly reason karta hai ki kab delegate karna hai — woh messages generate karta hai jaise \"I'll ask the web search agent to find sources on this topic\" — lekin koi subagent execution kabhi hota hi nahi. Coordinator phir waise proceed karta hai jaise delegation ho gaya ho aur incomplete information ke saath continue karta hai. Logs koi errors nahi dikhate.\n\nSabse likely cause kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "AgentDefinitions correctly configured hain, lekin coordinator ka system prompt explicitly available subagent types list nahi karta, jisse model unhe invoke kar sakta hai ye jaanne se rukta hai", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Coordinator ki allowedTools configuration me \"Task\" include nahi hai, isliye woh delegation ke baare me reason toh kar sakta hai lekin us tool ko invoke nahi kar sakta jo subagents spawn karne ke liye zaroori hai", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Coordinator ki max_tokens setting bohot low hai, jisse Task tool invocation truncate ho jaata hai subagent type parameter specify hone se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Subagent context isolation ka matlab hai ki coordinator se task descriptions automatically subagents tak nahi pahunchte; tumhe ClaudeAgentOptions me explicit context forwarding configure karna hoga", "c": false}], "e": "AllowedTools me Task tool ke bina, coordinator delegate karne ke baare me baat kar sakta hai lekin actually subagent call karne ka koi tareeka nahi hai — bilkul 'reasons about it, no execution, no errors' symptom ke jaisa. Baaki: A) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | C) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | D) Ye coordination boundary ko clearer nahi banata, isliye workflow phir bhi fragile ya inefficient rahega."}, "c64": {"q": "Production me, tum observe karte ho ki simple fact-checking queries (jaise \"Paris Climate Agreement kis saal sign hua tha?\") saare char subagents ko sequentially traverse karti hain, 40+ seconds aur significant tokens consume karte hue per query. Complex comparative research full pipeline se benefit leti hai. Tumhari query distribution diverse hai aur evolve ho rahi hai jaise-jaise users nayi applications discover karte hain.\n\nVarying query complexity ke liye optimize karne ka sabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Labeled historical data pe ek query complexity classifier train karo optimal subagent combinations predict karne ke liye, periodically retrain karte hue jaise-jaise query patterns evolve hon", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Pattern-based routing implement karo jo queries ko structure ke basis pe categorize kare (single-fact vs comparative vs analytical) aur har category ko ek predefined subagent combination se map kare", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Factual questions ke liye ek fast-path banao jo subagents ko completely bypass kare, baaki saari queries ko complete pipeline se route karte hue research thoroughness ensure karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Coordinator ko har query analyze karwao aur dynamically decide karwao ki kaunse subagents invoke karne hain uski query requirements ki assessment ke basis pe", "c": true}], "e": "LLM coordinator ko independently har query ke baare me reason karne do aur sirf woh subagents select karne do jo truly zaroori hain — ye approach diverse aur evolving query distributions ke liye naturally adapt karta hai. Baaki: A) Ye coordination boundary ko clearer nahi banata, isliye workflow phir bhi fragile ya inefficient rahega. | B) Ye coordination boundary ko clearer nahi banata, isliye workflow phir bhi fragile ya inefficient rahega. | C) Ye coordination boundary ko clearer nahi banata, isliye workflow phir bhi fragile ya inefficient rahega."}, "c66": {"q": "Users report karte hain ki final reports me kabhi-kabhi specific subtopics pe depth ki kami hoti hai. Investigation dikhati hai ki document analysis agent aksar gaps identify karta hai — jaise, note karte hue \"retrieved sources API authentication discuss karte hain lekin token refresh patterns pe details ki kami hai\" — lekin current strict pipeline ke under, ye insight actionable nahi hai kyunki search already complete ho chuka hai.\n\nSabse effective architectural change kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Search phase se pehle ek research planning agent add karo jo topics ko specific sub-questions me decompose kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Coordinator ko analysis output review karwao gap indicators ke liye aur gap-informed queries ke saath search ko re-invoke karo jab gaps detect hon", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Synthesis agent ko har section me confidence scores attach karwao aur insufficient coverage wale areas ko manual review ke liye flag karwao", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Analysis agent ko specific gaps coordinator ko report karwao, jo targeted searches trigger kare aur analysis ko re-invoke kare jab tak sufficient na ho jaaye", "c": true}], "e": "Core problem ek rigid one-way pipeline hai jaha gap insights search khatam hone ke baad aati hain. Sabse acha fix ek closed feedback loop hai: analysis agent specific gaps ko structured output ke roop me report karta hai, coordinator targeted follow-up searches launch karta hai, aur analysis dobara chalta hai jab tak coverage sufficient na ho. Isse missing-information signal actionable ban jaata hai, ek passive observation ki jagah. Baaki: C) Ye problem ko defer karta hai us system behavior ko solve karne ki bajaye jisne ise cause kiya."}, "c106": {"q": "Production monitoring dikhati hai ki research phase expected se zyada time leta hai. Analysis reveal karti hai ki coordinator web search subagent invoke karta hai, phir document analysis subagent invoke karta hai aur dobara wait karta hai. Ye tasks independent hain — inme se koi bhi doosre ke output pe depend nahi karta.\n\nIn subagents ko concurrently chalane ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Dono subagents ko Sonnet ki jagah Haiku-tier model use karne switch karo unka individual execution time kam karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Agent ke bahar ek async orchestration layer banao jo parallel threads spawn kare, har ek alag coordinator chalate hue", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Coordinator ke system prompt me detailed instructions add karo jo parallel execution ke performance benefits ek saath explain karein", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Coordinator ko structure karo taaki woh dono Task tool calls (web search aur document analysis ke liye) ek hi response message me emit kare", "c": true}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai coordinator ko structure karna taaki woh dono Task tool calls (web search aur document analysis ke liye) ek hi response message me emit kare. Ye described coordination problem ko fit karta hai aur responsibilities, delegation, ya handoff behavior ko zyada reliable banata hai. Baaki: A) Isse coordination overhead badhta hai aur justified nahi hai jab tak kaam clearly independent subtasks me separable na ho. | B) Isse coordination overhead badhta hai aur justified nahi hai jab tak kaam clearly independent subtasks me separable na ho. | C) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c111": {"q": "Synthesis agent apna initial pass complete karta hai lekin flag karta hai ki teen key research questions unanswered rehte hain kyunki web search aur document analysis agents ne un specific subtopics pe relevant information nahi dhoondhi. Coordinator currently directly report generation pe proceed karta hai, incomplete coverage wali reports produce karte hue.\n\nKaunsa change research completeness ko sabse effectively improve karega?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Web search aur document analysis ko bheji jaane wali queries ki initial breadth badhao relevant information miss hone ki probability kam karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Coordinator ko synthesis output ko gaps ke liye evaluate karwao, phir web search aur document analysis ko targeted queries ke saath re-delegate karwao synthesis ko dobara invoke karne se pehle", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Report generation agent ko note karwao ki konse research questions answer nahi ho paye, taaki users final output ki limitations samajh sakein", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Synthesis agent ko web search tools tak direct access do taaki woh autonomously knowledge gaps fill kar sake bina control coordinator ko wapas kiye", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai coordinator ko synthesis output ko gaps ke liye evaluate karwana, phir web search aur document analysis ko targeted queries ke saath re-delegate karwana synthesis ko dobara invoke karne se pehle. Ye described coordination problem ko fit karta hai aur responsibilities, delegation, ya handoff behavior ko zyada reliable banata hai. Baaki: A) Ye coordination boundary ko clearer nahi banata, isliye workflow phir bhi fragile ya inefficient rahega. | C) Ye coordination boundary ko clearer nahi banata, isliye workflow phir bhi fragile ya inefficient rahega. | D) Ye coordination boundary ko clearer nahi banata, isliye workflow phir bhi fragile ya inefficient rahega."}, "c119": {"q": "Tumne system ko configure kiya hai taaki saare char subagents ke paas complete set of 18 tools tak access ho. Testing ke dauran, agents aksar apni specialization ke bahar tools call karte hain — synthesis agent web searches attempt karta hai, aur report generator documents analyze karne ki koshish karta hai.\n\nIs poor tool selection behavior ka primary cause kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "18 tools me se choose karna, 4-5 relevant tools ki jagah, decision complexity ko reliable selection thresholds se zyada badha deta hai", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Coordinator track nahi kar sakta ki har subagent ke paas kaunsi capabilities hain, jisse tasks misroute ho jaate hain", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Tool definitions bohot zyada context window space consume karte hain, task content ke liye insufficient room chhodte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Agents ke system prompts me role descriptions us role ke bahar tools tak access hone se conflict karte hain", "c": false}], "e": "18 tools me se choose karna, 4-5 relevant tools ki jagah, decision complexity ko reliable selection thresholds se zyada badha deta hai. Ye tool-selection mistakes kam karta hai decision surface ko clearer aur agent ke task ke saath zyada aligned banake. Baaki: B) Ye us ambiguity ko kam nahi karta jo agent ko galat tool choose karne ki wajah bani. | C) Ye us ambiguity ko kam nahi karta jo agent ko galat tool choose karne ki wajah bani. | D) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c130": {"q": "Web search aur document analysis subagents apne tasks complete karne ke baad, coordinator ko synthesis subagent spawn karna hai findings ko synthesize karne ke liye.\n\nSynthesis subagent ko jo information chahiye woh provide karne ka correct approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Subagent ko tool definitions do jo use callbacks ke through doosre subagents se outputs request karne dein", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Reference identifiers pass karo aur subagent ko ek shared memory store tak read access ke saath configure karo jaha doosre subagents ne apne results deposit kiye", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Subagent ko sirf ek brief task description ke saath spawn karo, coordinator se automatic context inheritance pe rely karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Dono subagents ki complete findings directly synthesis subagent ke prompt me include karo", "c": false}], "e": "Anthropic ki multi-agent best practice hai ki subagents apne full outputs artifacts ke roop me external/shared storage me deposit karein aur lightweight references pass karein, taaki synthesis subagent prior results ko directly padhe lossy ya token-heavy copies receive karne ki jagah prompts ke through. Subagents ke beech callbacks (A) aur automatic context inheritance (D) is architecture me exist nahi karte, aur complete findings ko prompt me inline karna (B) context bloat karta hai aur information loss ka risk leta hai. Baaki: A) Isse coordination overhead badhta hai aur justified nahi hai jab tak kaam clearly independent subtasks me separable na ho. | C) Ye coordination boundary ko clearer nahi banata, isliye workflow phir bhi fragile ya inefficient rahega. | D) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c154": {"q": "Automated review pipeline ki initial testing ke dauran, tum notice karte ho ki bade PRs (50+ changed files) pe reviews kabhi-kabhi 20 minutes se zyada lete hain aur $8-12 per run cost karte hain extensive agentic loops ki wajah se — Claude files padhta hai, analysis tools chalata hai, aur kai baar iterate karta hai. Tumhari team chahti hai ki har invocation ek fixed iteration count aur ek fixed dollar amount pe abort ho, Claude Code khud se enforce kiya hua, surrounding job runner se nahi.\n\nKaunsa configuration change directly in dono per-invocation caps ko enforce karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "`--model` flag ko ek smaller, cheaper model pe switch karo taaki har iteration kam tokens aur lower per-call cost use kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "`--permission-mode dontAsk` set karo taaki explicitly allowed set me na hone wali koi bhi tool permission requests auto-deny ho jaayein", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "`claude -p` invocation me `--max-turns 10 --max-budget-usd 2.00` add karo iterations aur spend cap karne ke liye", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "GitHub Actions job step pe `timeout-minutes: 5` set karo aur per-run costs Anthropic Console usage dashboard ke through monitor karo", "c": false}], "e": "Required controls Claude Code ke khud ke andar native per-invocation limits hain: ek jo agentic turns ki sankhya cap kare aur ek jo us run ke liye dollar spend cap kare. In built-in runtime limits ka use karna oversized reviews rokne ka direct tareeka hai bina external job settings pe depend kiye ya indirect cost reductions pe. Baaki: B) Ye phir bhi critical decision model discretion pe chhod deta hai, jo exactly wahi hai jo scenario keh raha hai fail ho raha hai."}, "c8": {"q": "Ek MCP server add karne ke baad specialized code refactoring tools ke saath (`extract_function`, `rename_variable`, `inline_function`), tum notice karte ho ki agent abhi bhi refactoring tasks ke liye basic text manipulation use karta hai `Write` aur `Bash sed` commands ke through. MCP server connected hai aur kaam kar raha hai. Configuration examine karte waqt, tumhe pata chalta hai ki har MCP tool ki description minimal hai jaise \"extract_function: extracts a function from code.\"\n\nMCP refactoring tools ki adoption improve karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ise expected behavior ke roop me accept karo kyunki sed jaise simpler tools specialized refactoring tools se zyada predictable hain", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "MCP tool descriptions ko enhance karo taaki woh explain karein ki har tool kab text manipulation se better hai, aur expected inputs aur outputs clarify karo", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek request classifier implement karo jo refactoring intent detect kare aur un requests ko automatically MCP server pe route kare agent process karne se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Refactoring sessions ke liye agent ki configuration se `Write` tool remove karo taaki use code modifications ke liye MCP tools use karne hi pade", "c": false}], "e": "Tool selection un descriptions se driven hoti hai jo Claude dekhta hai. Jab MCP tools kehte hain 'extracts a function from code' aur Write/sed rich documentation ke saath aate hain, Claude Write/sed choose kar leta hai. Descriptions ko strengthen karo. Baaki: A) Behavior ko acceptable treat karna adoption problem ko unsolved chhod deta hai, agent ki decision-making improve karne ki bajaye. | C) Ye phir bhi critical decision model discretion pe chhod deta hai, jo exactly wahi hai jo scenario keh raha hai fail ho raha hai. | D) Alternatives remove karke tool use force karna behavior badal sakta hai, lekin real issue solve nahi karta agent ko samajhne me madad karna ki specialized tool kab appropriate hai."}, "c14": {"q": "Ek engineer jo abhi team me join hua hai, agent se pooch raha hai ki authentication aur authorization architecture samajhne me madad kare security improvements karne se pehle. Codebase me multiple services ke across 800+ files hain.\n\nKaunsa exploration strategy sabse effectively understanding build karega, Claude ke built-in tools aur context limits ko dekhte hue?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Pehle koi bhi CLAUDE.md aur README files padho, phir engineer se poocho ki auth system samajhne ke liye kaunsi 10-15 files sabse important hain", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Saari files padho jinke content ya filename me \"auth\", \"login\", \"permission\", ya \"token\" ho", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Parallel subagents launch karo alag-alag services simultaneously explore karne ke liye, phir unki findings ko ek architectural overview me synthesize karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Grep use karo authentication entry points dhoondhne ke liye, un files ko padho, phir imports aur function calls follow karo auth flow ko incrementally map karne ke liye", "c": true}], "e": "800+ files wale codebase ke saath, entry points se aur imports ke through incremental exploration structured understanding build karne ka sabse effective tareeka hai bina context se overwhelm hue. Saari related files padhna (B) bohot zyada context consume karega. Baaki: A) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | B) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | C) Isse coordination overhead badhta hai aur justified nahi hai jab tak kaam clearly independent subtasks me separable na ho."}, "c15": {"q": "Code analysis tools provide karne wale ek local MCP server integrate karne ke baad (`analyze_dependencies`, `find_dead_code`, `calculate_complexity`), tum notice karte ho ki agent abhi bhi Grep use karta hai dependencies inspect karne ke liye, chahe users explicitly \"code dependencies\" ke baare me pooch rahe hon. Tool definitions dikhati hain: `analyze_dependencies` imports analyze karke ek dependency graph return karta hai.\n\nAgent ki MCP tools selection improve karne ka sabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "`analyze_dependencies` ko granular tools me split karo: `list_imports`, `detect_transitive_deps`, `identify_circular_deps` — Grep ke saath overlap avoid karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "System prompt me routing questions add karo jo specify karein ki dependency-related questions ko Grep ki jagah MCP tools use karne chahiye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "MCP tool descriptions aur outputs ko expand karo — jaise \"Builds dependency graph with list_imports, direct_circular_deps\" — dependencies aur cycle analysis ko Grep se clearly distinguish karne ke liye", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Grep ko available tools se remove karo functional overlap eliminate karne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "Agents MCP tools use nahi karte kyunki tool descriptions itni detailed nahi hain ki Grep ke against kab use karna hai distinguish kar sakein. Descriptions ko specific output examples ke saath expand karo agents ko sahi tool samajhne aur choose karne me madad ke liye. Baaki: A) Surface-level searching yahan bohot narrow hai kyunki task ko simple text matching se zyada rich structural understanding chahiye. | B) Surface-level searching yahan bohot narrow hai kyunki task ko simple text matching se zyada rich structural understanding chahiye. | D) Surface-level searching yahan bohot narrow hai kyunki task ko simple text matching se zyada rich structural understanding chahiye."}, "c46": {"q": "Apna `lookup_order` MCP tool implement karte waqt, backend kabhi-kabhi errors return karta hai (jaise \"Order not found\" ya temporary database failures).\n\nIn errors ko agent ko wapas communicate karne ka correct pattern kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Tool handler se ek exception throw karo taaki agent framework use catch karke log kar sake", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Server-side error log karo aur ek empty result return karo model ko confuse hone se bachane ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Error message ko tool result content me return karo `isError` flag ko `true` set karke", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Ek success response return karo ek \"status\" field ke saath jo error type indicate kare", "c": false}], "e": "MCP ka designed pattern: error text ko content field me daalo aur `isError=true` mark karo. Claude ko dono milte hain — failure flag aur ek readable message reason karne ke liye. Baaki: A) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | B) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | D) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga."}, "c53": {"q": "Production logs dikhate hain inconsistent error responses jab `lookup_order` fail hota hai. Agent kabhi-kabhi retry karta hai (3-4 turns waste karte hue) error pe conclude karne se pehle. Tumhara MCP tool currently sirf ek plain text error message Claude ko return karta hai.\n\nSabse effective improvement kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek `analyze_error` MCP tool banao jise agent call kare error type determine karne ke liye ye decide karne se pehle ki kaise handle karna hai", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Apne MCP server me saare errors ke liye exponential backoff ke saath retry logic implement karo, sirf successful results agent ko return karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Structured error responses return karo `retryable: false` ke saath business errors ke liye aur Claude use karne ke liye ek customer-friendly explanation", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "System prompt me few-shot examples add karo jo dikhaye ki retryable ko non-retryable errors se error message text parse karke kaise distinguish karein", "c": false}], "e": "Jab tool sirf plain text return karta hai, agent transient vs permanent errors distinguish nahi kar sakta. Structured error response `retryable: false` ke saath business errors ke liye agents ko turant pata chal jaata hai ki retry karne ki zaroorat nahi, turns bachate hue aur customer experience improve karte hue. Baaki: A) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | B) Retry sirf tab madad karta hai jab problem transient ho; ye khud se ek design ya classification problem fix nahi karta. | D) Ye galat hai kyunki retry khud se underlying cause resolve nahi karta jab tak failure clearly transient na ho."}, "c65": {"q": "Production logs dikhate hain inconsistent error handling: jab `lookup_order` fail hota hai, agent kabhi-kabhi 5+ baar retry karta hai (wasteful jab order ID exist hi nahi karti), kabhi-kabhi turant escalate karta hai (premature temporary network issues ke liye), aur kabhi-kabhi users se clarification poochta hai (inappropriate jab issue ek backend permission error ho). Investigation dikhati hai ki tumhara MCP tool uniform error responses return karta hai: `{\"isError\": true, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Operation failed\"}]}`. Agent error types ke beech distinguish nahi kar sakta.\n\nSabse effective improvement kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "System prompt me few-shot examples add karo jo dikhaye ki error message patterns ko kaise interpret karein aur har ek ke liye appropriate responses select karein", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Apne MCP server me saare errors ke liye exponential backoff ke saath retry logic implement karo, retries exhaust hone ke baad hi agent ko return karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek `analyze_error` MCP tool banao jise agent kisi bhi failure ke baad call kare error category aur recommended action determine karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Error responses ko structured metadata ke saath enhance karo: `errorCategory` (transient/validation/permission) include karo, ek `isRetryable` boolean, aur ek description ki failure ka cause kya tha", "c": true}], "e": "Agents ko sahi decision lene ke liye zaroori information do: category, retryability, aur human-readable cause. Baaki: A) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte. | B) Retry sirf tab madad karta hai jab problem transient ho; ye khud se ek design ya classification problem fix nahi karta. | C) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga."}, "c70": {"q": "Tumhara `remove_team_member` tool ek `dry_run: boolean` parameter use karta hai impacts preview karne ke liye execution se pehle. Production monitoring dikhati hai ki agent 15% calls me preview step ko bypass kar deta hai `dry_run=false` directly call karke. Tumhe ensure karna hai ki har removal se pehle ek preview ho jo user explicitly confirm kare.\n\nSabse reliable approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Server-side validation add karo jo `dry_run=false` ko sirf tab allow kare jab same parameters wali ek `dry_run=true` call pichhle 60 seconds me hui ho", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Tool description me detailed instructions aur few-shot examples add karo jo require karein ki agent hamesha pehle `dry_run=true` ke saath call kare aur `dry_run=false` ke saath call karne se pehle user confirmation ka wait kare", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Do tools se replace karo: `preview_remove_member` impact details aur ek single-use confirmation token return kare; `execute_remove_member` ko us token ki zaroorat ho, execution ko specific previewed action se bind karte hue", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Tool ko confirmation required ke roop me annotate karo aur orchestration layer configure karo ki woh user se approval maange kisi bhi annotated tool ki call forward karne se pehle", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai Do tools se replace karna: `preview_remove_member` impact details aur ek single-use confirmation token return kare; `execute_remove_member` ko us token ki zaroorat ho, execution ko specific previewed action se bind karte hue. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: B) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte. | D) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c93": {"q": "Production logs dikhate hain inconsistent error handling: jab `tool_code` fail hota hai, agent kabhi-kabhi 5 baar retry karta hai (chahe `tool_id` exist na kare), kabhi-kabhi turant escalate karta hai (premature temporary network issues ke liye), aur kabhi-kabhi user-friendly explanation add karta hai (inappropriate jab issue ek backend permission error ho). Investigation dikhati hai ki chaaron MCP tool uniform error responses return karte hain: `{\"status\": \"error\", \"content\": \"{\"type\": \"Error\", \"message\": \"Operation failed.\"}\"}`.\n\nAgent alag types seekhta hai. Sabse effective improvement kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek `analyze_error` MCP tool banao jise agent kisi bhi failure ke baad call kare error category aur recommended action determine karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Apne MCP server me saare errors ke liye exponential backoff ke saath retry logic implement karo, retries exhaust hone ke baad hi agent ko return karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Error responses ko structured metadata ke saath enhance karo. `error_category` (transient/retriable/permission), `reason`, aur ek description include karo ki failure ka cause kya tha", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "System prompt me few-shot examples add karo jo dikhaye ki error message patterns ko kaise interpret karein aur har ek ke liye appropriate responses select karein", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai Error responses ko structured metadata ke saath enhance karna. `error_category` (transient/retriable/permission), `reason`, aur ek description include karo ki failure ka cause kya tha. Ye agent ko failure ke baare me clearer signals deta hai taaki woh sahi recovery action choose kar sake, blindly retry karne ya bohot jaldi escalate karne ki bajaye. Baaki: A) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | B) Retry sirf tab madad karta hai jab problem transient ho; ye khud se ek design ya classification problem fix nahi karta. | D) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte."}, "c110": {"q": "Tumhara productivity agent teen MCP servers se connect karta hai: ek issue tracker (`search_issues`, `get_issue`, `create_comment`), ek documentation wiki (`search_docs`, `get_page`, `list_spaces`), aur ek database explorer (`run_query`, `get_schema`, `list_databases`). Jab engineers cross-system questions poochte hain jaise \"PROJ-1234 me authentication refactor se kaunse database tables affect hote hain?\", monitoring dikhati hai ki agent 8-10 sequential tool calls karta hai, frequently exploratory calls issue karta hai kyunki use pata nahi hota ki har server me kya content hai, aur complex investigations complete karne se pehle context space exhaust kar deta hai.\n\nKaunsa architectural change MCP capabilities ko leverage karke in issues ko sabse acche se address karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Har server me ek `prepare_investigation` tool add karo jo ek natural language question accept kare aur relevant content summaries return kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Teeno servers ko ek unified MCP server me consolidate karo cross-referencing capabilities ke saath", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek orchestrator add karo jo keywords ke basis pe questions ko ek single server pe route kare", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Har server ke content catalog ko MCP resources ke roop me expose karo — issue summaries, documentation hierarchy, database schemas", "c": true}], "e": "MCP resources exactly is problem ke liye design kiya gaya protocol primitive hai: servers browsable, application-controlled context (issue summaries, doc hierarchies, database schemas) expose karte hain jise agent explore aur padh sakta hai bina exploratory tool-call round trips ke, directly visibility gap aur context exhaustion fix karte hue. A ek monolith rebuild karta hai MCP ke composable design ke against, C sirf zyada tools add karta hai bina MCP capabilities leverage kiye, aur D ka single-server keyword routing inherently cross-system questions break kar deta hai. Baaki: A) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | B) Sab kuch ek path me collapse karna precision kam karta hai aur usually system ko control karna zyada mushkil banata hai, aasan nahi. | C) Surface-level searching yahan bohot narrow hai kyunki task ko simple text matching se zyada rich structural understanding chahiye."}, "c113": {"q": "Tumhare agent ke paas alag-alag external services ke liye 50+ specialized API connectors ka access hai. Jaise-jaise connector library badhi, tool selection accuracy girke 58% ho gayi. Tumne ek `search_connectors(description)` tool design kiya jo matching connectors dhoondta hai, lekin testing me agents frequently search karna skip kar dete hain aur connectors ko directly call karte hain (aksar galat tarike se), ya search filtered results me se galat connectors select karta hai.\n\nDono issues address karne ke liye tool composition pattern kaise design karna chahiye?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek `find_and_execute(description, params)` composite tool design karo jo search kare aur immediately best matching connector execute kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Saare connector descriptions ko detailed usage samples, edge cases, aur input requirements ke saath enhance karo. Few-shot examples add karo jo correct search-then-use workflow dikhaye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "`search_connectors` design karo taaki woh matched connectors ko dynamically agent ke available tools me add kare. Connectors shuru me unavailable hote hain aur discover hone ke baad persist karte hain", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Connectors ko built-in compatibility validation ke saath design karo jo mismatched requests ke liye descriptive errors return kare", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai `search_connectors` design karna taaki woh matched connectors ko dynamically agent ke available tools me add kare. Connectors shuru me unavailable hote hain aur discover hone ke baad persist karte hain. Ye tool-selection mistakes kam karta hai decision surface ko clearer aur agent ke task ke saath zyada aligned banake. Baaki: A) Ye us ambiguity ko kam nahi karta jo agent ko galat tool choose karne ki wajah bani. | B) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte. | D) Ye us ambiguity ko kam nahi karta jo agent ko galat tool choose karne ki wajah bani."}, "c118": {"q": "Tumhare agent me ek `update_game_score` tool hai jo `game_date` (string), `home_team` (string), aur `away_team` (string) parameters accept karta hai. Production logs recurring issues dikhate hain: agent official names ki jagah team nicknames use karta hai, inconsistent date formats apply karta hai, aur jab teams ke pass same season me rematches ho, galat game select kar leta hai.\n\nKaunsa tool interface change in errors ko effectively rok sakta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Tool description me detailed examples add karo jo required date format aur official team names ki complete list dikhaye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Teeno parameters ko ek single `game_id` parameter se replace karo aur ek separate `search_games` lookup tool se jo matching game IDs return kare", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Dono team parameters ke liye valid team names list karte hue enum constraints add karo, aur date parameter ke liye ISO 8601 format enforce karta hua regex pattern add karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Rematches disambiguate karne ke liye ek `season` parameter add karo, aur ek `confirm_before_update` flag add karo jo resolved game details return kare agent ko verify karne ke liye score commit hone se pehle", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai teeno parameters ko ek single `game_id` parameter se replace karna aur ek separate `search_games` lookup tool se jo matching game IDs return kare. Ye agent ko failure ke baare me clearer signals deta hai taaki woh sahi recovery action choose kar sake, blindly retry karne ya bohot jaldi escalate karne ki bajaye. Baaki: A) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte. | C) Surface-level searching yahan bohot narrow hai kyunki task ko simple text matching se zyada rich structural understanding chahiye. | D) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga."}, "c123": {"q": "Tumhara resource allocation tool provisioning request hone ke baad ek simple acknowledgment message return karta hai. Users frequently allocations approve karte hain aur turant poochte hain \"woh kitne ka pada?\" ya \"woh kaunsa project tha?\" — indicate karte hue ki unhone bina samjhe confirm kar diya.\n\nKaunsa tool design change ise sabse effectively address karega?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Execution complete hone se pehle ek 60-second hold implement karo, users ko pending allocations review karne aur zaroorat pade toh cancel karne ka time dete hue", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek `user_acknowledged: boolean` parameter add karo jo `true` set hona zaroori ho, agent ke liye instructions ke saath ki ise sirf tab set kare jab user explicitly confirm kare ki unhone details review ki hain", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek `detail_level` parameter add karo \"minimal\" ya \"comprehensive\" options ke saath jo control kare ki agent confirmations me kitna context present karta hai", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Tool response me structured data return karo jisme cost estimate, target project, resource specifications, aur impact summary shamil ho", "c": true}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai tool response me structured data return karna jisme cost estimate, target project, resource specifications, aur impact summary shamil ho. Ye conclusions aur supporting evidence ke beech link preserve karta hai, jo scenario ki key requirement hai. Baaki: B) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c125": {"q": "Tumhara MCP server ek `check_availability` tool implement karta hai jo ek external calendar API query karta hai. Testing ke dauran, tumhe teen error conditions milte hain: (1) tool ek malformed request ke saath call hota hai, required `user_email` parameter missing ke saath (2) calendar API ek 404 return karta hai kyunki specified user calendar system me exist hi nahi karta (3) calendar API ek 503 return karta hai kyunki service temporarily unavailable hai.\n\nMCP ke error handling design ke mutabik har error ko kaise report karna chahiye?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Errors 1 aur 2 ko JSON-RPC protocol errors ke roop me report karo, error 3 ko `isError: true` ke saath ek tool result ke roop me report karo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Teeno ko JSON-RPC protocol errors ke roop me report karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Teeno ko `isError: true` ke saath tool results ke roop me report karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Error 1 ko ek JSON-RPC protocol error ke roop me report karo, errors 2 aur 3 ko `isError: true` ke saath tool results ke roop me report karo", "c": true}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai error 1 ko ek JSON-RPC protocol error ke roop me report karna, errors 2 aur 3 ko `isError: true` ke saath tool results ke roop me report karna. Ye agent ko failure ke baare me clearer signals deta hai taaki woh sahi recovery action choose kar sake, blindly retry karne ya bohot jaldi escalate karne ki bajaye. Baaki: A) Ye phir bhi fragile text-generation behavior pe rely karta hai, structure ko zyada reliable tarike se enforce karne ki bajaye. | B) Ye phir bhi fragile text-generation behavior pe rely karta hai, structure ko zyada reliable tarike se enforce karne ki bajaye. | C) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga."}, "c131": {"q": "Developer Productivity: Ek engineer agent se poochta hai monorepo me saari files dhoondhne ko jo `@company/auth` package import karti hain, ye samajhne ke liye ki authentication services ke across kaise use hoti hai.\n\nIs task ke liye kaunsa built-in tool sabse appropriate hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Grep, import statement pattern ko file contents ke across search karne ke liye", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Read, `package.json` files se shuru karke dependency declarations trace karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Bash, `find . -type d -name \"*auth*\"` execute karke matching directories explore karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Glob, unhi files dhoondhne ke liye jinke filename ya path me \"auth\" ho", "c": false}], "e": "Task har us file ko dhoondhna hai jiske content me `@company/auth` ka import ho, jo ek content-search problem hai — exactly wahi jiske liye built-in Grep tool (ripgrep-based) design kiya gaya hai. Glob aur find/Bash sirf filenames ya directory names match karte hain, jo bohot saari importing files miss kar dega jinke path me \"auth\" nahi hai, aur `package.json` files padhna sirf declared dependencies dikhata hai, actual usage sites nahi. Baaki: B) Ye phir bhi fragile text-generation behavior pe rely karta hai, structure ko zyada reliable tarike se enforce karne ki bajaye."}, "c132": {"q": "Tumhare MCP server me `archive_file(file_id)` aur `delete_file(file_id)` tools hain. Production logs dikhate hain ki agent `delete_file` call karta hai jab users \"purani backups remove karo\" poochte hain, jabki policy require karti hai ki backup files archive ki jaayein. Dono tools ki descriptions currently minimal hain: \"Archives a file\" aur \"Deletes a file.\"\n\nKaunsa change tool selection ko sabse directly improve karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek confirmation step add karo jo users ko \"CONFIRM DELETE\" type karne require kare `delete_file` execute hone se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Server-side validation implement karo jo `delete_file` calls ko backup tag wali files ke liye reject kare, ek error message return karte hue jo `archive_file` suggest kare", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "System prompt me few-shot examples add karo jo dikhaye ki \"backup\" ya \"old\" involve karne wali requests ko `archive_file` use karna chahiye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Tool descriptions ko expand karo use cases clarify karne ke liye, `delete_file` me guidance add karte hue jaise \"Do not use for backup files\"", "c": true}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai tool descriptions ko expand karna use cases clarify karne ke liye, `delete_file` me guidance add karte hue jaise \"Do not use for backup files\". Ye tool-selection mistakes kam karta hai decision surface ko clearer aur agent ke task ke saath zyada aligned banake. Baaki: A) Ye us ambiguity ko kam nahi karta jo agent ko galat tool choose karne ki wajah bani. | B) Ye us ambiguity ko kam nahi karta jo agent ko galat tool choose karne ki wajah bani. | C) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte."}, "c140": {"q": "Agent ke MCP tools ko delivery-specific capabilities ke saath expand karne ke baad [`apply_promo_code`, `update_delivery_address`, `reconcile_delivery`], total tool count 1 se 7 tak badh gaya hai. Humne observe kiya hai ki agent ki tool selection accuracy 86% se girke 71% ho gayi hai. Log analysis dikhati hai ki zyaadatar errors semantically overlapping tools ke beech agent ke choose karne me hote hain — `issue_credit` call karna jab `process_refund` correct tha, aur `check_delivery_status` call karna jab dekh rahe the ki `lookup_order` already needed data return kar deta.\n\nKaunsa approach error source me identify kiye gaye semantic overlap ko structurally eliminate karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Chhe naye tools pe `defer_loading` ke saath tool search tool enable karo, original do tools ko hamesha loaded rakhte hue, taaki agent specialized tools ko dynamically sirf zaroorat pade tab discover kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "System prompt me few-shot examples add karo jo har ambiguous tool ke liye correct selection demonstrate karein, jaise dikhaana ki `issue_credit` kab apply hota hai vs `process_refund` kab appropriate hai", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Semantically overlapping tools ko consolidate karo — `issue_credit` aur `process_refund` ko ek single `handle_promotions` tool me merge karo ek `action` parameter ke saath aur `check_delivery_status` ko `lookup_order` me fold karo ek optional `include_tracking` flag ke saath", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Tools ko do sub-agents me split karo — ek 'financial resolution' agent `issue_credit`, `process_refund`, `return_order`, aur `apply_promo_code` ke saath aur ek 'delivery operations' agent baaki delivery tools ke saath — unke beech ek coordinating routing ke saath", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai semantically overlapping tools ko consolidate karna — `issue_credit` aur `process_refund` ko ek single `handle_promotions` tool me merge karna ek `action` parameter ke saath aur `check_delivery_status` ko `lookup_order` me fold karna ek optional `include_tracking` flag ke saath. Ye tool-selection mistakes kam karta hai decision surface ko clearer aur agent ke task ke saath zyada aligned banake. Baaki: A) Ye us ambiguity ko kam nahi karta jo agent ko galat tool choose karne ki wajah bani. | B) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte. | D) Ye us ambiguity ko kam nahi karta jo agent ko galat tool choose karne ki wajah bani."}, "c152": {"q": "Tumne apne Claude agent ko teen MCP servers ke saath configure kiya hai: ek git operations ke liye, ek Jira ticket management ke liye, aur ek documentation search ke liye.\n\nJab ek user agent se poochta hai \"JIRA-123 ke liye ek branch banao aur ticket me documentation links add karo,\" agent in servers ke across tools kaise access karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Tumhe har turn ke liye specify karna hoga kaunsa MCP server use karna hai, aur agent ek waqt me sirf ek server ke tools access kar sakta hai", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Saare configured MCP servers ke tools connection time pe discover ho jaate hain aur agent ke liye simultaneously available hote hain", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Agent request ke basis pe sabse relevant server automatically select karta hai aur sirf us server ke tools load karta hai", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Agent har server ko sequentially query karta hai ye determine karne ke liye ki kaun kaunsa tool handle karta hai, tool name prefixes ke basis pe calls route karte hue", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai ki saare configured MCP servers ke tools connection time pe discover ho jaate hain aur agent ke liye simultaneously available hote hain. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: C) Choice ko auto pe chhodna phir bhi critical decision ko usi jagah rakhta hai jo already fail ho rahi hai."}, "c162": {"q": "Tumhari team Claude Code me MCP servers configure kar rahi hai. Tum ek shared venue lookup server add karna chahte ho jise saare team members access kar sakein, aur tum personally ek experimental music playlist server add karna chahte ho jise sirf tum test kar rahe ho.\n\nKaunsa configuration approach MCP server scopes ko correctly apply karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Dono servers ko apne local `~/.claude.json` me add karo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Venue server ko `.mcp.json` me add karo aur playlist server ko `~/.claude.json` me", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Dono servers ko project-level `.mcp.json` file me add karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Venue server ko `~/.claude.json` me add karo aur playlist server ko `.mcp.json` me", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai venue server ko `.mcp.json` me add karna aur playlist server ko `~/.claude.json` me. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: A) Ye phir bhi fragile text-generation behavior pe rely karta hai, structure ko zyada reliable tarike se enforce karne ki bajaye. | C) Ye phir bhi fragile text-generation behavior pe rely karta hai, structure ko zyada reliable tarike se enforce karne ki bajaye. | D) Ye phir bhi fragile text-generation behavior pe rely karta hai, structure ko zyada reliable tarike se enforce karne ki bajaye."}, "c2": {"q": "Tumhare agent ko ek 150-line utility module ke beech me ek naya helper function insert karna hai, do existing functions ke beech me. Edit tool fail ho jaata hai kyunki uska `old_string` parameter unique text nahi dhoondh paata match karne ke liye — file me repetitive docstrings, variable names, aur structural patterns hain.\n\nIs insertion ko complete karne ka sabse reliable tareeka kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Bash use karo function definition ko file ke end me append karne ke liye heredoc syntax use karke", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Edit use karo ek extremely long `old_string` ke saath jo 30+ lines context capture kare uniqueness guarantee karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Edit ka `replace_all` parameter use karo ek common pattern target karke aur naya function replacement text me embed karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Read use karo file load karne ke liye, appropriate location pe function add karo, phir Write se updated file save karo", "c": true}], "e": "Jab `old_string` unique text nahi dhoondh pata kyunki file me bohot saare repeating patterns hain, sabse reliable tareeka hai poori file padhna (Read), edit karna, aur likhna."}, "c88": {"q": "Tumne Claude Code se ek PDF report generation feature banwane ko kaha hai. Initial implementation database ko correctly query karta hai, lekin output me formatting issues hain: table columns bohot narrow hain jisse content truncate ho jaata hai, dates proper formatting ke bina display hote hain, aur page break handling galat hai. Tumne notice kiya hai ki ye issues ek doosre se interact karte hain — column widths change karne se dates render hone ka tareeka affect hota hai, aur page breaks content height pe depend karte hain.\n\nEk working solution ki taraf iterate karne ka sabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Fresh shuru karo ek detailed prompt ke saath jo saari formatting requirements upfront specify kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Claude ko ek correctly formatted report ka example dikhao aur use us output ko match karne ko kaho, specific technical issues list karne ki jagah", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Pehle column width issue address karo specific measurements ke saath, verify karo ki ye kaam karta hai, phir corrected columns ke andar date formatting fix karo, phir page breaks adjust karo — har change ke baad testing karte hue", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Teeno issues ek single detailed message me do exact specifications ke saath har ek ke liye, Claude ko unhe ek saath ek update me address karne dete hue", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai pehle column width issue address karna specific measurements ke saath, verify karna ki ye kaam karta hai, phir corrected columns ke andar date formatting fix karna, phir page breaks adjust karna — har change ke baad testing karte hue. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: A) Fresh shuru karna useful context waste kar deta hai jo scenario preserve karna chahta hai, isliye underlying problem solve kiye bina cost add karta hai."}, "c90": {"q": "Tumhare monorepo me shared coding standards hain `/docs/standards/security-rules.md` (user data handle karne wali services ke liye), `testing-patterns.md` (saare packages ke liye), aur `api-conventions.md` (API-facing services ke liye). Tumhare 15 packages feature domain ke hisaab se organized hain (`/packages/auth/`, `/packages/billing/`, `/packages/notifications/`, etc.) bina naming conventions ke jo indicate karein ki kaunse user data handle karte hain ya APIs expose karte hain. Package maintainers se expect kiya jaata hai ki woh apni local development settings khud configure karein, kyunki unhe apne package ke domain requirements pata hain. Currently, saari package CLAUDE.md files teeno standards duplicate karti hain, irrelevant guidance apply karte hue.\n\nSabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Saare standards root CLAUDE.md me daalo override instructions ke saath jaise \"security-rules.md ignore karo jab un packages me kaam karo jo user data handle nahi karte\"", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek `shared-standards.md` banao jo `@imports` use kare teeno standards combine karne ke liye, phir har package ki CLAUDE.md ko us combined file ko import karwao", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Har package ki CLAUDE.md me `@imports` use karo sirf un specific standard files ko reference karne ke liye jo us package ke liye relevant hain, maintainer ki domain knowledge ke basis pe", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Har standard ke liye `claude/rules/` files banao YAML frontmatter paths ke saath jo har package directory list kare jaha woh standard apply hona chahiye", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai har package ki CLAUDE.md me `@imports` use karna sirf un specific standard files ko reference karne ke liye jo us package ke liye relevant hain, maintainer ki domain knowledge ke basis pe. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: A) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c94": {"q": "Tumhare code review prompts me dono implementation changes aur corresponding test file shamil hote hain, lekin LLM ki review comments untested code paths point out karne me fail hoti hain. Analysis reveal karti hai ki model un functions ko correctly flag karta hai jinke koi tests hi nahi hain, lekin ye identify karne me fail hota hai jab tested functions ke andar conditional branches ya error-handling paths ki coverage nahi hoti.\n\nPipeline ko overcomplicate kiye bina branch-level coverage gaps ki detection improve karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Few-shot examples include karo jo dikhaye ek uncovered branch wala code, jode hue us review comment ke saath jo specific missing test case identify kare", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek multi-pass pipeline implement karo jaha separate LLM calls pehle saare conditional branches extract karein, phir har ek ko doosre pass me test assertions ke against cross-reference karein", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Prompt ko restructure karo implementation aur tests ko interleave karne ke liye, har function ke turant baad uske test cases present karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Explicit instructions add karo jo model ko direct karein har conditional branch aur exception path enumerate karne ke liye, phir verify karein ki har ek ka corresponding test assertion hai", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai few-shot examples include karna jo dikhaye ek uncovered branch wala code, jode hue us review comment ke saath jo specific missing test case identify kare. Ye agent ko failure ke baare me clearer signals deta hai taaki woh sahi recovery action choose kar sake, blindly retry karne ya bohot jaldi escalate karne ki bajaye. Baaki: B) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | C) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | D) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c96": {"q": "Tumhara pipeline har PR ko ek single API call se review karta hai ek static prompt ke saath jisme diff aur har changed file ka full text hota hai — unchanged files include nahi hoti. Reviews asynchronously post hote hain aur PR creation ko block nahi karte. Developers report karte hain ki reviews consistently cross-file interactions wale bugs miss kar dete hain — jaise, ek PR ek function ke parameters rename karta hai lekin review unchanged files me callers ko flag nahi karta jo abhi bhi old argument order use kar rahe hain. Evaluation dikhati hai ki cross-file bugs reviewed PRs ke 35% production incidents account karte hain.\n\nTumhare review design me sabse effective change kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Har changed file ke liye parallel review passes chalao direct dependents ko har pass me include karte hue, phir ek final summarization call se findings aggregate aur deduplicate karo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Review ko ek turn-limited agentic task ke roop me redesign karo jaha model files read kar sake aur codebase ko tools ke through search kar sake, references follow karte hue cross-file findings verify karne ke liye", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Static analysis use karo changed code ka ek dependency graph build karne ke liye, phir prompt ko expand karo saari files include karne ke liye jo kisi bhi changed file ke do dependency hops ke andar hon", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Chain-of-thought instructions add karo model se poochte hue ki diff me saare external references list kare, phir step-by-step reason kare ki har change doosri files me callers ko kaise affect kar sakta hai", "c": false}], "e": "Failure ek missing-context problem hai: callers unchanged files me rehte hain jo static prompt kabhi include hi nahi karta, isliye chain-of-thought (D) model ko us code ke baare me reason karne me madad nahi kar sakta jo woh dekh nahi sakta, aur static heuristics (A, C) context bloat karte hain phir bhi dynamic ya multi-hop references miss karte hue. Anthropic ki agent guidance agentic search favor karti hai — model ko exactly wahi context retrieve karne dena jo use chahiye file-read/search tools ke through — aur asynchronous, non-blocking review pipeline added latency tolerate karti hai, jabki ek turn limit cost ko bound karti hai. Baaki: A) Isse coordination overhead badhta hai aur justified nahi hai jab tak kaam clearly independent subtasks me separable na ho. | C) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | D) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c103": {"q": "Tumhari team ki CLAUDE.md me ek rule hai: \"4-space indentation use karo aur hamesha Prettier formatting chalao.\" Isके bawajood, code reviews reveal karti hain ki Claude Code jo files generate karta hai unme se roughly 30% inconsistent formatting use karti hain — kabhi 2-space indentation, kabhi missing trailing commas. Emphasis add karna (\"IMPORTANT: You MUST use Prettier formatting\") violations ko ghatakar ~15% kar deta hai, lekin eliminate nahi karta.\n\nSaare generated code ko consistently formatted ensure karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Formatting rules ko path-scoped `.claude/rules/` files me split karo jo tab load hon jab Claude matching file types pe kaam kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek PostToolUse hook configure karo `Edit|Write` matcher ke saath jo har file pe automatically Prettier chalaye jise Claude modify kare", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Formatting rules ko ek dedicated skill me extract karo jise Claude automatically load kare code generate karte waqt, correct formatting ke zyada detailed examples ke saath", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Ek Stop hook add karo ek prompt-based check ke saath jo evaluate kare ki generated code formatting standards follow karta hai ya nahi aur Claude ko violations fix karne ke liye prompt kare", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai ek PostToolUse hook configure karna `Edit|Write` matcher ke saath jo har file pe automatically Prettier chalaye jise Claude modify kare. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: C) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte. | D) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c107": {"q": "Tumhara automated review har PR ke liye Claude API call karta hai, `tool_use` use karke ek `report_findings` tool ke saath jo finding objects ka ek JSON array return karta hai (har ek me `file_path`, `line_number`, `severity`, `category`, aur `description` hote hain). 30+ files touch karne wale ek bade PR pe testing ke dauran, response `max_tokens` limit hit kar leta hai aur output mid-JSON truncate ho jaata hai, jisse tumhara pipeline ka parser fail ho jaata hai.\n\nIse handle karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "`max_tokens` ko model ke maximum tak badhao aur Claude ko instruct karo ki har finding description ko 50 words se kam rakhe", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Retry logic add karo jo truncated JSON detect kare aur request ko dobara bheje instructions ke saath sirf critical aur high severity findings report karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "`tool_use` se switch karke Claude ko prompt karo findings ko ek markdown list ke roop me return karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Review ko multiple API calls me split karo jo har ek changed files ke ek subset ko analyze kare, phir resulting findings arrays ko merge karo", "c": true}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai review ko multiple API calls me split karna jo har ek changed files ke ek subset ko analyze kare, phir resulting findings arrays ko merge karna. Ye output ko required structure ke saath aligned rakhne aur downstream parsing ya validation failures kam karne ka sabse reliable tareeka hai. Baaki: A) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | B) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | C) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c120": {"q": "Tumne apne project root pe ek CLAUDE.md file me API error handling conventions document kiye hain, specify karte hue ki endpoint handlers ek custom `ApiError` class use karein. Kai sessions ke baad, tum notice karte ho ki Claude Code kabhi in conventions ko follow karta hai aur kabhi generic try/catch blocks string messages ke saath use karta hai. Ye inconsistency alag-alag coding sessions me random lagti hai.\n\nSabse efficient pehla diagnostic step kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "`/memory` chalao ye check karne ke liye ki konsi memory files load hui hain aur verify karo ki tumhari CLAUDE.md included hai", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "`claude/rules/handlers.md` me path-specific rules banao YAML frontmatter ke saath jo error handling instructions ko tumhare API handler files tak scope kare", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "`~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` ya `~/.claude/rules/` me conflicting instructions dhoondo jo tumhari project conventions ko override kar sakti hain", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Apni CLAUDE.md me zyada detailed code examples add karo jo different endpoint types ke liye exact ApiError usage pattern dikhaye", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai `/memory` chalana ye check karne ke liye ki konsi memory files load hui hain aur verify karna ki tumhari CLAUDE.md included hai. Ye agent ko failure ke baare me clearer signals deta hai taaki woh sahi recovery action choose kar sake, blindly retry karne ya bohot jaldi escalate karne ki bajaye. Baaki: B) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | C) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | D) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte."}, "c121": {"q": "Tumhara CI pipeline roz approximately 50 PRs pe security-focused code reviews perform karta hai, currently synchronous API use karke $150/day cost karta hai. Reviews non-blocking hain — developers tests pass hone ke baad merge kar dete hain aur findings ko follow-up commits me address karte hain. Tum Message Batches API evaluate kar rahe ho uske 50% cost reduction ke liye.\n\nKaunsa factor sabse zyada determine karta hai ki batch processing is use case ke liye appropriate hai ya nahi?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Kya tumhara result processing reviews ko handle kar sakta hai jo submitted order se alag order me aati hain", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Kya PR creation ke 24 hours baad tak aane wali review feedback abhi bhi actionable rahegi", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Kya tum har review ko ek single request ke roop me structure kar sakte ho bina multi-turn refinement ke", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Kya per-review latency ko 30-60 seconds se near-instant tak kam karna tumhare workflow ke liye matter karta hai", "c": false}], "e": "Message Batches API asynchronous hai — zyaadatar batches 1 hour ke andar finish ho jaate hain lekin 24 hours tak le sakte hain — isliye decisive suitability factor latency tolerance hai: kya PR creation ke 24 hours baad tak deliver hui review findings abhi bhi actionable hain ek non-blocking, merge-then-fix workflow me. Batching latency badhata hai (B ulta hai), results `custom_id` ke through correlate hote hain isliye ordering ek non-issue hai (D), aur single-request structuring (A) latency question ke against secondary hai."}, "c129": {"q": "Tumhare code review assistant ko pull requests analyze karke teen aspects pe feedback dena hai: code style compliance, potential security issues, aur documentation completeness. Har aspect ko files padhna, analysis tools chalana, aur ek report section generate karna chahiye. Review process har PR ke liye same three-step workflow follow karta hai.\n\nIs workflow ke liye kaunsa task decomposition pattern sabse appropriate hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Routing — har PR ko type ke hisaab se classify karo (feature, bugfix, refactor) pehle, phir alag review prompts pe route karo jo us category ke liye optimized hain", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Prompt chaining — review ko sequential steps me todo jaha har aspect (style, security, documentation) separately analyze ho, outputs ko ek final synthesis step me combine karte hue", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Single comprehensive prompt — saari instructions ek prompt me include karo aur model ko teeno aspects simultaneously handle karne do", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Orchestrator-workers — ek central LLM se har PR analyze karwao dynamically determine karne ke liye ki kaunse checks chahiye, phir specialized worker LLMs ko har identified subtask ke liye delegate karo", "c": false}], "e": "Scenario explicitly kehta hai ki review \"har PR ke liye same three-step workflow follow karta hai,\" jo Anthropic ki \"Building Effective Agents\" guidance ke mutabik prompt chaining workflow ka textbook case hai: ek fixed, predictable sequence of subtasks jinme se har ek ko ek focused prompt handle kare, phir synthesize kiya jaaye. Orchestrator-workers (D) sirf tab justified hai jab zaroori subtasks har input ke hisaab se unpredictably vary karte hon, aur routing (B) tab apply hoti hai jab inputs distinct categories me aati hain jinhe different handling chahiye — dono fixed, identical workflow fit nahi karte. Baaki: A) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | C) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c137": {"q": "Tum ek complex graph traversal algorithm implement kar rahe ho specific performance requirements aur edge cases handle karne ke saath (disconnected nodes, cycles, weighted edges). Tum apna workflow structure karna chahte ho Claude ke saath efficient iterative refinement ke liye.\n\nKaunsa approach multiple iterations ke across progressive improvement ko sabse effectively enable karega?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Claude ko algorithm ki ek detailed natural language specification do, saari requirements aur edge cases samet. Har output ko manually review karo aur descriptive feedback do ki kya behavior badalna hai", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Claude se algorithm pe extensively research karwao aur extended thinking use karke ek detailed implementation plan banwao, phir us plan ke basis pe complete solution implement karwao", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek test suite likho jo expected behavior, edge cases, aur performance requirements cover kare implementation se pehle. Claude se code likhwao jo tests pass kare, phir har refinement request me test failures share karke iterate karo", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Claude ko documentation se ek reference implementation do, phir use code ko rewrite karne ko kaho tumhare codebase style match karne ke liye aur required edge case handling add karne ke liye, outputs ko reference ke against compare karte hue", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai ek test suite likhna jo expected behavior, edge cases, aur performance requirements cover kare implementation se pehle. Claude se code likhwana jo tests pass kare, phir har refinement request me test failures share karke iterate karna. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: D) Documentation useful background de sakti hai, lekin ye code me har real caller ya usage path dhoondhne ka reliable tareeka nahi hai."}, "c138": {"q": "Tumhare infrastructure-as-code repository me Terraform modules (`/terraform/`), Kubernetes manifests (`/kubernetes/`), aur CI/CD pipeline scripts (`/pipelines/`) shamil hain. Har ek ko different conventions chahiye, lekin tumhari single root CLAUDE.md 500+ lines tak badh gayi hai. Jab developers Kubernetes files pe kaam karte hain, Terraform-specific rules unnecessarily context me load ho jaati hain, tokens consume karte hue.\n\nReorganize karne ka sabse acha approach kya hai taaki sirf relevant guidance load ho specific file types edit karte waqt?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Root CLAUDE.md rakho aur `@path/to/import` syntax use karo tool-specific guidance files ko separate documents se modularly include karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Content ko subdirectory CLAUDE.md files me split karo (`/terraform/CLAUDE.md`, `/kubernetes/CLAUDE.md`), taaki Claude directory-specific guidance load kare", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "`.claude/rules/` me files banao YAML frontmatter path-scoping ke saath (jaise `paths: [\"terraform/**/*\"]`), rules ko sirf matching files edit karte waqt load karte hue", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Root CLAUDE.md ko clearly labeled sections me restructure karo headers ke saath (jaise \"## Terraform Conventions\"), organization aur readability improve karte hue", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai `.claude/rules/` me files banana YAML frontmatter path-scoping ke saath (jaise `paths: [\"terraform/**/*\"]`), rules ko sirf matching files edit karte waqt load karte hue. Ye context ko zyada deliberately manage karta hai taaki model sabse important information available rakhe bina brittle long-history recall pe depend kiye. Baaki: A) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | B) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | D) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai."}, "c144": {"q": "Tumhara test generation naye code ke liye unit tests produce karta hai, lekin reviews dikhati hain ki 55% low-value hain: trivial assertions jo sirf verify karte hain ki functions exceptions throw nahi karte, tests jo existing coverage duplicate karte hain, ya tests jo tumhari team ke fixture conventions ignore karte hain.\n\nLow-value tests generate hone ki rate ko shuru se kaise kam karein?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek two-phase generation implement karo jaha ek second Claude call har test ko quality criteria ke against score kare, low-scoring tests filter out karte hue developers ko results present karne se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Post-generation coverage analysis add karo jo automatically kisi bhi generated test ko filter kare jo existing tests jo provide karte hain us se zyada line coverage increase nahi karta", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Test generation ko un directories tak restrict karo jaha historical quality metrics higher acceptance rates dikhate hain, use un areas ke liye disable karte hue jaha generated tests consistently heavy editing require karte hain", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "CLAUDE.md me testing standards document karo jisme valuable test criteria, intended use cases ke saath available fixtures, aur meaningful behavioral tests ko trivial assertions se distinguish karne wale examples shamil hon", "c": true}], "e": "Sawaal explicitly poochta hai ki low-value tests ko \"shuru se generate\" hone se kaise roka jaaye, jiska matlab hai upstream cause fix karna: Claude ko context nahi hai ki team kya ek valuable test consider karti hai. CLAUDE.md me testing standards, fixture usage, aur good-vs-trivial examples document karna Claude ko generation time pe woh context deta hai, jabki A aur D sirf bad output ko baad me filter karte hain aur B problem solve karne ki jagah avoid karta hai."}, "c148": {"q": "Tumhari team frequently React components ko Vue me migrate karti hai. Tumne har migration ke dauran Claude Code ke follow karne ke liye ek step-by-step workflow likha hai, aur tum chahte ho ki team ka har developer `/migrate-component` type karke ise invoke kare. Workflow team ke iterate karne ke saath sync me rehna chahiye.\n\nSkill file kahan rakhni chahiye?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "`.claude/skills/migrate-component/SKILL.md` me project root pe, version control me committed", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Project ki root CLAUDE.md file me ek detailed instruction block ke roop me", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Project ki `.claude/settings.json` me ek `skillOverrides` entry use karke workflow register aur define karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "`~/.claude/skills/migrate-component/SKILL.md` me har developer ki machine pe", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai `.claude/skills/migrate-component/SKILL.md` me project root pe, version control me committed. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: C) Ye phir bhi fragile text-generation behavior pe rely karta hai, structure ko zyada reliable tarike se enforce karne ki bajaye."}, "c151": {"q": "Ek developer apne development session ke dauran ek function refactor karne ke liye Claude Code use karta hai. Commit karne se pehle, woh usi Claude session se code ko issues ke liye review karne ko kehte hain. Baad me, ek separate automated CI review kai bugs pakadti hai jo same-session review ne miss kar diye the.\n\nIs discrepancy ko sabse acche se kya explain karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Extended session length ki wajah se context window conversation history se bhar gaya, thorough analysis ke liye kam room chhodte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Claude session me apni prior reasoning ke baare me context retain karta hai, jisse woh apne khud ke decisions ko question karne ki possibility kam ho jaati hai", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "CI review ek zyada specific prompt use karta hai jo bugs pakadne ke liye tailored hai, jabki developer ki request bohot general thi", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "CI environment ke paas poore codebase context tak access hai jabki local session sirf current file dekhta hai", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai ye samajhna ki Claude session me apni prior reasoning ke baare me context retain karta hai, jisse woh apne khud ke decisions ko question karne ki possibility kam ho jaati hai. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: C) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c158": {"q": "Automated code review deploy karne ke baad, developers report karte hain ki approximately 35% flagged findings false positives hain jo consistent patterns me aati hain: style suggestion jo team conventions se contradict karti hain, security warnings un patterns ke liye jo tumhare deployment context me safe hain, aur performance suggestions jo tumhare specific use case ko degrade kar dengi. Tum false positives kam karna chahte ho genuine issues pakadne ki ability maintain karte hue.\n\nKaunsa approach model ko unseen novel code patterns pe apna judgment generalize karne me sabse acche se enable karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Un saare patterns ki ek comprehensive written specification banao jo flag nahi hone chahiye, phir is poori documentation ko system prompt me include karo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "System prompt me instructions add karo \"conservative raho,\" \"sirf definite issues flag karo,\" aur \"consider karo ki kuch patterns intentional ho sakte hain\"", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Post-processing implement karo jo keyword matching use karke findings filter kare jinme \"convention,\" \"context-dependent,\" ya \"trade-off\" jaise terms hon", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Apne prompt me few-shot examples include karo jo annotated code snippets dikhaye jo har category me acceptable patterns ko genuine issues se distinguish karein", "c": true}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai apne prompt me few-shot examples include karna jo annotated code snippets dikhaye jo har category me acceptable patterns ko genuine issues se distinguish karein. Ye context ko zyada deliberately manage karta hai taaki model sabse important information available rakhe bina brittle long-history recall pe depend kiye. Baaki: A) Documentation useful background de sakti hai, lekin ye code me har real caller ya usage path dhoondhne ka reliable tareeka nahi hai. | B) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | C) Surface-level searching yahan bohot narrow hai kyunki task ko simple text matching se zyada rich structural understanding chahiye."}, "c159": {"q": "Tum Claude Code use karke ek non-interactive automated code review pipeline set up kar rahe ho. Tum chahte ho ki Claude ek pulled Git diff (`git diff`) ko main branch ke against analyze kare aur code review instructions ka ek custom set apply kare. Lekin, tum notice karte ho ki jab tum pipeline chalate ho, Claude sirf raw diff text ko hi dekhta hai aur apne file-reading ya code navigation tools use karna completely band kar deta hai. Iske result me, woh broader codebase repository context inspect karne me fail hota hai, jo critical hai kyunki diff ek core function modify karta hai jise kai doosre external modules call karte hain.\n\nCLI invocation me kaunsa change Claude ko repository me related files padhne dega jabki woh tumhari custom review instructions bhi successfully apply karta rahe?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "`--system-prompt` ko completely remove karo aur review instructions ko repo root pe ek CLAUDE.md file me rakho, kyunki `--system-prompt` `-p` ke under tool use ke saath incompatible hai", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "`--system-prompt` ko `--append-system-prompt` se replace karo taaki tumhari review instructions Claude Code ke default prompt me add ho jaayein, file-reading aur code navigation tools use karne ke built-in guidance ko overwrite karne ki bajaye", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "`--system-prompt` rakho aur `--allowedTools \"Read, Glob, Grep\"` add karo taaki non-interactive mode file system tools permit kare jo woh otherwise disable karta hai", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Diff ko stdin ke through pipe karna band karo aur uski jagah diff contents ko prompt string ke andar embed karo, taaki Claude Code invocation ko ek agentic session ki tarah treat kare, stream-processing session ki jagah", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai `--system-prompt` ko `--append-system-prompt` se replace karna taaki tumhari review instructions Claude Code ke default prompt me add ho jaayein, file-reading aur code navigation tools use karne ke built-in guidance ko overwrite karne ki bajaye. Ye agent ko failure ke baare me clearer signals deta hai taaki woh sahi recovery action choose kar sake, blindly retry karne ya bohot jaldi escalate karne ki bajaye. Baaki: A) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | C) Surface-level searching yahan bohot narrow hai kyunki task ko simple text matching se zyada rich structural understanding chahiye. | D) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c160": {"q": "Tumhari development team ek bade codebase ke across test generation automate karne ke liye Claude Code use kar rahi hai. Lekin, developers frequently generated test suites reject kar rahe hain kyunki Claude ek high volume trivial assertions ya tests generate karta hai jo sirf line coverage maximize karte hain bina meaningful behavioral logic ya edge cases validate kiye. Tum Claude ko high-quality, production-ready tests directly generate karne ke liye guide karna chahte ho bina high latency introduce kiye ya core pipeline script modify kiye.\n\nKaunsi strategy sabse acche se ensure karti hai ki high-quality, meaningful tests shuru se hi generate hon?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "CLAUDE.md me testing standards document karo jisme valuable test criteria, intended use cases ke saath available fixtures, aur meaningful behavioral tests ko trivial assertions se distinguish karne wale examples shamil hon", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Test generation ko un directories tak restrict karo jaha historical quality metrics higher acceptance rates dikhate hain, use un areas ke liye disable karte hue jaha generated tests consistently heavy editing require karte hain", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek two-phase generation implement karo jaha ek second Claude call har test ko quality criteria ke against score kare, low-scoring tests filter out karte hue developers ko results present karne se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Post-generation coverage analysis add karo jo automatically kisi bhi generated test ko filter kare jo existing tests jo provide karte hain us se zyada line coverage increase nahi karta", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai CLAUDE.md me testing standards document karna jisme valuable test criteria, intended use cases ke saath available fixtures, aur meaningful behavioral tests ko trivial assertions se distinguish karne wale examples shamil hon. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai."}, "c10": {"q": "Ek engineer ne kal agent use karke ek legacy authentication module analyze kiya tha, do distinct refactoring approaches identify karte hue: microservice extract karna vs in-place refactor karna. Aaj, woh dono approaches ko depth me explore karna chahte hain — agent se har ek ke liye specific code changes propose karwate hue — kaunsa implement karna hai decide karne se pehle.\n\nIs exploration ko structure karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Kal ka session resume karo pehla approach explore karne ke liye, phir doosre ke liye ek naya session shuru karo, manually original context recreate karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "`fork_session` use karo kal ke analysis se do branches banane ke liye, har fork me ek approach explore karte hue", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Kal ka session resume karo aur dono approaches ko sequentially usi conversation thread me explore karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Do fresh sessions shuru karo, manually kal ke analysis findings ka ek summary provide karke context establish karte hue", "c": false}], "e": "`fork_session` usi analysis point se do branches banane deta hai, har branch alag approach explore karte hue ek doosre ko affect kiye bina, jabki pichle session ka poora context intact rehta hai. Baaki: A) Naye changes ko explicitly incorporate kiye bina resume karna stale assumptions ko agle step me carry forward karne ka risk leta hai. | C) Naye changes ko explicitly incorporate kiye bina resume karna stale assumptions ko agle step me carry forward karne ka risk leta hai. | D) Fresh sessions accumulated context ka advantage kho dete hain jo already available hai aur unnecessary rework create karte hain."}, "c13": {"q": "Ek engineer agent se poochta hai caching layer kaise kaam karta hai samajhne ke liye ek naya cache invalidation trigger add karne se pehle. Initial Grep searches ke baad, agent ne identify kiya hai ki caching logic 15 files (decorators, middleware, aur service classes samet, ~8,000 lines total) ke across span karti hai.\n\nContext constraints manage karte hue understanding build karne ke liye sabse effective agla step kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Imports aur class hierarchies analyze karo base cache class identify karne ke liye, us file ko Read karo interface samajhne ke liye, phir specific invalidation implementations trace karo", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Read tool use karo saari 15 files ko sequentially load karne ke liye, poore caching implementation ke across complete understanding build karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Grep use karo \"invalidate\" aur \"expire\" patterns saari files ke across search karne ke liye, phir sirf un specific line ranges ko minimal surrounding context ke saath Read karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Glob use karo common caching patterns match karne wali files dhoondhne ke liye (`cache.py`, `caching/`), sabse badi files ko pehle padhte hue prioritize karo, phir gaps ke liye chhoti files check karo", "c": false}], "e": "Class hierarchy se shuru karke base cache class dhoondhna, interface padhna, phir implementations trace karna sabse effective tareeka hai. Saari 15 files padhne se bacho (bohot zyada context) ya sirf patterns search karne se (architectural context ki kami). Baaki: B) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | C) Surface-level searching yahan bohot narrow hai kyunki task ko simple text matching se zyada rich structural understanding chahiye. | D) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai."}, "c16": {"q": "Tumhara extraction pipeline aise contracts process karta hai jinme frequently amendments hote hain. Jab ek contract me dono original terms aur baad ke amendments hote hain (jaise, original clause \"30-day payment terms\" specify karta hai jabki Amendment 1 ise \"45 days\" me badal deta hai), model inconsistently ek value ya doosri extract karta hai bina kisi indication ke ki kaunsi apply hoti hai.\n\nAmendments wale documents ke liye extraction accuracy improve karne ka sabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Post-extraction validation implement karo pattern matching use karke amendments detect karne ke liye aur un extractions ko manual review ke liye flag karo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Schema ko redesign karo taaki amended fields multiple values capture karein, har ek source location aur effective date ke saath", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Documents ko ek classifier se preprocess karo jo superseded sections identify aur remove kare main extraction step se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Prompt instructions add karo ki hamesha sabse recent amendment value extract karo aur superseded original terms ignore karo", "c": false}], "e": "Jab ek document me dono original terms aur amendments ho, schema ko dono values capture karni chahiye effective date aur source location ke saath. Ye complete information preserve karta hai aur downstream systems ko khud decide karne deta hai ki kaunsi values apply karni hain. Baaki: A) Ye problem ko defer karta hai us system behavior ko solve karne ki bajaye jisne ise cause kiya. | D) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c17": {"q": "Deployment ke baad, tumhe pata chalta hai ki 12% extractions me semantic errors hain jo JSON schema validation pass kar jaate hain (jaise, ek duration jaisa \"30 minutes\" galti se ek ingredient quantity field me place ho jaana). Human reviewers ke paas sirf 20% extractions check karne ki capacity hai.\n\nKaunsa approach reviewer attention ko sabse effectively allocate karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Un documents se saari extractions review karo jinme formatting anomalies hain jaise unusual layouts ya mixed content types", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Model ko field-level confidence scores output karwao, phir review thresholds calibrate karo ek labeled validation set use karke", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Un saari extractions ki review prioritize karo jaha required fields empty hon ya explicitly not found mark hon", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "20% extractions ko randomly sample karo review ke liye, corrections use karke accuracy track karo aur error patterns identify karo", "c": false}], "e": "Semantic errors ko schema validation ke through detect karna mushkil hai. 20% reviewer capacity optimize karne ke liye, model ko field-level confidence scores output karwao aur phir labeled validation set use karke optimal threshold dhoondo, review ko low confidence wali extractions pe focus karte hue. Baaki: A) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | C) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | D) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai."}, "c18": {"q": "Tumhara extraction pipeline invoices process karta hai aur line items, tax amounts, aur grand totals extract karta hai. Tumhe pata chalta hai ki 8% documents me extracted line item amounts extracted grand total tak sum nahi hote — downstream accounting system mismatches detect kar raha hai.\n\nSabse effective improvement kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek `calculated_total` field add karo jaha model line items independently extract kare, phir totals ko ek `is_total_consistent` boolean flag ke saath validate kare human review ke liye jab values differ karein", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "System prompt me few-shot examples add karo jaha extracted line items correctly sum hote hain desired extraction behavior demonstrate karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Line items aur totals ko independently extract karo, phir ek separate validation model use karo discrepancies reconcile karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Post-processing implement karo jo automatically line item amounts adjust kare jab extracted total match na kare", "c": false}], "e": "`calculated_total` field add karo taaki model line items se total calculate karke self-validate kar sake aur grand total se compare kar sake, ek boolean flag ke saath jo review needed cases flag kare. Ye method extraction step me hi mismatches detect kar leta hai. Baaki: B) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte."}, "c19": {"q": "Tumhara pipeline ek tool use karta hai `extract_metadata` naam ka ek JSON schema ke saath paper details ke liye. Testing ke dauran, agent kabhi-kabhi `extract_metadata` call karne me fail ho jaata hai kyunki woh direct answers provide karna chahta hai.\n\nMetadata extraction ko hamesha pehle ensure karne ka sabse reliable tareeka kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "`tool_choice` ko type \"tool\", name \"extract_metadata\" set karo aur enrichment requests ko subsequent turns me process karo extracted metadata receive karne ke baad", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "API call me `tool_choice` ko \"auto\" set karo, tools ke saath combine karke taaki Claude hamesha metadata ko doosre tool calls se pehle prioritize kare", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "`tool_choice` ko \"auto\" set karo aur tool definitions ko reorder karo `extract_metadata` ko pehle rakhte hue kyunki Claude earlier-listed tools ko prioritize karta hai", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "`tool_choice` ko type \"any\" set karo taaki Claude ko koi tool use karna hi pade, system prompt instructions ke saath combine karte hue `extract_metadata` ko pehle call karne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "`tool_choice` ko type \"tool\" aur name \"extract_metadata\" ke saath use karna Claude ko sahi tool pehle call karne force karta hai. Metadata receive karne ke baad, enrichment requests subsequent turns me process hote hain. Ye ek hi tareeka hai jo 100% guaranteed hai. Baaki: B) Choice ko auto pe chhodna phir bhi critical decision ko usi jagah rakhta hai jo already fail ho rahi hai. | C) Ye phir bhi critical decision ko model discretion pe chhod deta hai, jo exactly wahi hai jo scenario keh raha hai fail ho raha hai. | D) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c20": {"q": "Tumhara daily 10,000 documents ka batch complete hone ke baad, 300 documents (3%) \"context_length_exceeded\" errors ke saath fail ho gaye. Results file har failure ko `custom_id` se identify karti hai.\n\nIn failures ko process karne ka sabse cost-effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Poore 10,000 document batch ko ek larger context window wale model tier use karke resubmit karo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Sirf 300 failed documents ko resubmit karo unhe chhote pieces me chunk karne ke baad, phir partial extractions ko combine karo", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "300 failed documents ke liye `max_tokens` parameter badhao aur unhe ek naye batch me resubmit karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Poore batch ko prompt caching enabled ke saath reprocess karo identical system prompts ke saath requests retry karne ka cost kam karne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "`context_length_exceeded` ek error hai kyunki input bohot lamba hai, output nahi. Sirf 300 failed documents ko chhote pieces me chunk karne ke baad resubmit karo. Saare 10,000 documents reprocess karne ya `max_tokens` badhane ki zaroorat nahi. Baaki: A) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | C) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | D) Ye galat hai kyunki retry khud se underlying cause resolve nahi karta jab tak failure clearly transient na ho."}, "c21": {"q": "Tumhara extraction system e-commerce product descriptions parse karta hai specifications jaise dimensions, weight, aur materials ko JSON me extract karne ke liye. Ek well-defined schema hone ke bawajood, model inconsistently \"materials\" field extract karta hai — kabhi \"cotton blend\" return karta hai, kabhi \"Cotton/Polyester mix\", aur kabhi-kabhi field omit kar deta hai jab material information source me clearly present hoti hai.\n\nExtraction consistency improve karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Temperature ko 0 set karo randomness eliminate karne ke liye aur deterministic outputs ensure karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "\"materials\" field ko schema me optional ki jagah required banao model ko hamesha ek value extract karne force karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Few-shot examples add karo jo 2-3 complete input-output pairs dikhaye standardized material description formats ke saath", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Ek zyada capable model tier pe switch karo kyunki inconsistent extraction insufficient model capability indicate karta hai", "c": false}], "e": "Extraction me inconsistency aksar standard formats ke specific examples ki kami ki wajah se hoti hai. Standardized material descriptions wale few-shot examples model ko output properly format karna sikhaate hain, temperature=0 set karne ya field required banane se zyada effectively. Baaki: A) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | B) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | D) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai."}, "c22": {"q": "Tumhara system news articles se event metadata (date, location, organizer, attendee_count) extract karta hai ek JSON schema use karke jisme saare fields nullable hain. Evaluation ke dauran, tum observe karte ho ki model frequently plausible lekin incorrect values generate karta hai un fields ke liye jo article me mention nahi hain — jaise, attendee_count ke liye \"500\" output karna jab source me koi attendance information hi nahi hai.\n\nIn false extractions ko kam karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Prompt instructions add karo ki kisi bhi field ke liye null return karo jaha information source me directly stated nahi hai", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Saare schema fields ko required (non-nullable) banao strict validation rules ke saath ensure karne ke liye ki model sirf verifiable data output kare", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek post-processing step add karo ek second LLM call use karke verify karne ke liye ki har extracted value source document me exist karti hai", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Ek zyada capable model tier pe upgrade karo improved instruction-following ke saath hallucination tendencies kam karne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "Model probable values hallucinate karta hai un fields ke liye jo source me present nahi hain clear 'no information' instructions ki kami ki wajah se. Explicit instruction add karna 'agar information directly source me nahi hai toh null return karo' directly problem solve karta hai. Baaki: B) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | C) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | D) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai."}, "c23": {"q": "Strict schema definitions ke saath tool use implement karne ke baad, JSON syntax errors eliminate ho gaye hain, lekin 5% extractions me abhi bhi valid JSON hai empty arrays ya null values ke saath required fields jaise citations aur methodology ke liye. Spot-checking reveal karti hai ki source documents me ye information hai, lekin varied formats me — inline citations vs bibliographies, methodology sections vs introductions me embedded details.\n\nIn failures ko address karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Few-shot examples add karo jo varied structures wale documents se extractions demonstrate karein — dikhaate hue ki different formats me citations kaise identify karein aur section types ke across methodology details kaise locate karein", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek regex-based post-processing layer banao jo source documents ko citation patterns aur methodology keywords ke liye scan kare, empty fields populate karte hue jab model extract karne me fail ho", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Retry logic implement karo jo requests ko dobara bheje jab validation empty required fields detect kare", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Apne schema ko modify karo citations aur methodology ko optional banane ke liye, aur incomplete records ko manual review ke liye flag karo validation fail karne ki jagah", "c": false}], "e": "Kyunki same information kai alag formats me appear hoti hai (inline vs bibliography, section vs embedded), ye few-shot examples jo dikhaate hain in formats se kaise identify aur extract karein extraction improve karne ka sabse effective tareeka hain. Baaki: B) Surface-level searching yahan bohot narrow hai kyunki task ko simple text matching se zyada rich structural understanding chahiye. | C) Ye galat hai kyunki retry khud se underlying cause resolve nahi karta jab tak failure clearly transient na ho. | D) Manual review ek fallback ke roop me useful ho sakta hai, lekin ye us system behavior ko solve nahi karta jise sawaal improve karne ko keh raha hai."}, "c24": {"q": "Tumhara extraction system automatic retries implement karta hai jab validation fail ho. Har retry pe, specific validation error prompt me append hota hai. Ye retry-with-error-feedback approach zyaadatar failures ko 2-3 attempts ke andar resolve kar deta hai.\n\nKiस failure pattern ke liye additional retries SABSE KAM effective honge?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Model keywords ko ek nested object ke roop me extract karta hai category se organized jab schema ko strings ka ek flat array chahiye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Model citation counts ko locale-formatted strings (\"1,234\") ke roop me extract karta hai jab schema ko integers chahiye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Model co-authors ke liye \"et al.\" extract karta hai jab full list sirf ek external document me exist karti hai jo input me nahi hai", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Model dates ko ISO 8601 datetime strings (\"2023-03-15T00:00:00Z\") ke roop me extract karta hai jab schema ko sirf date portion (YYYY-MM-DD) chahiye", "c": false}], "e": "Koi bhi amount retrying model ko woh information nahi sikha sakti jo input me hai hi nahi. Retry-with-error-feedback sirf woh galtiyan fix karta hai jo model source se sahi kar sakta tha. Baaki: A) Surface-level searching yahan bohot narrow hai kyunki task ko simple text matching se zyada rich structural understanding chahiye. | B) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | D) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga."}, "c25": {"q": "Tumhara extraction pipeline restaurant menus process karta hai aur structured JSON output karna zaroori hai item names, descriptions, prices, aur dietary tags ke fields ke saath. Kuch menus inconsistent formatting use karte hain — prices \"$12\" vs \"12.00\" ke roop me, dietary info icons vs text ke roop me.\n\nSabse reliable approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Data ko as-is extract karo aur formats ko post-processing code me normalize karo Claude ke return karne ke baad", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Har document ke liye multiple extraction attempts request karo aur sabse common format select karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek strict output schema define karo aur apne prompt me format normalization rules include karo", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Har field ke liye separate extraction calls use karo har type ke consistent handling ensure karne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "Inconsistent formatting wale menus ke liye, strict output schema (structure) ko prompt me hi normalization rules (jaise: 'prices float ke roop me currency symbol ke bina') ke saath combine karna, extraction step me hi normalize karna, sabse effective aur simple hai. Baaki: A) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | B) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | D) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai."}, "c26": {"q": "Tumhara extraction tool use ke saath ek JSON schema use karta hai jaha `property_type` ek enum ke roop me define hai: ['house', 'apartment', 'condo', 'townhouse']. Deployment ke baad, 8% extractions schema validation fail ho jaati hain. Investigation reveal karti hai ki listings kai uncommon property types mention karti hain — \"studio\", \"loft\", \"duplex\", \"mobile home\", \"tiny house\", \"converted warehouse\" — aur naye types regularly appear hote rehte hain.\n\nSabse effective long-term solution kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "`property_type` ko ek enum se ek free-form string me badlo aur post-processing me ek normalization step implement karo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Enum ko continuously expand karo naye observed property types include karne ke liye aur additional edge cases ke liye monitoring add karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Apne enum me ek \"other\" value add karo ek separate `property_type_detail` string field ke saath specifics ke liye jab \"other\" select ho", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Apne prompt me few-shot examples add karo jo dikhaye ki unexpected property types ko closest existing enum value me kaise map karein", "c": false}], "e": "Kyunki naye property types constantly appear hote hain, hard enums hamesha outdated rahenge. 'Other' value add karna apni khud ki `property_type_detail` field ke saath saare current aur future edge cases handle karna deta hai bina enum ko constantly update kiye. Baaki: A) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | B) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | D) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte."}, "c27": {"q": "Tumhara system 3 mahine se 100% human review ke saath operate kar raha hai. Analysis dikhati hai ki >90% model confidence wali extractions overall 97% accuracy rakhti hain. Reviewer workload kam karne ke liye, tum high-confidence extractions ko automate karne ka plan bana rahe ho.\n\nDeploy karne se pehle, sabse critical validation step kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek two-week pilot chalao jo 25% high-confidence extractions ko directly downstream systems tak route kare aur error reports monitor kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Document type aur field ke hisaab se accuracy analyze karo verify karne ke liye ki high-confidence extractions saare segments me consistently perform karti hain, sirf aggregate me nahi", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Verify karo ki 97% accuracy saare downstream systems ki requirements meet karti hai jo extracted data consume karte hain", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Alag-alag confidence thresholds (85%, 90%, 95%) pe accuracy compare karo optimal cutoff dhoondhne ke liye jo automation maximize kare errors minimize karte hue", "c": false}], "e": "Aggregate accuracy segment failures chhupa deti hai — ek document type 70% ho sakta hai jabki doosre 99% hon. Sirf overall number se auto-routing weak segments me systemic errors ka risk leta hai."}, "c28": {"q": "Documents business hours ke through continuously aate hain aur unse structured data extract karni hoti hai. Costs kam karne ke liye, tum Message Batches API use karna chahte ho (50% discount, up-to-24-hour processing window). Tumhara SLA specify karta hai ki extraction results document arrival ke 30 hours ke andar 99.9% reliability ke saath available hone chahiye.\n\nKaunsi batching strategy sabse appropriate hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Saare documents ke liye batch processing ki jagah real-time API use karo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Har 4 hours pe batches submit karo us window ke documents ke saath", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Har 6 hours pe batches submit karo us window ke documents ke saath", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Din ke end me ek single batch submit karo us din ke saare documents ke saath", "c": false}], "e": "Har 4 hours pe batches submit karna ensure karta hai ki worst case me, documents maximum 4 hours + 24 hours processing = 28 hours wait karein jo 30 hours SLA se kam hai. Har 6 hours submit karna SLA violate kar sakta hai (6 + 24 = 30 hours bina safety buffer ke)."}, "c29": {"q": "Tumhara schema me ek `skills: string[]` field hai. Production monitoring teen consistency issues reveal karti hai: (1) compound phrases jaise \"Python and SQL\" kabhi ek entry ke roop me rakhi jaati hain, kabhi split ki jaati hain; (2) implied lekin unstated skills kabhi-kabhi extractions me appear hoti hain; (3) similar documents wildly different array lengths produce karte hain (5-10 vs 40+ entries). Tumhara prompt currently kehta hai \"Extract all skills mentioned.\"\n\nSabse effective improvement kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Few-shot examples add karo jo compound phrase handling, explicit mention criteria, aur appropriate entry granularity demonstrate karein", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Constraints add karo: \"Maximum 10-20 skills extract karo, ek entry me ek skill, sirf explicitly named skills\"", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Post-extraction normalization add karo jo skills ko ek canonical taxonomy se map kare aur similar entries deduplicate kare", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Schema ko `{skill: string, confidence: float, source_quote: string[]}` me enrich karo extraction metadata capture karne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "Teeno problems (compound phrases, implied skills, length inconsistency) sab expected behavior ke specific examples ki kami se stem karte hain. Few-shot examples jo compound phrase handling, explicit mention criteria, aur granularity demonstrate karein teeno issues ko directly address karte hain. Baaki: B) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | C) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | D) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai."}, "c30": {"q": "Tumhara extraction system do document types process karta hai: standard monthly reports (processing ke baad archive) aur urgent exception reports (receipt ke 30 minutes ke andar business alerts trigger karne zaroori). Dono same JSON schema use karte hain. Tum API costs minimize karna chahte ho latency requirements meet karte hue.\n\nProcessing pipeline ko kaise architect karna chahiye?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Standard reports ko Batch API pe route karo 50% cost savings ke liye, aur urgent exception reports ko real-time Messages API pe route karo", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Saare documents queue karo aur hourly batches submit karo, urgent documents ko expedited handling ke liye flag karte hue jab batch results wapas aayein", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Saare documents ko real-time Messages API me submit karo consistent processing latency ensure karne ke liye document types ke across", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Saare documents ko Batch API me `custom_ids` ke saath submit karo tracking ke liye. Jab results aayein, turant urgent documents process karo aur exceptions ke liye delayed alerts trigger karo", "c": false}], "e": "Standard reports (archived) Batch API se conform karte hain 50% cost save karne ke liye. Urgent exception reports ko 30 minutes ke andar alerts trigger karne chahiye isliye real-time Messages API use karna zaroori hai. Ye dono cost aur latency ke liye optimal architecture hai. Baaki: B) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | C) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | D) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai."}, "c61": {"q": "Tumhara extraction pipeline invoices process karta hai aur line items, subtotals, tax amounts, aur grand totals extract karta hai. Evaluation ke dauran, tumhe pata chalta hai ki 18% extractions me extracted line item amounts ka sum extracted grand total se match nahi karta — kabhi source document me OCR errors ki wajah se, kabhi model ki extraction mistakes ki wajah se. Downstream accounting systems mismatched totals wale records reject kar dete hain.\n\nExtraction reliability improve karne ka sabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Post-processing implement karo jo automatically line item amounts ko proportionally adjust kare jab unka sum stated total se match na kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek \"calculated_total\" field add karo jaha model extracted line items sum kare ek \"stated_total\" field ke saath. Values differ karne pe records ko human review ke liye flag karo", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Few-shot examples add karo jo invoices demonstrate karein jaha extracted line items correctly stated total tak sum hote hain, model ko mathematically consistent extractions produce karne encourage karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Line items aur totals ko independently extract karo, phir ek separate validation model use karo discrepancies reconcile karne ke liye ye determine karke ki kaunse extracted values sabse likely correct hain", "c": false}], "e": "`calculated_total` aur `stated_total` dono capture karna discrepancy ko ek first-class signal bana deta hai — uniformly dono OCR errors aur extraction mistakes detect karta hai, aur sirf 18% mismatched records ko human review pe route karta hai. Auto-adjust aur reconciliation model dono silently accounting system ke liye incorrect data fabricate/hide karte hain. Baaki: A) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | C) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte. | D) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga."}, "c71": {"q": "Tumhara invoice extraction strict JSON schemas ke saath tool use karta hai. JSON syntax errors kabhi nahi hote, lekin 12% extractions semantic validation fail hoti hain — jaise, line item amounts extracted total tak nahi jaate, ya vendor IDs valid formats se match nahi karte. Ye failures currently manual review pe route hoti hain.\n\nAccuracy maintain karte hue manual review volume kam karne ka sabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Zyada strict schema constraints add karo detailed field descriptions ke saath model ko shuru se hi invalid values generate karne se rokne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Validation fail hone pe extraction ko 3 baar tak retry karo, pehla result accept karo jo validation pass kare", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Post-processing logic implement karo jo common errors automatically correct kare, jaise totals ko line items se recalculate karna jab sums match na karein", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Jab validation fail ho, ek follow-up request karo document, extraction, aur validation errors ke saath model correction ke liye", "c": true}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai ki jab validation fail ho, ek follow-up request karo document, extraction, aur validation errors ke saath model correction ke liye. Ye output ko required structure ke saath aligned rakhne aur downstream parsing ya validation failures kam karne ka sabse reliable tareeka hai. Baaki: A) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | B) Ye galat hai kyunki retry khud se underlying cause resolve nahi karta jab tak failure clearly transient na ho. | C) Ye phir bhi critical decision ko model discretion pe chhod deta hai, jo exactly wahi hai jo scenario keh raha hai fail ho raha hai."}, "c72": {"q": "Tumhara system calendar invitations se event details extract karna zaroori hai aur JSON output karna zaroori hai jo strictly ek schema ke saath conform kare title, date, time, location, aur attendees ke fields ke saath. Downstream koi bhi malformed ya non-conformant JSON reject kar deta hai.\n\nKaunsa approach sabse reliable schema compliance deta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Apne prompt me detailed JSON formatting instructions aur target schema include karo, phir Claude ke text response ko JSON ke roop me parse karo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek tool define karo apne target schema ko input parameters ke roop me use karke aur Claude se use extracted data ke saath call karwao", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Instructions jaise \"Output only valid JSON matching the schema exactly\" append karo aur retry logic implement karo JSON parsing fail hone pe dobara prompt karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Claude ke response ko ek opening brace ke saath pre-fill karo JSON output force karne ke liye, phir response ko complete aur parse karo", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai ek tool define karna apne target schema ko input parameters ke roop me use karke aur Claude se use extracted data ke saath call karwana. Ye output ko required structure ke saath aligned rakhne aur downstream parsing ya validation failures kam karne ka sabse reliable tareeka hai. Baaki: A) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | C) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | D) Ye phir bhi fragile text-generation behavior pe rely karta hai, structure ko zyada reliable tarike se enforce karne ki bajaye."}, "c73": {"q": "Tumhara extraction system 12 fields aur detailed descriptions wale ek JSON schema ke saath `tool_use` use karta hai, complete tool definition ke liye approximately 2,500 tokens. 150K tokens se kam wale documents process karne se 98% accuracy milti hai. 175-190K tokens wale documents ke liye, accuracy girke 71% ho jaati hai, final third se information consistently miss hoti hai. Model ka context window 200K tokens hai.\n\nSabse likely cause kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "8-10 fields se zyada wale schemas parameter generation ke dauran decision complexity badha dete hain, extraction accuracy kam karte hue document length se independently", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Tool definitions input context tokens consume karte hain. System prompts aur document content ke saath combine hokar, total context limit ke close aa jaata hai, end-of-document processing degrade karte hue", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Bohot lambe documents model ki effective attention span ko exceed karte hain chahe context limits kuch bhi hon, prompt instructions se door content ke liye accuracy degradation cause karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Model attention ko input length ke across proportionally distribute karta hai, jisse woh fields jo sirf ek baar document ke end ke paas mention hote hain unhe insufficient processing focus milta hai", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai ye samajhna ki tool definitions input context tokens consume karte hain. System prompts aur document content ke saath combine hokar, total context limit ke close aa jaata hai, end-of-document processing degrade karte hue. Ye output ko required structure ke saath aligned rakhne aur downstream parsing ya validation failures kam karne ka sabse reliable tareeka hai. Baaki: A) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | C) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | D) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai."}, "c74": {"q": "Extraction pipeline alag-alag types ke documents receive karta hai — kuch invoices hain, kuch contracts hain, aur kuch receipts hain. Tumne separate extraction tools define kiye hain, har ek apne khud ke schema ke saath document type ke hisaab se tailored. Testing ke dauran, tum observe karte ho ki `tool_choice: \"auto\"` ke saath, Claude kabhi-kabhi conversational text return karta hai ek extraction tool call karne ki jagah, downstream parsing failures cause karte hue. Tumhe guaranteed structured output chahiye document type pehle se jaane bina.\n\nSabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "`tool_choice: \"any\"` set karo saare extraction tools defined ke saath", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek preliminary classification call add karo, phir ek second call karo `tool_choice` ko identified extraction tool pe force karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "`tool_choice: \"auto\"` rakho system prompt instructions ke saath jo tool use require karein", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Saare document types ko ek single unified-schema extraction tool me consolidate karo aur us tool ko force karo", "c": false}], "e": "Jab tumhe guaranteed structured output chahiye lekin document type upfront nahi pata, sabse reliable approach ek two-step flow hai: pehle classify karo, phir `tool_choice` ko correct extractor pe force karo. Selection ko auto pe chhodna phir bhi conversational responses allow karta hai, jabki sab kuch ek giant schema me collapse karna usually precision hurt karta hai. Baaki: B) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | C) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | D) Sab kuch ek path me collapse karna precision kam karta hai aur usually system ko control karna zyada mushkil banata hai, aasan nahi."}, "c75": {"q": "Monitoring dikhati hai ki 12% extractions Pydantic validation fail hoti hain specific errors ke saath jaise \"expected float for quantity, got '2 to 3'\". In requests ko bina modification retry karna failures produce karta hai.\n\nIn validation failures se recover karne ka sabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Temperature ko 0 set karo output variability eliminate karne ke liye aur consistent formatting ensure karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek follow-up request bhejo jisme validation error include ho, model se apna output correct karne ko pooch te hue", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek secondary pipeline implement karo ek larger model tier use karke un documents ko reprocess karne ke liye jo validation fail karte hain", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Source documents ko pre-process karo problematic formats ko standardize karne ke liye extraction ke liye bhejne se pehle", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai ek follow-up request bhejna jisme validation error include ho, model se apna output correct karne ko pooch te hue. Ye agent ko failure ke baare me clearer signals deta hai taaki woh sahi recovery action choose kar sake, blindly retry karne ya bohot jaldi escalate karne ki bajaye. Baaki: A) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | C) Model size badalna cost ya quality affect kar sakta hai, lekin ye is scenario me root cause ko directly address nahi karta. | D) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga."}, "c78": {"q": "Tumhara home renovation planning assistant ek system prompt use karta hai jo ek expert contractor persona define karta hai specific guidelines ke saath: hamesha budget ke baare me poochho, multiple price points pe alternatives suggest karo, aur timeline requirements confirm karo. Testing ke dauran, responses turns 1-4 ke liye in guidelines ko follow karte hain, lekin turn 7 tak, assistant generic advice deta hai budget ya timeline ke baare me pooche bina. Conversation total sirf 2,500 tokens hai.\n\nSabse likely cause kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Assistant ki accumulated responses system prompt ke influence ko dilute kar rahi hain", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "System prompts sirf initial behavior establish karte hain aur saare turns ke across persist nahi hote", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "System prompt instructions pe model ka attention naturally weaken ho jaata hai jaise-jaise turns accumulate hote hain", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "System prompt sirf first API request ke saath bheja jaata hai", "c": false}], "e": "Is case me conversation context window ke against abhi bhi short hai, isliye error token limit se nahi aa raha. Sabse likely problem ye hai ki system prompts ka influence dilute ho jaata hai jaise-jaise conversation history accumulate hoti hai, model ko initial guidelines follow karne me kam strict banate hue. Baaki: B) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | C) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | D) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c80": {"q": "QA testing ke dauran, tum notice karte ho ki Claude tumhare system prompt guidelines ko pehle 10-15 turns me consistently follow karta hai, lekin turn 25-30 tak, responses deviate hone lagte hain — informal tone use karna jab formality specify ki gayi thi, kabhi-kabhi required formatting skip karna, ya woh information types provide karna jo guidelines restrict karti hain. Conversation length context limits ke andar hi hai (typically 30,000 tokens out of 200,000 available).\n\nExtended conversations ke throughout consistent behavior maintain karne ka sabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Behavioral guidelines ko system prompt se first user message me move karo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "20 turns ke baad automatically ek naya conversation shuru karo, prior context ka ek summary pass karte hue continuity maintain karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "User-role messages insert karo jo critical guidelines ko natural conversation breakpoints pe reinforce karein, especially complex requests se pehle", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Post-response validation implement karo jo har response ko regenerate kare jab tak woh specified guidelines conform na kare", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai user-role messages insert karna jo critical guidelines ko natural conversation breakpoints pe reinforce karein, especially complex requests se pehle. Ye context ko zyada deliberately manage karta hai taaki model sabse important information available rakhe bina brittle long-history recall pe depend kiye. Baaki: A) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | B) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | D) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai."}, "c84": {"q": "Tumhare conversational AI tutor ka ek 2,800-token system prompt hai jisme teaching methodology, persona guidelines, aur different proficiency levels ke explanations adapt karne ke detailed written instructions hain. User testing reveal karti hai ki 12 turns se zyada wale conversations me (approximately 4,000 tokens conversation history), assistant increasingly proficiency-adaptation guidelines ignore karta hai, learner ke stated level ke bawajood intermediate-level explanations pe default karte hue.\n\nExtended conversations me in guidelines ka consistent adherence ensure karne ka sabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Proficiency requirements ka ek condensed reminder conversation me inject karo ek system message ke roop me har 4-5 turns pe", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Verbose proficiency guidelines ko few-shot examples se replace karo jo har proficiency level pe appropriate responses demonstrate karein, vocabulary, complexity, aur explanation depth me concrete differences dikhaate hue", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Har assistant response ke baad, ek separate API call karo evaluate karne ke liye ki kya difficulty level learner ke profile se match karta hai, unaligned responses regenerate karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "System prompt ko restructure karo proficiency-adaptation rules ko ek clearly-marked final section me rakhne ke liye turant conversation history shuru hone se pehle", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai verbose proficiency guidelines ko few-shot examples se replace karna jo har proficiency level pe appropriate responses demonstrate karein, vocabulary, complexity, aur explanation depth me concrete differences dikhaate hue. Ye context ko zyada deliberately manage karta hai taaki model sabse important information available rakhe bina brittle long-history recall pe depend kiye. Baaki: A) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | C) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | D) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c91": {"q": "System ko uploaded resumes se candidate information (name, contact details, skills, work experience, education) extract karna zaroori hai. Extracted data ko strictly ek predefined JSON schema ke saath conform karna zaroori hai, kyunki missing required fields ya incorrect data types downstream validation failures cause karengi.\n\nClaude ke output ko consistently schema ke saath match karwane ka sabse reliable approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Claude ke text response ko regex patterns se parse karo JSON objects extract karne ke liye, malformed responses ke liye retry logic use karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Do separate API calls karo — pehle information ko text ke roop me extract karo, phir Claude se us text ko JSON ke roop me format karne ko poocho", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek tool define karo ek input schema ke saath jo tumhari required JSON structure se match kare aur Claude ke `tool_use` response se data extract karo", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "System prompt me detailed JSON formatting instructions aur ek template example include karo, Claude se sirf valid JSON output karne ko poochte hue", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai ek tool define karna ek input schema ke saath jo tumhari required JSON structure se match kare aur Claude ke `tool_use` response se data extract karna. Ye output ko required structure ke saath aligned rakhne aur downstream parsing ya validation failures kam karne ka sabse reliable tareeka hai. Baaki: A) Ye galat hai kyunki retry khud se underlying cause resolve nahi karta jab tak failure clearly transient na ho. | B) Ye phir bhi fragile text-generation behavior pe rely karta hai, structure ko zyada reliable tarike se enforce karne ki bajaye. | D) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c95": {"q": "Tumhara pipeline ek tool use karta hai `extract_metadata` naam ka ek JSON schema ke saath paper details ke liye. Tumne `lookup_citations` aur `verify_doi` tools bhi enrichment ke liye define kiye hain. Testing ke dauran, tum notice karte ho ki jab users requests include karte hain jaise \"metadata extract karo aur mujhe batao ki kitni citations hain,\" Claude kabhi-kabhi `lookup_citations` pehle call kar leta hai, jo fail hoti hai kyunki use woh DOI chahiye jo `extract_metadata` provide karti.\n\nStructured metadata extraction ko hamesha pehle ensure karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Pipeline ke har API call ke liye `tool_choice` ko `{\"type\": \"tool\", \"name\": \"extract_metadata\"}` set karo, ensure karte hue ki Claude hamesha metadata extract kare kisi bhi enrichment se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "`tool_choice` ko \"any\" set karo taaki Claude ko koi tool use karna hi pade, system prompt instructions ke saath combine karte hue `extract_metadata` ko prioritize karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "`tool_choice` ko \"auto\" set karo aur tool definitions ko reorder karo taaki `extract_metadata` tools array me pehle appear kare, kyunki Claude earlier-listed tools ko prioritize karta hai", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "`tool_choice` ko `{\"type\": \"tool\", \"name\": \"extract_metadata\"}` set karo aur enrichment requests ko subsequent turns me process karo extracted metadata receive karne ke baad", "c": true}], "e": "`tool_choice`=specific-tool deterministically `extract_metadata` ko first turn pe force karta hai. Phir tum control wapas 'auto' ko de dete ho model ko citations/DOI enrichment metadata context me hone ke saath use karne dete hue. Baaki: A) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | B) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | C) Ye phir bhi critical decision ko model discretion pe chhod deta hai, jo exactly wahi hai jo scenario keh raha hai fail ho raha hai."}, "c102": {"q": "Tumhe ek date validation check add karna hai ensure karne ke liye ki event dates future me hon. Isके liye ek existing function me ek single file me ek conditional statement add karna hai.\n\nSabse appropriate approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Plan mode me jao analyze karne ke liye ki validation reservation flow ke doosre parts ko kaise impact kar sakta hai", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Pehle plan mode me jao ek detailed implementation strategy banane ke liye change karne se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Direct execution use karo change karne ke liye", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Extended thinking mode enabled ke saath shuru karo validation logic ke baare me thorough reasoning ensure karne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai direct execution use karna change karne ke liye. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai."}, "c114": {"q": "Tumhara publish article tool ek external CMS API call karta hai jo kabhi-kabhi transient errors (network timeouts, 503s) aur non-transient errors (403 permission denied, 422 validation failure) return karta hai. Currently, har error directly agent ko return hoti hai, jisse agent non-transient errors retry karta hai aur un failures pe turns waste karta hai jo kabhi succeed nahi hongi.\n\nTool implementation aur agent ke beech error-handling responsibility ko kaise partition karna chahiye?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Saare errors ko detailed context ke saath turant agent ko surface karo, aur agent ko decide karne do ki kaunse errors retry karne hain aur kitni baar — tool implementation ko stateless aur simple rakhte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Tool ke andar saare errors handle karo: har error type ke liye exponential backoff ke saath retries implement karo, aur sirf ek fixed sankhya retry attempts exhaust hone ke baad hi failure agent ko surface karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek universal error handler implement karo jo saare exceptions catch kare aur ek generic \"tool unavailable — try again later\" message return kare, agent ko error complexity se shield karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Transient errors (timeouts, 503s) ko automatic retries ke saath tool implementation ke andar handle karo, aur non-transient errors (permission denied, validation failures) ko descriptive messages ke saath agent ko surface karo taaki woh corrective action le sake", "c": true}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai transient errors (timeouts, 503s) ko automatic retries ke saath tool implementation ke andar handle karna, aur non-transient errors (permission denied, validation failures) ko descriptive messages ke saath agent ko surface karna taaki woh corrective action le sake. Ye agent ko failure ke baare me clearer signals deta hai taaki woh sahi recovery action choose kar sake, blindly retry karne ya bohot jaldi escalate karne ki bajaye. Baaki: A) Retry sirf tab madad karta hai jab problem transient ho; ye khud se ek design ya classification problem fix nahi karta. | B) Retry sirf tab madad karta hai jab problem transient ho; ye khud se ek design ya classification problem fix nahi karta. | C) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga."}, "c117": {"q": "Tumhara document extraction tool ML models use karta hai invoice fields (vendor, amount, date) extract karne ke liye. Models har extracted field ke liye confidence scores (0.0-1.0) return karte hain. Production me, tum observe karte ho: (1) agent low-confidence extractions ke saath aage badhta hai jo 23% baar incorrect hoti hain, aur (2) agent unnecessary human review request karta hai 31% extractions ke liye jo actually correct thi.\n\nTool ke output ko kaise restructure karna chahiye?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Saare fields ke across ek aggregate extraction quality score compute karo aur use extracted values ke saath return karo. Ek text summary include karo jo overall extraction reliability describe kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Fields ko unke raw confidence scores ke saath return karo aur apne system prompt me detailed few-shot examples add karo jo dikhaye ki different confidence ranges ko kaise interpret karein aur kab human review request karein", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Fields ko confidence scores ke saath return karo, saath me ek `requires_review` boolean jo tumhare tested confidence thresholds use karke compute kiya gaya ho, ek `review_reasons` array ke saath jo explain kare ki kaunse fields ne review trigger kiya", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Fields ko confidence thresholds ke basis pe verified aur needs_verification objects me organized karke return karo", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai fields ko confidence scores ke saath return karna, saath me ek `requires_review` boolean jo tumhare tested confidence thresholds use karke compute kiya gaya ho, ek `review_reasons` array ke saath jo explain kare ki kaunse fields ne review trigger kiya. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: B) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte."}, "c126": {"q": "Tumhara system 3 hafton se chal raha hai aur human reviewers ne 847 extractions correct ki hain. Analysis ek recurring pattern reveal karti hai: jab recipes informal measurements use karti hain jaise \"a handful\" ya \"a splash,\" model ya toh specific amounts invent kar deta hai ya fields empty chhod deta hai — jo saari corrections ka 23% account karta hai.\n\nExtraction accuracy improve karne ke liye is feedback ko kaise use karna chahiye?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Apna JSON schema update karo ek \"measurement_type\" enum field add karne ke liye (precise/informal)", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek post-processing layer implement karo jo pattern matching use kare source text me informal measurement phrases detect karne ke liye aur values automatically populate kare jab extraction empty ho", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Apne prompt me few-shot examples add karo jo informal measurements ka correct handling demonstrate karein — unhe verbatim extract karte hue convert ya omit karne ki bajaye", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "847 corrected extractions pe model ko fine-tune karo", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai apne prompt me few-shot examples add karna jo informal measurements ka correct handling demonstrate karein — unhe verbatim extract karte hue convert ya omit karne ki bajaye. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: A) Ye phir bhi fragile text-generation behavior pe rely karta hai, structure ko zyada reliable tarike se enforce karne ki bajaye."}, "c128": {"q": "Tumhara automated reviewer ek single prompt use karta hai jo security issues, API design, aur business logic correctness cover karta hai. Tumhari evaluation suite strong recall findings (82%) dikhati hai lekin quiz scoring me business logic edge cases ke liye poor recall (34%). Jab tum logic bugs ke few-shot examples prompt me add karte ho, logic recall 41% ho jaata hai lekin API design recall girke 68% ho jaata hai.\n\nDono categories ke across detection improve karne ke liye is trade-off ko kaise address karein?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Sirf changed files aur surrounding code ki jagah poora repository context ke roop me provide karo, model ko business logic ki deeper visibility dete hue", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Few-shot examples ko ek detailed checklist se replace karo specific logic edge cases verify karne ke liye, jaise score calculation ya grading thresholds me division-by-zero", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Review ko separate focused prompts me split karo — ek security aur API design ke liye, doosra business logic ke liye — har ek apne dedicated examples ke saath, phir posting se pehle findings combine karo", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Ek zyada capable model tier pe upgrade karo, kyunki uski stronger reasoning dono concern types ko ek single prompt me handle kar legi aur recall trade-off eliminate kar degi", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai review ko separate focused prompts me split karna — ek security aur API design ke liye, doosra business logic ke liye — har ek apne dedicated examples ke saath, phir posting se pehle findings combine karna. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: B) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte. | D) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c134": {"q": "Tumhari team 50,000 legacy legal contracts se structured data extract kar rahi hai do-hafte ki deadline ke andar. 500 sample documents ke saath initial testing dikhati hai ki 82% pehli try me JSON schema pass kar jaate hain, jabki baaki 18% diverse issues ki wajah se fail hote hain — missing required fields, malformed dates, aur incorrectly identified parties. Jo documents fail hote hain unhe usually extraction succeed hone se pehle apne specific failure modes ko target karne wale refinements chahiye hote hain.\n\nKaunsi batch processing strategy deadline meet karte hue sabse cost-efficient hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "2,000 sample documents ko real-time API se process karo failure patterns identify karke prompts refine karne ke liye, phir saare 50,000 ko optimized prompts ke saath batch process karo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Saare 50,000 documents ke liye real-time API use karo kyunki batch API ka 24-hour processing window unacceptable deadline risk create karta hai", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Documents ko 10 sequential batches me split karo har ek 5,000 ka, batches ke beech results analyze karke prompts refine karte hue extraction quality progressively improve karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Saare 50,000 documents batch API se submit karo, phir failed extractions ko successive batches me submit karo — har batch ke beech prompts refine karte hue — jab tak saare documents validation pass na kar lein", "c": true}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai saare 50,000 documents batch API se submit karna, phir failed extractions ko successive batches me submit karna — har batch ke beech prompts refine karte hue — jab tak saare documents validation pass na kar lein. Ye output ko required structure ke saath aligned rakhne aur downstream parsing ya validation failures kam karne ka sabse reliable tareeka hai. Baaki: A) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | B) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | C) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c135": {"q": "Ek updated system prompt deploy karne ke baad jo response quality improve karta hai, kai hafton ke multi-session conversations wale users report karte hain ki assistant ab apne earlier statements se contradict karta hai aur ek noticeably different communication style rakhta hai. Naye users ko ye issues face nahi hote.\n\nIse resolve karne ka best approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Sessions resume hone pe ek transition message add karo explain karte hue ki assistant update hua hai aur behavior different ho sakta hai", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Existing conversations ke summaries ko naye prompt use karke regenerate karo aur stored histories replace karo past context ko current behavior ke saath align karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Naye system prompt me instructions add karo jo assistant ko direct karein conversation history me kisi bhi prior statement ke saath consistency maintain karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "System prompts ko version karo aur har conversation ko us prompt version se associate karo jiske under woh shuru hui thi, updates ko sirf naye conversations pe apply karte hue", "c": true}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai system prompts ko version karna aur har conversation ko us prompt version se associate karna jiske under woh shuru hui thi, updates ko sirf naye conversations pe apply karte hue. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: B) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | C) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c142": {"q": "Tumhara fitness coaching assistant ek system prompt use karta hai detailed conditional logic ke saath: \"Agar user beginner hone ka mention kare, step-by-step form instructions provide karo. Agar woh 'progressive overload' ya 'superset' term use kare, concisely respond karo. Agar woh injury history ke baare me pooche, hamesha physician consult karne recommend karo.\" Evaluation ke dauran, tumhe pata chalta hai ki assistant explicit expertise declarations ke liye correct hai lekin struggle karta hai jab users clearly apna level state nahi karte — aksar overly detailed responses pe default karte hue technical terms jaise contextual cues ke bawajood.\n\nKaunsa system prompt change implicit expertise signals pick up na karne wali is failure ko sabse directly address karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Additional expertise signals cover karne ke liye zyada conditional branches add karo, jaise \"Agar user specific rep ranges mention kare ya periodization ke baare me pooche, advanced treat karo\"", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek pre-conversation intake implement karo jo users se apna experience level rate karne ko kahe, phir us rating ko system prompt me context ke roop me inject karo saare subsequent responses ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Zyaadatar conditionals ko ek general principle se replace karo: \"Explanation depth ko user expertise se match karne ke liye adapt karo, unki terminology mirror karte hue.\" Sirf safety-critical conditional consultations ke baare me rakho", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Model ke liye ek explicit instruction add karo jo use experience level ke baare me ek clarifying question poochne ko kahe jab bhi user ki expertise unke first message se immediately clear na ho", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai zyaadatar conditionals ko ek general principle se replace karna: \"Explanation depth ko user expertise se match karne ke liye adapt karo, unki terminology mirror karte hue.\" Sirf safety-critical conditional consultations ke baare me rakho. Ye agent ko failure ke baare me clearer signals deta hai taaki woh sahi recovery action choose kar sake, blindly retry karne ya bohot jaldi escalate karne ki bajaye. Baaki: A) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | B) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | D) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga."}, "c146": {"q": "Tumhara portfolio value tool user ke investment portfolio ki total value return karta hai. Tum decide kar rahe ho ki explicit fields wali ek structured JSON object return karein ya information ko ek formatted text string ke roop me return karein.\n\nDefined fields ke saath structured output use karne ka primary advantage kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Structured JSON natural language se significantly kam tokens consume karta hai, API costs substantially kam karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Structured JSON model dwara deterministically process hota hai, values extract karte waqt accuracy significantly improve karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Agent free form text parse kiye bina reliably specific values extract kar sakta hai, subsequent operations me errors kam karte hue", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "JSON schemas automatically validate karte hain ki underlying API ne correct data return kiya hai agent process karne se pehle", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai ye samajhna ki agent free form text parse kiye bina reliably specific values extract kar sakta hai, subsequent operations me errors kam karte hue. Ye output ko required structure ke saath aligned rakhne aur downstream parsing ya validation failures kam karne ka sabse reliable tareeka hai. Baaki: A) Ye phir bhi fragile text-generation behavior pe rely karta hai, structure ko zyada reliable tarike se enforce karne ki bajaye. | B) Ye phir bhi fragile text-generation behavior pe rely karta hai, structure ko zyada reliable tarike se enforce karne ki bajaye. | D) Choice ko auto pe chhodna phir bhi critical decision ko usi jagah rakhta hai jo already fail ho rahi hai."}, "c149": {"q": "System product reviews process karta hai tool use ke saath ek defined schema ke saath: rating (integer 1-5), pros (string array), cons (string array), aur overall_sentiment (enum: positive, negative, mixed). Testing brief ya ambiguous reviews (~20% dataset) ke saath do issues reveal karti hai: (1) reviews jaise \"Great product!\" ke liye, Claude specific pros aur cons fabricate karta hai indicate karne ki jagah ki ye information explicitly stated nahi hai, aur (2) sarcastic reviews jaise \"Well that was... interesting\" ke liye, Claude sentiment arbitrarily choose kar leta hai kyunki ambiguous cases ke liye koi option nahi hai.\n\nKaunsa schema modification dono issues sabse acche se address karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek `extraction_confidence` field (0.0-1.0) add karo har value ke liye, aur outputs filter karo jaha koi confidence ek threshold se neeche gire", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "`pros` aur `cons` ko optional fields banao, aur \"neutral\" aur \"unclear\" ko sentiment enum me add karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "`pros`/`cons` ke liye empty arrays ko valid output ke roop me allow karo, aur \"unclear\" ko sentiment enum me add karo", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "`pros`/`cons` ke liye null values allow karo, aur \"unclear\" ko sentiment enum me add karo", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai `pros`/`cons` ke liye empty arrays ko valid output ke roop me allow karna, aur \"unclear\" ko sentiment enum me add karna. Ye output ko required structure ke saath aligned rakhne aur downstream parsing ya validation failures kam karne ka sabse reliable tareeka hai. Baaki: A) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | B) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai. | D) Ye approach bohot brittle hai un cases ke liye jaha output ko ek required structure ke saath consistently aligned rehna hai."}, "c155": {"q": "Tumhara `update_user_profile` tool ek `user_id` (required) aur ek optional `fields_to_update` object accept karta hai. Testing me, Claude frequently `user_id` omit kar deta hai ya incorrectly structured data pass karta hai.\n\nClaude ko samajhne me madad karne ke liye ki kaunse parameter values provide karne hain, sabse critical kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Clear parameter descriptions jo expected format explain karein, jaise \"user_id : UUID of the user to update (required)\"", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Verbose parameter names jo format hints encode karein, jaise `user_id_string_uuid_format`", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Detailed error responses jo explain karein ki invalid parameter values kyun reject hui", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Strict JSON Schema type constraints jo `user_id` ko required mark karein aur `fields_to_update` ko object type define karein", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai clear parameter descriptions jo expected format explain karein, jaise \"user_id : UUID of the user to update (required)\". Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: D) Ye phir bhi fragile text-generation behavior pe rely karta hai, structure ko zyada reliable tarike se enforce karne ki bajaye."}, "c5": {"q": "Tumhara agent 25 minutes se ek game engine ka rendering subsystem explore kar raha hai — shader code, buffer management, aur frame synchronization logic padhte hue. Ek engineer ab use ye samjhne ko kehta hai ki physics engine rendering ke saath kaise integrate hota hai collision debug overlays ke liye. Tum notice karte ho ki recent responses \"typical rendering patterns\" reference karte hain, us specific VulkanPipeline aur FrameGraph classes ki jagah jo usne pehle discover ki thi.\n\nSabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Current context me continue karo zyada targeted prompts ke saath jo specific classes ko naam se reference karein", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Key rendering findings ko summarize karo, phir physics exploration ke liye ek sub-agent spawn karo us summary ko uske initial context me daalte hue", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Physics independently explore karne ke liye ek sub-agent spawn karo, phir manually uski findings ko main conversation me accumulated rendering knowledge ke saath synthesize karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "`/clear` use karo context ko completely reset karne ke liye, phir project ki CLAUDE.md se file paths use karke physics exploration se fresh shuru karo", "c": false}], "e": "Generic \"typical rendering patterns\" responses ek lambi, bloated session se context degradation signal karte hain, isliye fix hai valuable rendering knowledge ko ek summary me compact karna aur use physics task ke liye ek fresh context wale sub-agent ko dena. Ye Anthropic ki context-management best practice follow karta hai — summarization plus clean contexts wale sub-agents — specific VulkanPipeline/FrameGraph findings preserve karte hue jin pe integration task depend karta hai, A (knowledge kho deta hai), B (sub-agent ke paas zaroori rendering context nahi hai aur synthesis degraded context me hoti hai), ya D (degraded context me continue karta hai) ke ulat. Baaki: A) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | D) Context reset karna useful information waste kar sakta hai aur khud se ek behtar investigation strategy create nahi karta."}, "c6": {"q": "Ek engineer agent se poochta hai ek function ke saare callers dhoondho use remove karne se pehle. Function ek core library me defined hai lekin wrapper modules ke through bhi expose hota hai jo domain-specific use ke liye function rename kar dete hain (jaise, library me `calculateTax`, orders module me `computeOrderTax` ban jaata hai).\n\nKaunsa exploration strategy sabse reliably saare callers identify karega?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Library aur wrapper modules ko padho function ke saare exposed names identify karne ke liye, phir har naam ko codebase ke across Grep karo", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Project documentation me function naam search karo intended usage patterns samajhne aur documented integration points tak navigate karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Grep use karo saari files dhoondhne ke liye jo library ya wrapper modules se import karti hain, phir har file padho check karne ke liye ki woh function use karti hai ya nahi", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Grep use karo function ke original naam ko codebase ke across search karne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "Kyunki function kai wrapper modules ke through alag naamon se expose hota hai, saare naam (original + wrappers me aliases) determine karna zaroori hai, phir har naam ko Grep karna. Sirf original naam Grep karna (D) wrappers use karne wale callers miss kar dega. Baaki: B) Documentation useful background de sakti hai, lekin ye code me har real caller ya usage path dhoondhne ka reliable tareeka nahi hai. | C) Surface-level searching yahan bohot narrow hai kyunki task ko simple text matching se zyada rich structural understanding chahiye. | D) Surface-level searching yahan bohot narrow hai kyunki task ko simple text matching se zyada rich structural understanding chahiye."}, "c7": {"q": "Testing ke dauran, tum observe karte ho ki extended exploration sessions me (30+ minutes), agent code structure ke baare me inconsistent answers dena shuru kar deta hai jo usne pehle discuss kiya tha. Engineers report karte hain ki unhe un modules ke baare me context repeat karna padta hai jo already explore ho chuke hain.\n\nIse address karne ka sabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Exploration shuru hone se pehle saari source files ka summaries banao, sirf in compressed representations ko context me load karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Automatic context clearing implement karo har 15 minutes pe ensure karne ke liye ki agent fresh, uncontaminated context ke saath shuru kare", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek higher-capacity model tier pe switch karo accumulated exploration data ke liye zyada context window space provide karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Agent se ek scratchpad file maintain karwao jo key findings record kare, subsequent questions ke liye use reference karte hue", "c": true}], "e": "Context window limited hai aur 30+ minutes ke baad, purani information push out ho jaati hai. Ek scratchpad file maintain karo key findings record karne ke liye taaki agent unhe reference kar sake bina context me memory pe depend kiye. Baaki: A) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | B) Context ko blindly clear karna useful information remove kar deta hai aur symptom treat karta hai, important cheez preserve karne ka behtar tareeka design karne ki jagah. | C) Model size badalna capacity ya cost affect karta hai, lekin ye question me describe kiya gaya workflow mistake directly fix nahi karta."}, "c9": {"q": "Ek engineer agent se poochta hai ek legacy payment processing module me error handling investigate karne ko jo 15 files ke across span karta hai. Pehli 8 files padhne ke baad, agent ki responses noticeably kam accurate ho rahi hain — woh pehle discovered code patterns bhool raha hai aur abhi tak saari test files locate nahi ki hain ya complete data flow trace nahi kiya hai.\n\nIs investigation ko complete karne ka sabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Baaki files explore karne ke liye ek subagent spawn karo, discovered patterns ka ek summary uske initial context ke roop me provide karte hue", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Grep use karo baaki files ke across specific function names search karne ke liye, context me load hone wala content kam karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ab tak ke findings ka ek summary ek file me document karo, phir ek naye context ke saath fresh shuru karo us summary ko reference ke roop me use karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "`/clear` se current context close karo aur fresh shuru karo, sirf sabse critical files ko dobara padhte hue", "c": false}], "e": "Jab agent bohot saari files padhne ke baad context kho raha hai, current findings ke ek summary ke saath ek naya subagent spawn karna investigation continue karne ka optimal tareeka hai. Main agent coordinate karta hai jabki subagent clean context ke saath explore karta hai. Baaki: B) Surface-level searching yahan bohot narrow hai kyunki task ko simple text matching se zyada rich structural understanding chahiye. | C) Fresh shuru karna useful context waste kar deta hai jo scenario preserve karna chahta hai, isliye underlying problem solve kiye bina cost add karta hai. | D) Fresh shuru karna useful context waste kar deta hai jo scenario preserve karna chahta hai, isliye underlying problem solve kiye bina cost add karta hai."}, "c11": {"q": "Tumhara agent ne ek complex service module analyze kiya hai — 23 source files padh ke, request flows trace karke, aur error handling patterns identify karke. Ek developer commit karne se pehle do testing strategies compare karna chahta hai: mocked external services wale end-to-end tests vs expected outputs capture karne wale snapshot tests. Unhe dono approaches independently develop karni hain trade-offs evaluate karne ke liye.\n\nSessions ko kaise manage karna chahiye?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Analysis session ki key findings ko ek file me export karo, phir do naye sessions banao jo is file ko reference karein", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Original session me continue karo, pehle end-to-end tests develop karke, phir snapshot tests sequentially", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Do fresh sessions shuru karo, har ek ko relevant source files dobara padhne dete hue shuru karne se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Analysis session ko `fork_session` enabled ke saath resume karo, har testing strategy ke liye ek separate branch banate hue", "c": true}], "e": "`fork_session` usi analysis point se do branches banane deta hai, har branch ek independent testing strategy develop karta hai ek doosre ko affect kiye bina, jabki analysis session ka poora context intact rehta hai. Baaki: A) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | B) Dono paths ko sequentially handle karna branches ko separate rakhne ka point miss kar deta hai aur comparison ya independent exploration ko harder banata hai. | C) Fresh shuru karna useful context waste kar deta hai jo scenario preserve karna chahta hai, isliye underlying problem solve kiye bina cost add karta hai."}, "c12": {"q": "Tumhara codebase exploration tool session IDs store karta hai taaki engineers investigations ko work sessions ke across continue kar sakein. Ek engineer ne kal ek ghanta lagakar ek legacy authentication module analyze kiya, uski architecture aur dependencies ke baare me context build karte hue. Woh aaj continue karna chahte hain. Session ID valid hai, lekin version control dikhata hai ki agent ne pehle padhi 12 me se 3 files raat ko ek teammate ke merge se modify hui thi.\n\nKaunsa approach efficiency aur accuracy ka sabse acha balance karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Session resume karo agent ko changed files ke baare me inform kiye bina", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Session resume karo aur agent ko batao ki targeted re-analysis ke liye kaunsi specific files change hui hain", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek fresh session shuru karo ensure karne ke liye ki agent current codebase state ke saath kaam kare bina stale assumptions ke", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Session resume karo aur turant agent se saari 12 pichli analyzed files dobara padhwao", "c": false}], "e": "Session resume + changed files ki notification sabse balanced tareeka hai: 9 files ka context unchanged rakho (costly re-reads avoid karo), aur agent ko naye changes ke baare me update karo accuracy ensure karne ke liye. Baaki: A) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | C) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | D) Fresh shuru karna useful context waste kar deta hai jo scenario preserve karna chahta hai, isliye underlying problem solve kiye bina cost add karta hai."}, "c35": {"q": "Production reviews final reports me uncertainty ke inconsistent handling reveal karti hain. Kabhi confidence calibrations ko standardized uncertainty expressions me synthesize kiya jaata hai, kabhi results vague estimates produce karte hain bina clear methodology ke.\n\nKaunsa system-level improvement is inconsistency ko sabse acche se address karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek confidence calibration layer implement karo jaha synthesis agent uncertainty expressions ko standardized probability representations (0.0-1.0) me normalize kare, phir unke calibrated confidence ko weight kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Synthesis agent ko instruct karo ki woh explicit sections use kare confirmed findings ko contested analysis se separate karne ke liye, original source characterizations preserve karte hue", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek verification subagent add karo jo sources ke across findings cross-reference kare, sirf synthesis accept karte hue jo kam se kam do independent sources se corroborated ho", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Subagents ko configure karo ki woh sirf sufficient coverage breadth, source diversity, aur quality criteria wali findings report karein synthesis agent ko results pass karne se pehle", "c": false}], "e": "Report structure clearly confirmed findings ko un se separate karta hai jo controversial hain, jabki original context preserve karte hue — ye balance aur accuracy ensure karne ka tareeka hai bina kisi bhi case me bohot zyada hedge kiye."}, "c47": {"q": "25+ turns ke across ek billing dispute investigate karne ke baad, tumne identify kiya hai ki duplicate charges ek payment gateway timeout ki wajah se hue the jisne retry logic trigger kiya. Required refund ($847) tumhari $500 authorization limit se zyada hai. Tumhe `escalate_to_human` call karna hai, aur human agent ke paas tumhari conversation transcript tak access nahi hoga.\n\nEffective resolution enable karne ke liye kaunsa context pass karna chahiye?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek structured summary: customer ID, root cause, refund amount, aur recommended action", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Sirf tumhara diagnosis aur refund amount", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Customer ka original complaint verbatim plus tool result excerpts jo duplicate transactions dikhaye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Poori conversation transcript saare tool results ke saath", "c": false}], "e": "Human agents ko quickly resolve karne ke liye kaafi information chahiye, lekin poori transcript ki zaroorat nahi. Customer ID, root cause, refund amount aur recommended action wala structured summary exactly wahi provide karta hai jo zaroori hai concise aur actionable tareeke se. Baaki: B) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | C) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | D) Poora transcript dump karna noise add karta hai aur agle actor ke liye key facts jaldi dhoondhna mushkil banata hai."}, "c48": {"q": "Tumhara agent ne ek customer ki return requests investigate karte waqt `lookup_order` kai baar call kiya hai. Har response me 40+ fields hain (items, shipping details, payment info, status history). Tool outputs ab conversation ke context ka majority represent karte hain. Customer do aur orders mention karta hai jinke baare me baat karna chahta hai.\n\nAdditional lookups karne se pehle sabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Saare tool responses ko ek vector database me semantic indexing ke saath move karo, relevant portions retrieve karte hue jaise conversation continue hoti hai", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Har existing order response se sirf return-relevant fields (items, purchase date, return window, status) extract karo, verbose details remove karte hue", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Existing tool output context modify kiye bina additional lookups ke saath aage badho", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Model se har order ke key details ka ek natural language summary generate karwao, structured responses ko prose descriptions se replace karte hue", "c": false}], "e": "Jab tool outputs zyaadatar context le lete hain, tumhe sirf return-relevant fields (items, purchase date, return window, status) rakhne ke liye trim karna hai lookups add karne se pehle. Context window ko free karta hai bina important information kho ye. Baaki: A) Ye infrastructure ya indirection add karta hai, lekin sawaal actually ek simpler coordination pattern choose karne ke baare me hai jo current workflow fit kare. | C) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | D) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai."}, "c49": {"q": "Ek customer bhejta hai: \"Ye frustrating hai. Maine apna issue do baar explain kiya hai aur kuch resolve nahi ho raha. Mujhe abhi ek real person se baat karni hai.\" Agent ne abhi tak unke account investigate karne ke liye koi tools call nahi ki hain.\n\nAgent ko kya karna chahiye?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Briefly explain karo ki agent kya help kar sakta hai aur issue quickly resolve karne ka offer do, sirf tab escalate karte hue jab customer apni request repeat kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Turant `escalate_to_human` call karo conversation history ke saath", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Frustration acknowledge karo aur specific issue samajhne ke liye ek targeted question poocho escalate karne se pehle", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Pehle `get_customer` aur `lookup_order` call karo account context gather karne ke liye, phir human agent ko escalate karo", "c": false}], "e": "Customer 'do baar' kehta hai lekin tumhare paas abhi context nahi hai. Ek empathetic question, intended hai tumhe pehli baar me hi resolve karne ka opportunity dene ke liye bina frustration incur kiye ya potential handoff delay kiye. Baaki: B) Escalation yahan bohot jaldi hai kyunki scenario ek behtar system behavior maang raha hai, primary fix ke roop me handoff nahi. | D) Escalation yahan bohot jaldi hai kyunki scenario ek behtar system behavior maang raha hai, primary fix ke roop me handoff nahi."}, "c50": {"q": "Tum escalation logic implement kar rahe ho ye decide karne ke liye ki agent ko kab `escalate_to_human` call karna chahiye. Tumhari team escalation trigger karne ke liye char alag approaches propose karti hai.\n\nKaunsa approach sabse reliably un cases identify karega jinhe genuinely human intervention chahiye?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Sentiment analysis implement karo jo frustration indicators monitor kare (negative language, repeated questions, exclamation marks) aur escalation trigger kare jab frustration score ek configured threshold se zyada ho", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek rules engine banao jo specific issue types, customer segments, aur product categories ko escalation decisions se map kare, model judgment calls ki zaroorat remove karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Agent ko configure karo teen consecutive tool calls ke baad escalate karne ke liye jo customer ke stated issue resolve karne me fail hon, ek reasonable attempt ensure karte hue human involve karne se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Agent ko instruct karo ki escalate kare jab customer ek human request kare, jab issue ko policy exceptions chahiye, ya jab agent meaningful progress na kar sake", "c": true}], "e": "Clear escalation conditions define karna (customer human request karta hai, policy exceptions chahiye, koi meaningful progress nahi) sabse comprehensive aur flexible approach hai. Rules engine (B) bohot rigid hai, sentiment analysis (A) itna reliable nahi hai, fixed retry count (C) bohot mechanical hai. Baaki: C) Escalation yahan bohot jaldi hai kyunki scenario ek behtar system behavior maang raha hai, primary fix ke roop me handoff nahi."}, "c51": {"q": "Tumhara agent ek billing dispute handle kar raha hai. `get_customer` aur `lookup_order` call karne ke baad, woh identify karta hai ki dispute ek promotional pricing error involve karta hai jise manager approval chahiye — agent ke authorization level se bahar.\n\nWorkflow ko is mid-process escalation ko kaise handle karna chahiye?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "`escalate_to_human` call karo sirf customer ka original message pass karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "`process_refund` se refund attempt karo phir bhi, sirf tab escalate karte hue jab system transaction reject kare", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek structured handoff compile karo customer details, order info, aur identified issue ke saath `escalate_to_human` call karne se pehle", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Poori conversation aur tool response history ek database me persist karo, phir ek reference ID ke saath `escalate_to_human` call karo", "c": false}], "e": "Mid-process escalation ko human agent ke liye kaafi context provide karna zaroori hai. Structured handoff compile karna customer details, order information aur identified issue ke saath ensure karta hai ki human agent ke paas resolve karne ke liye kaafi information hai bina shuru se dobara investigate kiye. Baaki: A) Escalation yahan bohot jaldi hai kyunki scenario ek behtar system behavior maang raha hai, primary fix ke roop me handoff nahi. | B) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | D) Escalation yahan bohot jaldi hai kyunki scenario ek behtar system behavior maang raha hai, primary fix ke roop me handoff nahi."}, "c52": {"q": "Ek billing dispute resolution ke dauran, tumhara agent successfully `get_customer` ke through customer info aur `lookup_order` ke through order details retrieve kar leta hai, lekin `process_refund` ke through refund process karne ki koshish karte waqt, tool ek timeout error return karta hai. Agent ke paas billing explain karne, refund eligibility confirm karne, aur refund eligibility verify karne ke liye kaafi information hai, lekin backend failure ki wajah se actually refund process nahi kar sakta.\n\nKaunsa approach first-contact resolution aur appropriate error handling ka sabse acha balance karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Turant ek human agent ko escalate karo kyunki refund action complete nahi ho sakta", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "`process_refund` ke liye exponential backoff ke saath automatic retries implement karo, conversation ko open rakhte hue jab tak refund successfully process na ho jaaye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Confirm karo ki refund process hoga aur conversation close karo, kyunki system ke paas ise automatically complete karne ke liye saari zaroori information hai", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Billing explain karo, refund eligibility confirm karo, system issue acknowledge karo jo immediate processing rok raha hai, aur escalation ya baad me retry offer karo", "c": true}], "e": "Woh partial value do jo tum de sakte ho (explanation + eligibility), failure ke baare me honest raho, aur customer ko human escalation ya retry ke beech choose karne do. Classic graceful degradation. Baaki: A) Escalation yahan bohot jaldi hai kyunki scenario ek behtar system behavior maang raha hai, primary fix ke roop me handoff nahi. | B) Ye phir bhi critical decision ko model discretion pe chhod deta hai, jo exactly wahi hai jo scenario keh raha hai fail ho raha hai. | C) Choice ko auto pe chhodna phir bhi critical decision ko usi jagah rakhta hai jo already fail ho rahi hai."}, "c55": {"q": "Ek customer likhta hai: \"Main is return pe kai dinon se back and forth kar raha hoon. Mujhe bas kisi aise se baat karni hai jo actually help kar sake.\" Agent ne `lookup_order` ke through confirm kar liya hai ki return straightforward hai — policy ke andar hai aur immediate processing ke liye eligible hai.\n\nAgent ko kya karna chahiye?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "`process_refund` ke through refund process karo underlying issue resolve karne ke liye, phir unhe inform karo ki complete ho gaya", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Poocho ki specifically pichli attempts me kya kaam nahi kiya, escalate ya automatically resolve karne ka decide karne se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Frustration acknowledge karo, unhe batao ki ye abhi resolvable hai, aur ise complete karne ya escalate karne ka offer do", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Customer ki request honor karne ke liye turant `escalate_to_human` call karo", "c": false}], "e": "Return eligible hai aur turant process ho sakta hai, lekin customer frustrated hai. Agent ko escalate (D) ya bina pooche process (A) karne ka decision nahi lena chahiye. Sabse acha approach hai frustration acknowledge karna, batana ki issue turant resolve ho sakta hai, aur customer ko choose karne dena. Baaki: B) Escalation yahan bohot jaldi hai kyunki scenario ek behtar system behavior maang raha hai, primary fix ke roop me handoff nahi. | D) Escalation yahan bohot jaldi hai kyunki scenario ek behtar system behavior maang raha hai, primary fix ke roop me handoff nahi."}, "c56": {"q": "Compliance require karti hai ki $500 se zyada wale refunds automatically ek human agent ko escalate hone chahiye — ye rule model discretion pe nahi chhoda ja sakta. Clear system prompt instructions ke bawajood, production logs dikhate hain ki agent kabhi-kabhi high-value refunds directly process kar deta hai (3% failure rate).\n\nGuaranteed compliance kaise achieve karein?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "System prompt ko emphatic language ke saath strengthen karo: \"CRITICAL POLICY: $500 se zyada refunds ko MUST human escalation trigger karna chahiye. Inhe kabhi bhi directly process mat karo.\"", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Prompt me few-shot examples add karo jo different refund amounts pe correct escalation behavior dikhaye ($400, $500, $600)", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Refund tool ko modify karo ek error return karne ke liye message ke saath \"Amount exceeds policy limit—please escalate\" jab threshold exceed ho", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Ek hook implement karo tool calls intercept karne ke liye; jab refund process amount $500 se zyada ho, use block karo aur human escalation invoke karo", "c": true}], "e": "Jab compliance mandatory hai aur model discretion pe nahi chhodi ja sakti, programmatic protection ko infrastructure level pe implement karna zaroori hai. Hook se tool calls intercept karna aur $500 se zyada refunds block karna guaranteed compliance deta hai, model behavior ya prompt interpretation se independent. Baaki: A) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | B) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte. | C) Escalation yahan bohot jaldi hai kyunki scenario ek behtar system behavior maang raha hai, primary fix ke roop me handoff nahi."}, "c57": {"q": "Ek customer ek hi session me teen alag issues raise karta hai: ek refund inquiry (turns 1-15), ek subscription question (turns 16-30), aur ek payment method update (turns 31-45). Turn 48 pe, customer poochta hai \"Mere refund ka kya hua?\" Conversation context limits ke close pahunch rahi hai.\n\nKaunsi strategy poori session me saare issues address karne ki agent ki ability ko sabse acche se maintain karti hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "MCP tools pe rely karo relevant information ko on-demand re-fetch karne ke liye jab customer earlier issues reference kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Structured issue data (order IDs, amounts, statuses) ko extract aur persist karo ek separate context layer me", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Sliding window context implement karo jo sabse recent 30 turns retain kare", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Earlier turns ko ek narrative description me summarize karo, active issue ke liye hi poori message history preserve karte hue", "c": true}], "e": "Progressive summarization already resolved topics ko compress karta hai jabki active thread ko verbatim rakhta hai — ye lambe multi-issue conversations ke liye classic pattern hai jo context limit ke close aa rahi hai. Baaki: A) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | B) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | C) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai."}, "c58": {"q": "Agent password reset karne se pehle ek multi-step process ke through customer identity verify karta hai. Testing ke dauran, tum notice karte ho ki customer ke third verification question ka answer dene ke baad, agent unse dobara unka naam poochta hai, jaise earlier exchange kabhi hua hi na ho.\n\nIs behavior ka sabse likely cause kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Verification tool har successful validation step ke baad agent ka internal state clear kar raha hai", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Claude ki memory retention default se sirf do conversational turns tak limited hai, use extend karne ke liye explicit configuration chahiye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Conversation history subsequent API requests me pass nahi ho rahi", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Prompt me instructions ki kami hai jo Claude ko batayein ki multiple exchanges ke across information yaad rakhe", "c": false}], "e": "Claude ke paas API calls ke beech koi inherent memory nahi hai. Agar agent dobara provide ki gayi information poochta hai, sabse common reason ye hai ki conversation history subsequent API requests ke dauran pass nahi hui thi. Prompt instructions (D) ya tool behavior (A) main cause nahi hain. Baaki: D) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c59": {"q": "Tumhara `process_refund` tool do types ke errors return karta hai: technical errors (\"503 Service Unavailable\", \"Connection timeout\") jo transient hain (5% calls), aur business errors (\"Order exceeds 30-day return window\", \"Item already refunded\") jo permanent hain (12% calls). Monitoring dikhati hai ki agent 3-4 turns waste karta hai business errors retry karke jo kabhi succeed nahi ho sakte. Currently, dono error types Claude ko sirf ek plain text message return karte hain.\n\nCustomer-facing response quality improve karte hue wasted retries kam karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek `check_refund_eligibility` tool add karo jo `process_refund` se pehle call hona zaroori ho business rule violations rokne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Few-shot examples add karo jo dikhaye ki retryable ko non-retryable errors se error message text parse karke kaise distinguish karein", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Structured error responses return karo `retryable: false` ke saath business errors ke liye aur Claude use karne ke liye ek customer-friendly explanation", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Sirf technical errors ke liye tool level pe automatic retry logic implement karo, business errors ko bina retries ke Claude ko pass karte hue", "c": false}], "e": "Business errors me `retryable: false` flag add karna Claude ko turant bina retry ke pata chalne deta hai, aur customer-friendly explanation customers se communicate karne ke liye. Retry (technical) vs no-retry (business) logic ko tool level pe separate karna sabse cleanest solution hai. Baaki: A) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | B) Ye galat hai kyunki retry khud se underlying cause resolve nahi karta jab tak failure clearly transient na ho. | D) Choice ko auto pe chhodna phir bhi critical decision ko usi jagah rakhta hai jo already fail ho rahi hai."}, "c60": {"q": "Ek customer apni initial session ke 4 hours baad usi billing dispute ke baare me wapas aata hai. Pichli 32-turn session me context hai: `lookup_status_result` messages jisme \"Status: Pending Refund\" hai aur pichle lookup results se significant tokens. Agent ko customer ko poori tarah answer dene ke liye prepared hona chahiye.\n\nKaunsa approach returning customers ko sabse reliably handle karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Poori conversation ke saath resume karo aur ek system prompt instruction add karo jo agent ko pending refund resolve karna prioritize karne ko kahe", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek naya session banao pichli interaction ke ek structured summary ke saath (issue type, resolution steps, current status), phir zaroorat pade toh fresh tool calls karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek naya session shuru karo, pichli interaction ka ek structured summary inject karo (issue type, resolution steps, current status), phir zaroorat pade toh fresh tool calls karo", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "State ke saath resume karo aur agent ko configure karo ki woh saare pichle `tool_results` messages automatically dobara call kare data freshness ensure karne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "4 hours ke baad, cached data stale ho sakta hai. Pichli interaction ke ek structured summary ke saath ek naya session shuru karna (issue type, taken steps, current status) zaroori context provide karta hai, jabki fresh tool calls data accuracy ensure karte hain. Baaki: A) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | B) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | D) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai."}, "c62": {"q": "Ek engineer tumhare agent se ek legacy payment processing module me untested code paths identify karne ko kehta hai jo 45 files ke across span karta hai. Pehli 8 source files padhne ke baad, agent ki responses noticeably kam accurate ho rahi hain — woh pehle discussed code patterns bhool raha hai aur abhi tak saari test files locate nahi ki hain ya critical payment flows trace nahi kiye hain.\n\nIs investigation ko complete karne ka sabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Full files padhne ki jagah specific function names search karne ke liye Grep use karo switch karo, baaki exploration ke liye context me load hone wala content kam karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Specific questions investigate karne ke liye subagents spawn karo (jaise \"payment processing ke liye saari test files dhoondo\", \"refund flow dependencies trace karo\") jabki main agent findings coordinate kare aur high-level understanding preserve kare", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Saare current findings ek summary report me document karo, context completely clear karo, phir us report ko investigation continue karne ke liye sole reference ke roop me use karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "`/clear` se context clear karo, phir selectively sirf sabse critical files ko dobara padho jo ab tak discover hui hain, key findings ko ek scratchpad file me likhte hue jo context resets ke beech persist kare", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse strong approach hai well-scoped investigations ko fresh context wale subagents ko delegate karna jabki main agent architectural overview rakhta hai. Ye system ko ek single context window ko overload kiye bina deep exploration continue karne deta hai, aur dono detailed findings aur high-level coordination preserve karta hai. Baaki: A) Surface-level searching yahan bohot narrow hai kyunki task ko simple text matching se zyada rich structural understanding chahiye. | C) Ek summary madad kar sakta hai, lekin ise sole source of truth banana detail strip kar deta hai jo abhi bhi accurate follow-up work ke liye chahiye ho sakti hai. | D) Fresh shuru karna useful context waste kar deta hai jo scenario preserve karna chahta hai, isliye underlying problem solve kiye bina cost add karta hai."}, "c67": {"q": "Currently isके liye content ko manually conversations me copy-paste karna padta hai. Team chahti hai ki agent is standard Jira ticket data ko directly access kare.\n\nSabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Jira ke API ko wrap karta hua ek custom MCP server banao tools ke saath jo specifically is team ke code review workflow ke liye design kiye gaye hon", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Jira tickets ko repository me markdown files me export karo jise agent Read tool use karke access kare", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek existing Jira MCP server integrate karo jo tickets, comments, aur metadata ko discoverable tool interfaces ke through expose kare", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Bash tool use karo curl ke saath Jira ke REST API call karne ke liye, authentication headers include karte hue aur JSON responses inline parse karte hue", "c": false}], "e": "Jira tickets jaise standard third-party service data ke liye, Anthropic ki recommended practice ek existing MCP server integrate karna hai, jo discoverable, typed tool interfaces managed authentication ke saath provide karta hai. Ek custom MCP server banana (A) standard ticket data ke liye unnecessary effort hai, markdown exports (B) stale ho jaate hain aur manual syncing chahte hain, aur ad-hoc curl calls (D) brittle hain aur credentials inline expose karte hain. Baaki: D) Ye phir bhi fragile text-generation behavior pe rely karta hai, structure ko zyada reliable tarike se enforce karne ki bajaye."}, "c68": {"q": "Ek critical bug production users ko affect kar raha hai. Error logs OrderProcessing module me exceptions dikhate hain ek clear stack trace ke saath jo ek specific area point karta hai, lekin tumne is module pe pehle kaam nahi kiya.\n\nSabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Direct execution use karo stack trace examine karne ke liye, relevant code padho, aur root cause identify hone ke baad ek fix implement karo", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Initial information gather karne ke liye direct execution se shuru karo, phir plan mode me switch karo ek comprehensive solution design karne ke liye implement karne se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Plan mode use karo error ko module ke design ke context me analyze karne ke liye, potential root causes enumerate karo, aur systematically fixes prioritize karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Plan mode me jao module ki architecture aur dependencies explore karne ke liye koi bhi fix attempt karne se pehle", "c": false}], "e": "Debugging adaptive hoti hai — har file jo tum padhte ho agle sabse useful step ko badal deti hai, isliye agent ko evidence follow karne do. Stack trace already directly failure ki taraf point karta hai, isliye direct execution (trace padho, relevant code padho, root cause identify hone ke baad fix karo) sabse fast, reliable path hai. Baaki: B) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | C) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | D) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga."}, "c69": {"q": "Automated review deploy karne ke baad, tum notice karte ho high precision lekin low recall — real bugs undetected slip ho rahe hain. Investigation reveal karti hai ki tumhara review prompt Claude ko instruct karta hai \"sirf high-confidence issues report karo jinke baare me tum certain ho\" aur \"not commenting ki taraf err karo.\" Developers low noise appreciate karte hain, lekin ek race condition jisne production outage cause kiya ek reviewed PR me visible tha aur unreported gaya.\n\nBug detection substantially improve karte hue false positive rates apni team ke liye manageable rakhne ka sabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Related test files, recent git history, aur module ke dependency graph ko diff ke saath include karke context window expand karo, Claude ko issue severity assess karne ke liye richer signals dete hue", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Conservative filtering instructions remove karo aur Claude ko prompt karo saare potential issues report karne ke liye, phir ek programmatic filter apply karo deduplicate karne aur un categories ko suppress karne ke liye jo historically false positives generate karti hain", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Detailed few-shot examples add karo jo bug categories demonstrate karein jo Claude ko flag karni chahiye — race conditions, null dereferences, error handling gaps — jabki high-confidence filtering instruction rakhte hue current precision levels maintain karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Review ko ek finding stage me split karo jaha Claude ka goal coverage hai — har potential issue ko confidence aur severity metadata ke saath flag karna — aur ek separate stage jo un findings ko threshold kare", "c": true}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai coverage ko filtering se separate karna. Review stage ko har plausible finding report karne do confidence aur severity metadata ke saath, phir baad ke stage me thresholding apply karo. Ye recall ko substantially improve karta hai bina team ko raw unfiltered output ko final review result ke roop me accept karne pe force kiye. Baaki: B) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | C) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte."}, "c76": {"q": "Teen mahine ke weekly sessions ke baad, tumhari conversation history 85,000 tokens tak badh gayi hai. Jab users poochte hain \"Isolation ke theme ke baare me humne kya conclude kiya tha?\", assistant generic literary analysis provide karta hai group ke specific insights pichli sessions se reference karne ki jagah. Discussions aksar pichli meetings ke conclusions pe build hoti hain, isliye narrative context maintain karna important hai.\n\nSabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Progressive summarization implement karo jaha older conversation blocks ko concise summaries se replace kiya jaaye jo explicitly key conclusions, decisions, aur recurring themes extract karein, recent exchanges verbatim rakhte hue", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Semantic embedding use karo poori conversation history index karne ke liye aur sirf relevant past exchanges retrieve karo har user query ke liye, linear conversation format ko retrieved segments se replace karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Rolling window truncation implement karo sirf sabse recent 25,000 tokens rakhne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Structured XML tags add karo significant discussion conclusions mark karne ke liye poori conversation history me", "c": false}], "e": "Jab ek conversation lambi ho jaati hai lekin phir bhi earlier conclusions pe depend karti hai, progressive summarization sabse balanced approach hai. Ye older discussion ko reusable takeaways me compress karta hai jabki recent exchanges verbatim preserve karta hai. Baaki: B) Poora transcript dump karna noise add karta hai aur agle actor ke liye key facts jaldi dhoondhna mushkil banata hai. | C) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | D) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai."}, "c77": {"q": "Tum ek feature implement kar rahe ho jaha users apni playlist preferences ko kai conversation turns ke through refine karte hain. Deploy karne ke baad, tum notice karte ho ki Claude ke responses wo reflect nahi karte jo usi conversation me pehle kaha gaya tha — jaise, ek user kehta hai ki use jazz pasand hai, lekin do messages baad Claude poochta hai ki unhe kaunse genres pasand hain.\n\nSabse likely cause kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Claude ko conversation memory maintain karne ke liye ek vector database connection chahiye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Conversation length se model ka context window exceed ho gaya hai", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Tumhari application `messages` array me prior messages include nahi kar rahi", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Claude API ko ek `session_id` parameter chahiye jo tumne configure nahi kiya hai", "c": false}], "e": "Agar Claude turant bhool jaata hai ki usi conversation me kuch turns pehle kya kaha gaya tha, usually iski wajah ye hoti hai ki application har API call me poori message history retransmit nahi karti. Claude requests ke across koi state maintain nahi karta agar application context dobara provide nahi karti. Baaki: A) Ye infrastructure add karta hai lekin question me describe kiya gaya failure mode directly solve nahi karta."}, "c79": {"q": "Users report karte hain ki extended conversations ke dauran, AI specific topics, examples, aur preferences ka track kho deta hai jo unhone session me pehle mention kiye the. Tumhari current implementation ek sliding window use karti hai jo sirf sabse recent 25 message pairs rakhti hai context limits ke andar rehne ke liye.\n\nContext size manage karte hue earlier conversation content ki awareness maintain karne ka sabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Poori conversation history pe vector similarity search implement karo, relevant past messages retrieve karte hue har user query ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Window size ko 50 message pairs tak badhao truncation se pehle zyada conversation history retain karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Har turn ek separate API call add karo dropped ho rahe messages ko summarize karne ke liye, is running summary ko conversation me prepend karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Sliding window ko ek hybrid approach se replace karo: older messages summarize karo jabki recent messages verbatim rakho", "c": true}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai sliding window ko ek hybrid approach se replace karna: older messages summarize karna jabki recent messages verbatim rakhna. Ye context ko zyada deliberately manage karta hai taaki model sabse important information available rakhe bina brittle long-history recall pe depend kiye. Baaki: A) Poora transcript dump karna noise add karta hai aur agle actor ke liye key facts jaldi dhoondhna mushkil banata hai. | B) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | C) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai."}, "c81": {"q": "Order tracking ke baare me ek conversation ke dauran, tumhara external system ek webhook receive karta hai jo indicate karta hai ki user ka package ship ho gaya hai. User actively chat kar raha hai aur likely jald hi ek follow-up message bhejega. Tum chahte ho ki assistant is status change ko naturally apne next response me incorporate kare.\n\nSabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Assistant ko configure karo ki woh har response ki shuruat me ek `get_order_status` tool call kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Status update ko agle user message me prefix ke roop me append karo API call karne se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Turant ek API request bhejo update ke saath ek synthetic user message ke roop me, ek unsolicited assistant response generate karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Current shipping status ko system prompt me add karo agle API call se pehle", "c": true}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai current shipping status ko system prompt me add karna agle API call se pehle. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai."}, "c82": {"q": "Users report karte hain ki responses turns ke across repetitive lagte hain — har message \"Certainly!\" ya \"I'd be happy to help!\" jaisi phrases se shuru hota hai chahe conversation deep ho jaaye. Tum chahte ho ki responses zyada natural feel hon, in repetitive openers ke bina.\n\nSabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Temperature parameter kam karo response openings ko zyada deterministic aur kam variable banane ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "System prompt instructions add karo phrases specify karte hue jo avoid karne hain, jaise \"Kabhi bhi 'Certainly' ya similar affirmations se responses shuru mat karo\"", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek partial assistant message append karo ek direct response opening ke saath jise model continue karega", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Post-processing implement karo response beginnings se common greeting phrases detect aur strip karne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai ek partial assistant message append karna ek direct response opening ke saath jise model continue karega. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: B) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c83": {"q": "Users frequently ambiguous requests bhejte hain jaise \"party ke liye ek venue book karo\" bina date, guest count, ya budget specify kiye. Tumhari evaluation dikhati hai ki assistant average 4.2 clarifying questions poochta hai koi action lene se pehle, jisse 35% users mid-conversation abandon kar dete hain. Lekin, jab tum questions kam karte ho, users kabhi-kabhi aisi recommendations receive karte hain jo unki preferences match nahi karti.\n\nIs trade-off ko improve karne ka sabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Assistant ko instruct karo ki conversation history ke basis pe explicit assumptions state kare, recommendations ke saath aage badhe corrections invite karte hue, aur clarifying questions ko sirf irreversible actions jaise bookings confirm karne ke liye reserve kare", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Assistant ko configure karo saari clarifying questions ko ek single compound question me consolidate karne ke liye (jaise \"kaunsi date, guest count, aur budget consider kar rahe ho?\") total conversational turns kam karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Assistant ko configure karo reasonable defaults ke saath aage badhne ke liye (medium-sized venue, next weekend, moderate budget) bina in assumptions ko explicitly state kiye, users ko corrections provide karne dete hue agar results expectations match na karein", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Ek structured intake form implement karo jo saare required parameters (date, guest count, budget, venue type) upfront collect kare assistant ke koi bhi recommendations dene se pehle", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai assistant ko instruct karna ki conversation history ke basis pe explicit assumptions state kare, recommendations ke saath aage badhe corrections invite karte hue, aur clarifying questions ko sirf irreversible actions jaise bookings confirm karne ke liye reserve kare. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: B) Sab kuch ek path me collapse karna precision kam karta hai aur usually system ko control karna zyada mushkil banata hai, aasan nahi."}, "c85": {"q": "System 85% se kam extraction confidence wale documents ko human review pe route karta hai. Ek quarterly audit reveal karti hai ki 12% high-confidence extractions (>85%) me bhi errors hain — cases jaha model plausible-but-incorrect values dhoondta hai. Error sources vary karte hain: competitor specs dikhane wali comparison tables, different product variants reference karne wale appendices, aur ambiguous phrasing jise model misinterpret karta hai. Tumhe in high-confidence errors ko catch karne aur measure karne ke liye ek sustainable strategy chahiye ki kya improvements time ke saath error rate kam karte hain.\n\nKaunsa approach sabse effective hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek verification pass add karo jo har high-confidence document se dobara extract kare, un cases ko flag karte hue jaha do extraction attempts different results produce karein", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Stratified random sampling implement karo weekly high-confidence extractions ka ek fixed percentage review karte hue, error rate measurement aur novel pattern detection enable karte hue", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Heuristic rules implement karo jo comparison tables ya appendices wale documents ko review ke liye flag karein confidence score se independent", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Confidence threshold ko 85% se 70% tak kam karo, extractions ka ek larger volume human review pe route karte hue", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai stratified random sampling implement karna weekly high-confidence extractions ka ek fixed percentage review karte hue, error rate measurement aur novel pattern detection enable karte hue. Ye agent ko failure ke baare me clearer signals deta hai taaki woh sahi recovery action choose kar sake, blindly retry karne ya bohot jaldi escalate karne ki bajaye. Baaki: A) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | C) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | D) Escalation yahan bohot jaldi hai kyunki scenario ek behtar system behavior maang raha hai, primary fix ke roop me handoff nahi."}, "c86": {"q": "Tumhara research assistant users ko academic papers analyze karne me madad karta hai extended conversations me. User testing ek recurring issue reveal karti hai: jab conversations 60K tokens exceed karti hain, users follow-up questions poochte hain jinhe pichle discuss kiye gaye papers se precise numerical details chahiye hoti hain — sample sizes, exact p-values, specific inclusion criteria. Tumhara current approach 8 turns ke baad paper discussions ko summarize karta hai context limits ke andar rehne ke liye. Users report karte hain ki in precision-dependent questions ke responses aksar hedged ya inaccurate hote hain.\n\nSabse effective architectural change kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Retrieval implement karo jo relevant paper sections ko re-inject kare jab user ka question suggest kare ki unhe specific numerical details chahiye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Har paper se extract kiye gaye key facts (sample sizes, statistics, methods) ka ek structured database maintain karo aur relevant entries ko context me retrieve karo jab precision-dependent questions detect hon", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Methodology aur results sections ke source text ko context me permanently rakho, jabki sirf conversational discussion aur interpretation portions summarize karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Ek separate Claude call use karo explicit instructions ke saath higher-fidelity summaries generate karne ke liye jo saare numerical details aur statistical values preserve karein", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai har paper se extract kiye gaye key facts (sample sizes, statistics, methods) ka ek structured database maintain karna aur relevant entries ko context me retrieve karna jab precision-dependent questions detect hon. Ye context ko zyada deliberately manage karta hai taaki model sabse important information available rakhe bina brittle long-history recall pe depend kiye. Baaki: A) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | C) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | D) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c87": {"q": "Ek security audit tumhari authentication library ko v2 se v3 tak update karne require karti hai. Migration guide breaking changes document karti hai: `authenticate()` ab ek Promise return karta hai callback accept karne ki jagah, User type me restructured fields hain, aur teen deprecated methods remove ho gaye hain. Grep dikhata hai ki library kai modules ke across 45 files me imported hai.\n\nSabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Migration transformations encapsulate karta hua ek custom slash command banao, phir use har file ke against execute karo bina prior codebase exploration ke", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Dependency version update karo, test suite chalao, aur Claude Code use karo har failure ko fix karne ke liye jaise woh appear hoti hai", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Plan mode me jao modules ke across library usage explore karne ke liye, affected code paths map karo, phir implement karne se pehle ek migration strategy banao", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Migration guide ke breaking changes ko apne prompt me paste karo aur direct execution use karo saare usages ko 45 files ke across update karne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai plan mode me jaana modules ke across library usage explore karne ke liye, affected code paths map karna, phir implement karne se pehle ek migration strategy banana. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: D) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c89": {"q": "Tum ek naya payment processing module implement kar rahe ho jise apne project ke established patterns follow karne chahiye database transactions, error handling, aur audit logging ke liye. Tumne teen existing modules identify kiye hain jo in patterns ko exemplify karte hain: `db_utils.py`, `error_handlers.py`, aur `audit_logger.py`. Ye ek one-off integration task hai — ye patterns tumhari team wiki me well-documented hain aur unhe additional project-level documentation ki zaroorat nahi.\n\nSabse effective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Teeno modules ke patterns ko apne prompt me natural language me describe karo, transaction handling approach, error format, aur logging conventions explain karte hue jo Claude ko follow karni chahiye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "`@references` use karo teeno modules ko directly apne prompt me include karne ke liye, Claude ko patterns ke concrete code examples dete hue jo follow karni hain", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Har pattern ki documentation apni CLAUDE.md file me add karo, unhe project conventions ke roop me establish karte hue jo Claude automatically apply karega", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Claude se apna codebase explore karne ko kaho transaction, error handling, aur logging patterns dhoondhne aur samajhne ke liye naya module generate karne se pehle", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai `@references` use karna teeno modules ko directly apne prompt me include karne ke liye, Claude ko patterns ke concrete code examples dete hue jo follow karni hain. Ye agent ko failure ke baare me clearer signals deta hai taaki woh sahi recovery action choose kar sake, blindly retry karne ya bohot jaldi escalate karne ki bajaye. Baaki: A) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | C) Documentation useful background de sakti hai, lekin ye code me har real caller ya usage path dhoondhne ka reliable tareeka nahi hai. | D) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga."}, "c92": {"q": "Anthropic ki tool use documentation kehti hai: \"Instructive error messages likho. Generic errors jaise 'failed' ki jagah, ye include karo ki kya galat hua aur Claude ko agla kya try karna chahiye.\" Ek billing dispute agent `lookup_order` use karta hai, jo saare exceptions catch karta hai aur ek `tool_result` return karta hai `is_error: true` ke saath aur message \"execution failed\". Monitoring do failure modes dikhati hai: agent identical call ko retry karta hai jab tak turn limit hit na ho, ya turant `escalate_to_human` call kar deta hai alternative tools try kiye bina.\n\nKaunsa change documented recommendation follow karta hai aur Claude ko har error type ke liye correct recovery action select karne ke liye zaroori information deta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Agentic loop me ek error classification step add karo jo tool errors ko Claude ke dekhne se pehle intercept kare, har ek ko \"retry\", \"try_alternative,\" ya \"escalate\" tag kare, aur us recommendation ko tool result me add kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "`is_error: true` remove karo aur error details ko normal tool content ke roop me return karo, taaki Claude response ko data ke roop me reason kare, ek flagged failure condition treat karne ki jagah jo retry behavior ko bias karti hai", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Error-type-specific messages return karo `is_error: true` ke saath, jaise, \"order not found — get_customer try karo phone se search karne ke liye\" data errors ke liye aur \"Database timeout (transient) — retry succeed hona chahiye\" infrastructure errors ke liye", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Har tool implementation ke andar exponential backoff ke saath retry logic implement karo taaki transient errors transparently tool ke andar hi resolve ho jaayein kisi bhi failure result Claude ko agentic loop me surface hone se pehle", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai error-type-specific messages return karna `is_error: true` ke saath, jaise, \"order not found — get_customer try karo phone se search karne ke liye\" data errors ke liye aur \"Database timeout (transient) — retry succeed hona chahiye\" infrastructure errors ke liye. Ye agent ko failure ke baare me clearer signals deta hai taaki woh sahi recovery action choose kar sake, blindly retry karne ya bohot jaldi escalate karne ki bajaye. Baaki: A) Ye galat hai kyunki retry khud se underlying cause resolve nahi karta jab tak failure clearly transient na ho. | B) Ye galat hai kyunki retry khud se underlying cause resolve nahi karta jab tak failure clearly transient na ho. | D) Ye galat hai kyunki retry khud se underlying cause resolve nahi karta jab tak failure clearly transient na ho."}, "c97": {"q": "Tumhara `searchFlights` tool ek external airline API call karta hai jo kabhi-kabhi ek 503 Service Unavailable error return karta hai.\n\nApni tool implementation me is error ko handle karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Error ko internally log karo aur ek empty response return karo, model ko flight data ke bina continue karne dete hue", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Tool result me ek error message return karo explain karte hue ki service temporarily unavailable hai", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek empty flight list return karo jaise search succeed hui ho lekin koi matching flights nahi mili", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Request ko automatically 5 baar tak exponential backoff ke saath retry karo results agent ko return karne se pehle", "c": true}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai request ko automatically 5 baar tak exponential backoff ke saath retry karna results agent ko return karne se pehle. Ye agent ko failure ke baare me clearer signals deta hai taaki woh sahi recovery action choose kar sake, blindly retry karne ya bohot jaldi escalate karne ki bajaye. Baaki: A) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | B) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | C) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga."}, "c98": {"q": "Tumhare agent ke paas ek `log_workout` tool hai jo `exercise_type` (string), `value` (number), aur `measurement` (string) accept karta hai. Production monitoring dikhati hai ki agent frequently mismatched combinations pass karta hai — cardio exercises jaise running ke liye `measurement: \"reps\"` use karna, ya strength exercises jaise bench press ke liye `measurement: \"miles\"` use karna. Tumhari exercises naturally do categories me divide hoti hain: cardio (time ya distance me measured) aur strength (reps aur sets me measured). 23% tool calls me invalid combinations hain.\n\nKaunsa approach in errors ko sabse effectively kam karega?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Server-side validation implement karo invalid combinations ke liye descriptive errors return karte hue, agent ko corrections ke saath retry karne dete hue", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Tool description me explicit examples add karo valid combinations dikhaate hue (jaise, \"Running ke liye: minutes ya miles use karo. Push-ups ke liye: reps use karo\") har exercise category ke liye constraints ke saath", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "`log_cardio_workout` (duration_minutes ya distance_miles parameters ke saath) aur `log_strength_workout` (reps aur sets parameters ke saath) me split karo", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "`measurement` pe enum constraints add karo values ko \"minutes\", \"miles\", \"reps\", ya \"sets\" tak limit karte hue arbitrary measurement strings rokne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai `log_cardio_workout` (duration_minutes ya distance_miles parameters ke saath) aur `log_strength_workout` (reps aur sets parameters ke saath) me split karna. Ye agent ko failure ke baare me clearer signals deta hai taaki woh sahi recovery action choose kar sake, blindly retry karne ya bohot jaldi escalate karne ki bajaye. Baaki: A) Ye galat hai kyunki retry khud se underlying cause resolve nahi karta jab tak failure clearly transient na ho. | B) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte. | D) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga."}, "c99": {"q": "Initial testing ke dauran, tum notice karte ho ki Claude conversation me pehle ke vocabulary words yaad nahi rakhta lagta. Jab ek student poochta hai \"Kya tum mujhe un words pe quiz kar sakte ho?\", woh aise respond karta hai jaise koi words discuss hi nahi hue.\n\nSabse likely explanation kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Tum har API request me prior messages include nahi kar rahe — stateless API conversation history retain nahi karta", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Tumhe conversation persistence enable karni hai ek session ID parameter har API call ke saath pass karke", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Tumhare system prompt me explicit instructions chahiye jo Claude ko batayein ki earlier turns se information yaad rakhe", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Model ka context window bhar gaya hai, jisse earlier conversation content drop ho rahi hai", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai ye samajhna ki tum har API request me prior messages include nahi kar rahe — stateless API conversation history retain nahi karta. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: C) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c100": {"q": "Ek naye user ka pehla message hai \"Mera focus music set up karo.\" Iska matlab ho sakta hai preferences configure karna, ek playlist banana, ya turant music play karna. Tumhara system teeno actions support karta hai.\n\nEffective approach kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Preference configuration shuru karo genres, tempos, aur artists ke baare me poochte hue jo woh focus ke liye prefer karte hain", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Curated tracks ke saath ek naya \"Focus\" playlist banao aur user ko notify karo ki woh ready hai", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Action type ke baare me ek clarifying question poocho: abhi play karein ya baad ke liye configure karein", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Turant popular focus tracks play karo aur user ko zaroorat pade toh redirect karne do", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai action type ke baare me ek clarifying question poochna: abhi play karein ya baad ke liye configure karein. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai."}, "c101": {"q": "Tumhara conversational assistant frequently multiple clarifying questions generate karta hai jab users ambiguous requests karte hain. Jab ek user poochta hai \"Kya tum report me meri madad kar sakte ho?\", assistant respond karta hai: \"Main help karke khush hounga! Kya tum mujhe bata sakte ho: 1) Kaunsi report? 2) Kis tarah ki help — drafting, reviewing, ya formatting? 3) Tumhari deadline kya hai?\" User analytics 40% conversation abandonment rate dikhati hain in multi-question responses ke baad.\n\nAmbiguity ko appropriately handle karte hue friction kam karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek preprocessing step add karo ek smaller model use karke request ambiguity ko 1-5 scale pe classify karne ke liye, high-ambiguity requests ko ek clarification dialog pe route karte hue aur low-ambiguity requests ko directly assistant ko", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "System prompt ko modify karo assistant ko instruct karne ke liye ki available context se reasonable assumptions banaye, un assumptions ko explicitly state kare, aur agar interpretation galat ho toh adjust karne ka offer de", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Common request patterns ka ek lookup table banao predefined default interpretations ke saath, assistant ko un defaults ke saath respond karwate hue bina made gaye assumptions state kiye", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Assistant ko ek clarifying question per turn tak limit karo, conversation history use karte hue answers accumulate karne ke liye multiple exchanges ke across, sab kuch upfront request karne ki jagah", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai system prompt ko modify karna assistant ko instruct karne ke liye ki available context se reasonable assumptions banaye, un assumptions ko explicitly state kare, aur agar interpretation galat ho toh adjust karne ka offer de. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: A) Model size badalna cost ya quality affect kar sakta hai, lekin ye is scenario me root cause ko directly address nahi karta."}, "c104": {"q": "Tum `/products` endpoint ko speed up karne ke liye ek caching layer implement kar rahe ho API responses ke liye. Tumhare paas ek rough idea hai — Redis ek 5-minute TTL ke saath — lekin tum production caching me naye ho aur sure nahi ho ki ek robust implementation ke liye aur kya considerations chahiye.\n\nApna iterative workflow shuru karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek minimal request se shuru karo: \"Redis caching `/products` me 5-minute TTL ke saath add karo.\" Features aur issues fix karo follow-up prompts ke through jaise testing ke dauran problems surface hon", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Apne known requirements ke saath ek specification likho aur uncertain areas ke liye \"TBD\" markers ke saath, Claude se har TBD ke liye solutions propose karwate hue jaise woh implement karta hai", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Plan mode use karo current `/products` endpoint implementation analyze karne ke liye, phir apni caching requirements provide karo ek baar Claude explain kar de ki existing code kaise structure hai", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Claude se implement karne se pehle caching requirements ke baare me tumhe interview karne ko kaho, considerations surface karte hue jaise invalidation strategies, cache layers, consistency guarantees, aur failure modes", "c": true}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai Claude se implement karne se pehle caching requirements ke baare me tumhe interview karne ko kehna, considerations surface karte hue jaise invalidation strategies, cache layers, consistency guarantees, aur failure modes. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: A) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c105": {"q": "Tumne Claude se ek data migration script likhne ko kaha hai, lekin initial output required fields me null values wale records ko correctly handle nahi karta.\n\nEk working solution ki taraf iterate karne ka sabse effective tareeka kya hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Generated code ko manually edit karo null handling fix karne ke liye, phir Claude ke saath doosre parts pe kaam continue karo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Null value problem ko detail me describe karo aur Claude se poore script ko improved edge case handling ke saath regenerate karne ko kaho", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek test case provide karo null values wale example input aur expected output ke saath, phir Claude se use fix karne ko kaho", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Apne prompt me \"edge cases ke baare me zyada sochो\" add karo aur migration logic ka ek complete rewrite request karo", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai ek test case provide karna null values wale example input aur expected output ke saath, phir Claude se use fix karne ko kehna. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: D) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c108": {"q": "Ek engineer production logs me ek unfamiliar error message dekhta hai \"SYNC_CONFLICT: entity version mismatch detected\" lekin nahi jaanta ki codebase ki 12 services me se kaunsi ise generate karti hai. Woh agent se source code locate karne me madad maangte hain.\n\nKaunsa exploration approach sabse efficiently responsible code dhoondega?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Glob use karo un directories me files dhoondhne ke liye jo commonly error handling se associated hain (jaise `errors/`, `exceptions/`, ya `handlers/`) services ke across, phir har matching file Read karo", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Grep use karo error message se distinctive text search karne ke liye (jaise \"SYNC_CONFLICT\" ya \"entity version mismatch\"), phir matching files ko Read karo context samajhne ke liye", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Project ka README aur service configuration files padho architecture samajhne ke liye, phir service directory me source files ko systematically Read karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Grep use karo saari files dhoondhne ke liye jo project ke error handling module se import karti hain, phir un files ko Read karo custom error definitions locate karne ke liye", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai Grep use karna error message se distinctive text search karne ke liye (jaise \"SYNC_CONFLICT\" ya \"entity version mismatch\"), phir matching files ko Read karna context samajhne ke liye. Ye agent ko failure ke baare me clearer signals deta hai taaki woh sahi recovery action choose kar sake, blindly retry karne ya bohot jaldi escalate karne ki bajaye. Baaki: A) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | C) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | D) Surface-level searching yahan bohot narrow hai kyunki task ko simple text matching se zyada rich structural understanding chahiye."}, "c109": {"q": "Ek engineer tumhare agent se poochta hai comprehensive tests add karne ko ek 200 files wali legacy codebase me minimal existing test coverage ke saath. Engineer ne specify nahi kiya ki kaunse modules prioritize karne hain.\n\nAgent ko is open-ended task ko kaise decompose karna chahiye?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Glob aur Grep use karo codebase structure map karne ke liye, heavily-coupled modules identify karo, high-impact areas ke liye ek prioritized plan banao, aur dependencies discover hone pe revise karo", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Directory structure ke basis pe upfront ek fixed testing schedule banao, har top-level directory ko equal effort allocate karte hue code complexity ya business importance ke bina", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Saari 200 files ko systematically padho ek complete function inventory banane ke liye koi bhi tests likhne se pehle, testing plan ko har function account karte hue ensure karte hue shuru karne se pehle", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Pehle module se alphabetically tests likhna shuru karo, test failures aur imports use karke related files ko organically discover karte hue", "c": false}], "e": "Anthropic ki agent best practices efficient context gathering ko search tools (Glob/Grep) ke saath favor karti hain, har file exhaustively padhne ki jagah, jo context aur time waste karega. High-impact, heavily-coupled modules prioritize karna aur plan ko iteratively revise karna jaise dependencies surface hoti hain, ek open-ended task decompose karne ka sahi tareeka hai; A wasteful hai, B impact/complexity ignore karta hai, aur C arbitrary aur unplanned hai."}, "c112": {"q": "Tumhara documents (query) tool results ko \"Found 3 documents: Q2 Budget Proposal, Q2 Budget Forecast, Annual Review\" ke roop me return karta hai. Tum chahte ho ki agent document (4, multi) aur doc (24, multi) kar sake.\n\nKaunsa return format in multi-step workflows ko sabse acche se enable karega?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Size aur authors samet zyada detailed human-readable descriptions", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "URLs jinpe users click karke document apne browser me khol sakein", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Structured data jisme har result ke liye document IDs aur metadata ho", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Search results se extract ki gayi document titles ka ek JSON array", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai structured data jisme har result ke liye document IDs aur metadata ho. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: A) Escalation yahan bohot jaldi hai kyunki scenario ek behtar system behavior maang raha hai, primary fix ke roop me handoff nahi. | D) Ye phir bhi fragile text-generation behavior pe rely karta hai, structure ko zyada reliable tarike se enforce karne ki bajaye."}, "c115": {"q": "Tumhara scheduling agent `get_available_slots(date, provider_id)` use karta hai open appointment times retrieve karne ke liye, phir `book_appointment(provider_id, slot_time, patient_id)` slot reserve karne ke liye. Tickets dikhate hain ki 15% booking attempts \"slot no longer available\" ke saath fail hote hain kyunki koi doosra user availability check aur booking call ke beech slot book kar leta hai.\n\nIn tools ko kaise refactor karna chahiye?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Dono tools rakho lekin agent ke system prompt me retry logic add karo, use instruct karte hue ki `get_available_slots` dobara call kare aur ek different time select kare agar booking fail ho", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Dono tools ko ek single `find_and_book_appointment` me combine karo jo atomically availability check kare aur book kare, ya toh confirmed booking ya available alternatives return karte hue", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek `hold_slot(provider_id, slot_time)` tool add karo jo ek 60 second temporary reservation banaye, agent ko availability check karne aur booking ke beech ise call karna require karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "`book_appointment` ko modify karo detailed failure information return karne ke liye jisme currently available alternative slots shamil hon jab requested slot unavailable ho, agent ko ek different time ke saath retry karne enable karte hue", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai dono tools ko ek single `find_and_book_appointment` me combine karna jo atomically availability check kare aur book kare, ya toh confirmed booking ya available alternatives return karte hue. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: A) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | D) Ye galat hai kyunki retry khud se underlying cause resolve nahi karta jab tak failure clearly transient na ho."}, "c116": {"q": "Production monitoring dikhati hai ki tumhara `search_catalog` tool 12% time fail hota hai: 8% network timeouts hain jo turant retry karne pe succeed ho jaate hain, jabki 4% query syntax errors hain malformed user-provided filters se jo kabhi succeed nahi hote chahe kitni bhi retry ki jaaye. Currently, dono error types agent ko identically return hote hain, jisse woh syntax errors retry karke turns waste karta hai aur timeouts ke liye users ko \"baad me try karo\" bolta hai.\n\nTool ki error handling ko kaise modify karna chahiye?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Apne system prompt me few-shot examples add karo jo dikhaye ki network errors ko syntax errors se kaise distinguish karein aur har case ko appropriately handle karein", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Saare errors ko ek `retryable` boolean flag aur error type details ke saath return karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Saare errors pe uniformly exponential backoff retry logic apply karo, max retries exhaust hone ke baad ek generic \"service temporarily unavailable\" message return karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Tool ke andar network timeouts ke liye automatic retry backoff ke saath implement karo; syntax errors ko turant parameter validation details ke saath return karo", "c": true}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai tool ke andar network timeouts ke liye automatic retry backoff ke saath implement karna; syntax errors ko turant parameter validation details ke saath return karna. Ye agent ko failure ke baare me clearer signals deta hai taaki woh sahi recovery action choose kar sake, blindly retry karne ya bohot jaldi escalate karne ki bajaye. Baaki: A) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte. | B) Retry sirf tab madad karta hai jab problem transient ho; ye khud se ek design ya classification problem fix nahi karta. | C) Retry sirf tab madad karta hai jab problem transient ho; ye khud se ek design ya classification problem fix nahi karta."}, "c122": {"q": "Ek dinner party plan karne me madad karte hue 40-minute session ke baad, conversation 78,000 tokens tak badh gayi hai. History me shamil hai: (1) user ka mention karna ki ek guest ko severe shellfish allergy hai, (2) 8 servings ke liye recipes scale karne ke measurements, (3) user ki clarification ki \"room temperature butter\" unki kitchen me 68°F ka matlab hai, aur (4) meal timing aur presentation ke baare me general back-and-forth. Tumhe window limit reach hone se pehle context management implement karna hai.\n\nKaunsa approach information preservation aur token reduction ka sabse acha balance karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Poori conversation ko externally store karo aur semantic search use karo har turn ke liye relevant portions retrieve karne ke liye, sirf matching segments ko context me load karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek sliding window implement karo jo sirf sabse recent 20,000 tokens retain kare, users pe rely karte hue important information dobara state karne ke liye jab relevant ho", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Poori conversation history ko ek concise summary me summarize karo main discussed topics capture karte hue, phir aage naye messages append karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Critical structured data (allergies, serving counts, user-defined terms) ko ek compact reference section me extract karo, general discussion summarize karo, aur recent exchanges verbatim retain karo", "c": true}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai critical structured data (allergies, serving counts, user-defined terms) ko ek compact reference section me extract karna, general discussion summarize karna, aur recent exchanges verbatim retain karna. Ye context ko zyada deliberately manage karta hai taaki model sabse important information available rakhe bina brittle long-history recall pe depend kiye. Baaki: A) Poora transcript dump karna noise add karta hai aur agle actor ke liye key facts jaldi dhoondhna mushkil banata hai. | B) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | C) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai."}, "c124": {"q": "Tumhara `searchProducts` tool ek external catalog API query karta hai jo paginated results return karta hai (50 items per request). Production logs dikhate hain ki queries frequently 200+ products match karti hain, aur ye design jo saari pages auto-fetch karta hai 15-20 second delays cause karta hai.\n\nPagination handling ko kaise redesign karna chahiye?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Pagination ke liye separate `searchProducts` aur `fetchMoreResults` tools banao", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek `maxPages` parameter add karo (default: 2) jo control kare ki internally kitni pages fetch hoti hain", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Server-side relevance ranking implement karo aur sirf top 50 sabse relevant items return karo", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "First page return karo total match count aur additional pages ke liye ek cursor ke saath", "c": true}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai first page return karna total match count aur additional pages ke liye ek cursor ke saath. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai."}, "c127": {"q": "\"Tum ek critical project pe Lead Data Scientist/Engineer ho. Technical details ya data me kuch poori tarah sahi nahi hai, aur ye expected outputs ko negatively impact karta hai. Unhe evaluation data ke liye dono approaches independently develop karne hain...\n\nTum is scenario ko kaise manage karoge?\"", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Analysis session ko `fork_session` enabled ke saath resume karo, har testing strategy ke liye ek separate branch banate hue", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Original session me continue karo, pehle end-to-end tests develop karke, phir snapshot tests sequentially", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Analysis session ki key findings ko ek file me export karo, phir do naye sessions banao jo is file ko reference karein", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Do fresh sessions shuru karo, har ek ko relevant source files dobara padhne dete hue shuru karne se pehle", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai analysis session ko `fork_session` enabled ke saath resume karna, har testing strategy ke liye ek separate branch banate hue. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: B) Dono paths ko sequentially handle karna branches ko separate rakhne ka point miss kar deta hai aur comparison ya independent exploration ko harder banata hai. | D) Fresh shuru karna useful context waste kar deta hai jo scenario preserve karna chahta hai, isliye underlying problem solve kiye bina cost add karta hai."}, "c133": {"q": "Tumhare CRM agent ka `delete_contact` tool requests handle karta hai jaise \"Acme Corp ke liye duplicate entry delete karo.\" Database me similarly named records hain (jaise, \"Acme Corp,\" \"Acme Corporation,\" \"ACME Corp Inc.\"), aur analytics dikhati hain ki 8% deletions 24 hours ke andar reverse hoti hain misidentified records ki wajah se. Users ne bhi complain kiya hai ki current multi-step confirmation flow routine cleanup tasks me bohot zyada friction add karta hai.\n\nKaunsa approach error rate ko sabse effectively kam karta hai workflow efficiency maintain karte hue?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek 30-day recovery window ke saath soft-delete implement karo taaki users deletion workflow ko slow kiye bina mistakes undo kar sakein", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Users se require karo ki woh CRM interface se exact record ID supply karein natural language references to contact names use karne ki jagah", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Automated duplicate detection deploy karo jo probable duplicates identify aur merge kare, manual deletion requests ki zaroorat remove karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Matched records ko differentiating fields ke saath present karo aur intended target ka single-click confirmation require karo deletion execute karne se pehle", "c": true}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai matched records ko differentiating fields ke saath present karna aur intended target ka single-click confirmation require karna deletion execute karne se pehle. Ye agent ko failure ke baare me clearer signals deta hai taaki woh sahi recovery action choose kar sake, blindly retry karne ya bohot jaldi escalate karne ki bajaye. Baaki: A) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | B) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | C) Choice ko auto pe chhodna phir bhi critical decision ko usi jagah rakhta hai jo already fail ho rahi hai."}, "c136": {"q": "Evaluation dikhati hai 94% extraction accuracy short meeting transcripts (<30 minutes) pe lekin sirf 68% longer transcripts (>60 minutes) pe jaha discussions meander karti hain aur key information poore transcript me scattered hoti hai. Dono lengths ke transcripts model ke context window ke andar fit hote hain.\n\nKaunsa pattern complex, lambe documents pe accuracy ko sabse effectively improve karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek pre-extraction step add karo jaha model structured extraction perform karne se pehle key discussions aur conclusions summarize kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Few-shot examples add karo jo scattered information wali lambi meetings se correct extraction demonstrate karein", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Lambe transcripts ko chunks me split karo, har chunk se separately extract karo, phir results merge aur deduplicate karo", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Extraction task ke liye ek zyada capable model tier pe upgrade karo", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai lambe transcripts ko chunks me split karna, har chunk se separately extract karna, phir results merge aur deduplicate karna. Ye context ko zyada deliberately manage karta hai taaki model sabse important information available rakhe bina brittle long-history recall pe depend kiye. Baaki: A) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | B) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte. | D) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai."}, "c139": {"q": "Agent ke MCP tools ko delivery-specific capabilities ke saath expand karne ke baad (`check_delivery_status`, `contact_driver`, `issue_credit`, `apply_promo_code`, `update_delivery_address`, `reschedule_delivery`), total tool count 4 se 10 tak badh gaya hai. Tumhari evaluation suite dikhati hai ki tool selection accuracy girke 71% ho gayi hai. Log analysis reveal karti hai ki zyaadatar errors semantically overlapping tools ke beech agent ke choose karne me hote hain — `issue_credit` call karna jab `process_refund` correct hai, aur `check_delivery_status` call karna jab `lookup_order` already needed data return karta hai.\n\nKaunsa approach error source ke roop me logged semantic overlaps ko structurally eliminate karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Semantically overlapping tools ko consolidate karo — `issue_credit` aur `process_refund` ko ek single `resolve_compensation` tool me merge karo ek optional `include_tracking` flag ke saath", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Chhe naye tools pe `defer_loading` ke saath tool search tool enable karo, original char tools ko hamesha loaded rakhte hue, taaki agent use dynamically call kare jab zaroorat pade", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Tools ko do sub-agents me split karo — ek \"financial resolution\" agent `process_refund`, `issue_credit`, aur `apply_promo_code` ke saath, aur ek \"delivery\" agent baaki delivery tools ke saath — ek coordinator unke beech routing karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "System prompt me few-shot examples add karo jo har ambiguous tool pair ke liye correct selection demonstrate karein, jaise dikhaana ki `issue_credit` ya `process_refund` kab appropriate hai", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai semantically overlapping tools ko consolidate karna — `issue_credit` aur `process_refund` ko ek single `resolve_compensation` tool me merge karna ek optional `include_tracking` flag ke saath. Ye tool-selection mistakes kam karta hai decision surface ko clearer aur agent ke task ke saath zyada aligned banake. Baaki: B) Ye us ambiguity ko kam nahi karta jo agent ko galat tool choose karne ki wajah bani. | C) Ye us ambiguity ko kam nahi karta jo agent ko galat tool choose karne ki wajah bani. | D) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte."}, "c141": {"q": "Tumhare order management system ko teen distinct operations ke liye tools chahiye: refunds issue karna (amount aur reason chahiye), orders cancel karna (reason chahiye), aur reschedule karna (shipping address chahiye). Har operation ek `order_id` parameter share karta hai lekin different additional requirements rakhta hai. Testing ke dauran tum notice karte ho ki current design frequently required parameters omit kar deta hai ya irrelevant unhe include kar leta hai.\n\nKaunsa design change parameter accuracy ko sabse effectively improve karega?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Teen separate tools me split karo (har ek sirf un parameters define kare jo us specific operation ke liye required hain)", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Ek unified tool rakho ek nested operation object parameter ke saath jiski internal structure operation type ke hisaab se vary kare, tool description me documented", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek unified tool rakho lekin JSON Schema if-then-else conditionals add karo enforce karne ke liye ki parameters jaise amount sirf tab required hon jab operation type \"refund\" ho", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Ek unified tool rakho saare parameters optional mark ke saath, lekin system prompt me few-shot examples add karo jo har operation ke liye correct parameter combinations dikhaye", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai teen separate tools me split karna (har ek sirf un parameters define kare jo us specific operation ke liye required hain). Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: C) Ye phir bhi fragile text-generation behavior pe rely karta hai, structure ko zyada reliable tarike se enforce karne ki bajaye. | D) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte."}, "c143": {"q": "Tum ek security scanning workflow bana rahe ho.\n\nJab engineers ko ek dangerous function jaise `eval()` ke saare occurrences ek badi codebase ke across dhoondhne hain, tumhara agent content search ke liye kaunsa tool use kare?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Grep use karo pattern \"eval(\" ko codebase ki saari files ke across search karne ke liye", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Glob use karo ek pattern ke saath jaise `/*eval*` files dhoondhne ke liye, phir har matching file Read karo", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Project ki main entry file padho aur import statements follow karo trace karne ke liye ki `eval` kaha use ho sakta hai", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Bash use karo `ls -R | grep eval` chalane ke liye recursively un files list karne ke liye jinme eval hai", "c": false}], "e": "Grep purpose-built content-search tool hai (ripgrep-based) file contents ke andar patterns dhoondhne ke liye ek badi codebase ke across, jo exactly wahi hai jo saare `eval(` call sites locate karne ke liye chahiye. Glob sirf file names match karta hai, entry files padhna aur imports trace karna scale nahi karta ya coverage guarantee nahi karta, aur `ls -R | grep` sirf file names match karta hai, file contents nahi. Baaki: D) Surface-level searching yahan bohot narrow hai kyunki task ko simple text matching se zyada rich structural understanding chahiye."}, "c145": {"q": "Tumhara expense reimbursement agent employee requests ko ek `process_reimbursement` tool use karke process karta hai. Company policy require karti hai ki $500 se zyada wale reimbursements ko funds disburse hone se pehle approve kiya jaana chahiye.\n\nAgent roz sainkado requests handle karta hai, aur tumhe threshold enforcement ko tamper-proof chahiye chahe agent ko kaise bhi prompt kiya jaaye. Kaunsa approach ensure karta hai ki $500 approval threshold bypass na ho sake?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "`process_reimbursement` tool `amount` aur `details` accept karta hai, aur internally threshold enforce karta hai; $500 se kam amounts auto-disburse hote hain aur tool ek success confirmation return karta hai. $500 se zyada amounts tool ko ek pending approval request create karwate hain aur ek status return karte hain jo indicate kare ki manager review pending hai", "c": true}, {"l": "B", "t": "Do tools provide karo: `auto_reimburse` (hard-coded $500 limit ke saath) aur `manager_approval`. Detailed system prompt instructions include karo agent ko amount check karne aur appropriate tool use karne ko bolte hue. Ek PostToolUse hook add karo jo auditing ke liye log kare kaunsa tool call hua", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Threshold check ko ek PreToolUse hook me implement karo jo `amount` parameter inspect kare `process_reimbursement` execute hone se pehle. Agar amount $500 se zyada ho, hook context ko modify kare ek `requires_approval: true` flag add karne ke liye, jise tool disburse karne se pehle check kare", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "`process_reimbursement` tool ek `approved_by_manager` parameter accept karta hai. System prompt agent ko instruct karta hai ki ise sirf tab `true` set kare jab confirm ho jaaye ki ek manager ne request approve ki hai. Ek nightly audit script un saare reimbursements review karta hai jaha `approved_by_manager` `true` set tha", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai `process_reimbursement` tool ka `amount` aur `details` accept karna, aur internally threshold enforce karna; $500 se kam amounts auto-disburse hote hain aur tool ek success confirmation return karta hai. $500 se zyada amounts tool ko ek pending approval request create karwate hain aur ek status return karte hain jo indicate kare ki manager review pending hai. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: B) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | D) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c147": {"q": "Performance analysis reveal karti hai ki tumhara context saari pichli queries ke accumulated RAG results se bana hai, jo conversation history ko crowd out kar raha hai aur 15+ turns ke baad coherence degradation cause kar raha hai.\n\nKaunsa approach is issue ko sabse acche se address karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Semantic deduplication implement karo accumulated RAG results aur conversation turns ke across redundant information identify aur remove karne ke liye", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Context budget ko shift karo RAG results ko favor karne ke liye conversation history allocation kam karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Last 2-3 queries ke RAG results ke liye ek sliding window implement karo conversation history preserve karte hue", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Saare RAG results ko ek consolidated summary document me compress karo jo har retrieval ke baad incrementally update ho", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai last 2-3 queries ke RAG results ke liye ek sliding window implement karna conversation history preserve karte hue. Ye context ko zyada deliberately manage karta hai taaki model sabse important information available rakhe bina brittle long-history recall pe depend kiye. Baaki: A) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | B) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | D) Sab kuch ek path me collapse karna precision kam karta hai aur usually system ko control karna zyada mushkil banata hai, aasan nahi."}, "c150": {"q": "Production logs dikhate hain ki jab agent complex billing disputes handle karta hai jinhe 6+ tool calls chahiye, kabhi-kabhi woh apna `max_turns` limit exhaust kar deta hai data gather karne ke baad aur resolution complete karne ya escalate karne se pehle. Team ka goal hai ye guarantee karna ki har customer interaction ya toh ek completed resolution ke saath khatam ho ya ek human escalation ke saath, chahe agent loop kaise bhi terminate ho.\n\nKaunsa approach ye guarantee achieve karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "System prompt instructions add karo jo agent ko batayein ki `escalate_to_human` call kare apni findings ke ek summary ke saath jab bhi woh determine kare ki dispute resolve nahi kar sakta", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Orchestration-layer code add karo jo har loop termination ke baad agent ka outcome check kare — agar loop bina completed resolution ya escalation ke khatam hua, programmatically `escalate_to_human` call kare accumulated conversation context aur tool results ke saath", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Ek pre-tool-use hook implement karo jo tool invocations count kare aur loop ko automatic escalation ke saath terminate kare jab agent apni remaining actions ka 80% reach kare", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Workflow ko do sequential agent invocations me split karo — pehla agent `get_customer` aur `lookup_order` ke through information gather kare, phir doosra agent us data ka use kare aur `process_refund` ya `escalate_to_human` handle kare, har ek apne separate turn budgets ke saath", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai orchestration-layer code add karna jo har loop termination ke baad agent ka outcome check kare — agar loop bina completed resolution ya escalation ke khatam hua, programmatically `escalate_to_human` call kare accumulated conversation context aur tool results ke saath. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai. Baaki: A) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye. | C) Ye phir bhi critical decision ko model discretion pe chhod deta hai, jo exactly wahi hai jo scenario keh raha hai fail ho raha hai. | D) Escalation yahan bohot jaldi hai kyunki scenario ek behtar system behavior maang raha hai, primary fix ke roop me handoff nahi."}, "c153": {"q": "Ek engineer do requests submit karta hai: • Request A: \"`getUserData` function ko har jagah jaha use hota hai `fetchUserProfile` me rename karo.\" • Request B: \"Poore data processing module me error handling improve karo — try/catch blocks add karo, meaningful error messages, aur ensure karo ki failures silently data corrupt na karein.\"\n\nKis request ke liye ek explicit multi-phase workflow specify karna (jaise analyze → propose → implement with review) outcome quality ko sabse zyada improve karta hai?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Request A, function rename task", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Dono requests equally benefit karti hain", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Request B, error handling task", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "Koi bhi request significantly benefit nahi karti", "c": false}], "e": "Request B open-ended aur judgment-heavy hai — \"error handling improve karo\" ko current behavior analyze karna, ye decide karna ki try/catch kaha belong karta hai, aur meaningful messages choose karna chahiye, isliye ek explicit analyze → propose → implement-with-review workflow quality ko materially badhata hai aur code changes se pehle bad design pakadta hai. Request A ek mechanical, well-defined rename hai jise ek simple find-and-replace-style execution theek se handle kar leta hai, isliye multi-phase structure zyada add nahi karta. Baaki: A) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | B) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga. | D) Ye failure ko bohot ambiguous chhod deta hai, agent ke paas sahi recovery action choose karne ka koi basis nahi hoga."}, "c156": {"q": "Tumhari conversation history do types ke content include karti hai: persistent story elements (character backgrounds, plot structure, world rules) jinhe poore time consistent rehna zaroori hai, aur extensive brainstorming discussion jo zyaadatar ephemeral hai. 40+ turns ke baad, tum context limits hit kar rahe ho aur users report karte hain ki assistant established character traits \"bhool jaata hai,\" narrative consistency break karte hue.\n\nKaunsa approach persistent story elements ko model ke liye available rakhne ka sabse acha tareeka hai jabki context space wapas reclaim ho?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Ek sliding-window approach apply karo sirf sabse recent 25 turns rakhte hue, model pe rely karte hue ki woh recent discussion flow se earlier context infer kare", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Persistent story elements ko ek retained \"story bible\" section me context start pe separate karo, trimming ya summarization sirf brainstorming discussion pe apply karte hue", "c": true}, {"l": "C", "t": "Saari history ko ek vector database me store karo aur har naye message ke liye semantically similar passages retrieve karo, conversation history ko retrieved chunks se replace karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "Poori conversation history ko har 20 turns pe ek condensed synopsis me summarize karo, tokens free karne ke liye full history replace karte hue", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai persistent story elements ko ek retained \"story bible\" section me context start pe separate karna, trimming ya summarization sirf brainstorming discussion pe apply karte hue. Ye context ko zyada deliberately manage karta hai taaki model sabse important information available rakhe bina brittle long-history recall pe depend kiye. Baaki: A) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | C) Ye infrastructure ya indirection add karta hai, lekin sawaal actually ek simpler coordination pattern choose karne ke baare me hai jo current workflow fit kare. | D) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai."}, "c157": {"q": "Users frequently apni search criteria mid-conversation refine karte hain. Tum ek pattern notice karte ho: jab users kehte hain \"Actually, budget ko $650K tak badha do\" ya \"Mujhe ab ek house ki jagah condo prefer karunga,\" assistant kabhi-kabhi baad ke responses me original preferences reference karna continue karta hai — chahe updates conversation history me clearly present hon. Context usage sirf 35% capacity pe hai.\n\nKaunsa solution sabse reliably ensure karta hai ki model current preferences use kare?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Few-shot examples include karo jo dikhaye ki assistant correctly preference changes ko acknowledge aur apply karta hai responses me", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "Conversation pruning implement karo outdated preferences wale turns remove karne ke liye, ensure karte hue ki sirf current wale context me rahein", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "Current preferences ke saath ek structured state object maintain karo, changes hone pe use update karo, aur use har request me include karo", "c": true}, {"l": "D", "t": "System prompt instructions add karo emphasize karte hue ki model ko hamesha sabse recently stated preferences ko earlier wali se prioritize karna chahiye", "c": false}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai current preferences ke saath ek structured state object maintain karna, changes hone pe use update karna, aur use har request me include karna. Ye context ko zyada deliberately manage karta hai taaki model sabse important information available rakhe bina brittle long-history recall pe depend kiye. Baaki: A) Examples margin pe behavior improve kar sakte hain, lekin is failure ke peeche ke deeper control ya architecture issue ko address nahi karte. | B) Ye sahi information ko sahi form me preserve nahi karta, isliye real context-management problem solve karne me fail hota hai. | D) Sirf prompt wording yahan kaafi nahi hai, kyunki scenario ko instructions se zyada strong structural mechanism chahiye."}, "c161": {"q": "Tumhara music discovery assistant ko consistently ek enthusiastic tone maintain karna chahiye, har recommendation ke liye apna reasoning explain karna chahiye, aur user preferences behtar samajhne ke liye clarifying questions poochni chahiye. Tum chahte ho ki ye behavior saari user interactions me reliably persist kare.\n\nIn behavioral guidelines ko kaha define karna chahiye?", "o": [{"l": "A", "t": "Environmental variables me jo tumhari application API client ko pass karti hai", "c": false}, {"l": "B", "t": "First assistant message me, Claude ko in guidelines ko aage follow karne ka instruct karte hue", "c": false}, {"l": "C", "t": "API ko bhejne se pehle har user message me prepended", "c": false}, {"l": "D", "t": "System prompt me", "c": true}], "e": "Sabse acha approach hai system prompt me. Ye directly scenario me describe kiya gaya failure ya constraint address karta hai aur weaker, zyada ambiguous alternatives se zyada reliable hai."}};
